Phnom Penh Capital Administration Holds a Dissemination and Consultation Forum in Chroy Changvar District to Hear Some Suggestions and Concerns of Citizens
(Phnom Penh): In the dissemination and consultation forum of Phnom Penh Capital Council, Khan Chroy Changvar, on the morning of October 6, 2022, people raised the issue of rising garbage prices, requesting clean water network, requesting to solve the problem of opening the road. Public and urging authorities to eliminate gambling and drugs.
The forum was held at OCIC Market in the presence of Mr. Mop Sarin, Chairman of the Phnom Penh Municipal Council and Mr. Khleang Huot, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, representing Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh.
In this public forum, people raised many concerns, including raising the price of garbage from 4,000 Riels to 10,000 Riels, requesting a clean water network in Bak Kheng village, Sangkat Prek Leap, asking for a solution to open public roads and raising Urges the authorities to eradicate gambling and drugs and to help solve the problem of flooding caused by floods in some areas in Chroy Changva district.
The people said that the action of the Phnom Penh Municipal Administrative Unity Command on cracking down on gambling and illegal pawnshops was fully applauded by the people and urged to continue to crack down more successfully.
Mr. Khleang Huot, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, said that the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has not ignored the issue of flooding, but has continuously addressed the people, including immediate action and planning to relieve the flooding.
He stated that "In order to participate in the comments and raise questions and requests of the people in the forum and consultation of the Phnom Penh Capital Council, there are 13 oral questions and requests equal to 16 issues and questions and requests. Blessings in the mailbox 16 issues.
He added that all the comments and suggestions of the people really bring great potential and made the Phnom Penh Capital Administration reflect its inactive points in the past to improve and Improve local development and find solutions for the people to be transparent and effective as a representative of public administration.
