Ukraine and its allies have called Russia's referendum on the Donetsk, Luhanskerson and Zaporizia regions illegal. The draft resolution of the UN General Assembly, organized by the West, aims to condemn Russia's "illegal referendum" and "attempted illegal occupation" of the region.
Russia has not completely taken control of the four areas it claims to include, and Ukrainian forces have recaptured much of the territory since early September. During Russia's annexation of Crimea in 2014, the General Assembly adopted a formal decision that a referendum would not be valid if there were 100 votes in favor, 11 against and 58 abstentions.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol instructed officials to continue to fill all the chicken coops on the streets so that it will not be difficult for people to travel
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, instructed the technical working group to continue its work on closing the chicken coop during the rainy season. This, without leaving that road, makes it difficult for people to travel.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol made this recommendation on October 5, 2022 at the Ministry's office on the occasion of chairing the weekly meeting on October 1, 2022, with the participation of ministry leaders and government officials from units under the ministry.
The meeting discussed with a focus on work including:
1: Some challenges that arose during the trial operation of the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway and solutions to prevent illegal activities in order to promote the use of the expressway can run smoothly and efficiently.
2: Improving the collection of tolls from the use of expressways and the sharing of operational data, ensuring business transparency, company and traffic safety to the people through DIP technology mechanism, which is a modern technology to reduce time and provide convenience. To expressway users.
3: Progress of the project to build an international tourist port in Kampot province, which is part of promoting transportation and logistics in Cambodia to be better.
4: Progress of the construction of wastewater treatment plant in Sihanoukville, which is an important project to reduce pollution due to wastewater and improve the beauty of Sihanoukville.
5: Problems of the condition of National Road No. 3 (Kampot-Veal Renh), especially the 20-kilometer-long road that is badly damaged to find a solution for improvement through special techniques (deep soil excavation) 18 meters out).
6. Impact of road infrastructure due to floods in the capitals and provinces in 2022 due to floods and flash floods and emergency measures for emergency rehabilitation.
7: Progress of work to improve National Road 4, which is being repaired in accordance with standards and technical specifications.
After the meeting, the two sides exchanged views in a spirit of high regard for the work that is being prepared and successfully implemented according to the planned plan. Senior Minister Chanthol also provided good comments and recommendations. To assist in the implementation of all projects to be more efficient and high quality work as well.
In addition, the Senior Minister also thanked the leaders, civil servants and members of all working groups who worked hard to fulfill their skills with care and a high sense of responsibility and instructed and Encourage all civil servants to work harder and more consciously to bring benefits and progress to the motherland.
Speaking at the opening ceremony of the conference "Vision of Cambodia 2022" to discuss the recovery of Cambodia after the Kovid 19 crisis this morning, October 6, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded about the financial support to the people affected by Kovid 19 and the poor. Samdech also reminded of the efforts of the Royal Government to seek free vaccines for citizens.
