Samdech Techo Hun Sen has just finished a long trip abroad to complete his work, including:
On September 21, 2022, Samdech Techo traveled to New York, USA to deliver a speech at the United Nations on September 23, 2022 * Visit to Havana, Cuba on September 24-25 September 2022 * Travel to Tokyo, Japan to attend the funeral of former Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe.
This recommendation was made on the occasion that Samdech presided over the opening of the conference "Vision of Cambodia 2022" in Phnom Penh on October 6, 2022.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said: As an additional input for the discussion in today's conference, I would like to share the thoughts and direction of the Royal Government as follows:
First, in addition to vaccination, the Royal Government will encourage investment in the health sector to develop a strong health system that can help and protect people from Kovid 19, as well as other pandemics that may occur in the future. The future.
Second, the development of the social protection system is an investment in the people and the provision of economic security to the people, especially the poor and vulnerable families. In this spirit, the Royal Government will continue to strengthen the social assistance and social security system and expand its coverage more specifically, by encouraging and encouraging people in the informal economy to enter the system for protection. Other.
Third, the development of human resources, both knowledge and skills, is an indispensable factor in improving economic productivity and shifting the economic structure from a low-skilled labor-intensive economy to a skilled-skilled economy. And technology.
Fourth, although the Cambodian economy relies heavily on foreign direct investment and exports, small and medium enterprises are the backbone of the economy, contributing significantly to the creation of jobs and jobs for the Cambodian people. In this regard, the Royal Government has made the development of small and medium enterprises a top priority by providing technical and financial support, improving the business environment and encouraging systemic economic participation.
Sixth, promoting green economic development and climate resilience is also an essential part of supporting sustainable socio-economic development by supporting the expansion of cooperation on green infrastructure construction, promoting transition. Energy and the use of green technology.
In this regard, the successful implementation of the major goals of the Public Financial Management Reform Program will make a significant contribution to Cambodia's future socio-economic development.
