LONDON: Vladimir Putin's nuclear threat and the defeat of the Russian army in Ukraine in recent weeks have been a test of the "strategic alliance" between Putin and Chinese President Xi Jinping. Ping. That is, how strong will the alliance that Putin and Xi Jinping claim is "borderless friendship" if Putin really decides to use nuclear weapons?
On the other hand, if Putin does use nuclear weapons against Ukraine, the United States and Europe, China's major trading partners, will have an excuse to put pressure on China, which could push other non-nuclear-armed countries in the region. Asia, which has poor relations with China, such as Japan, South Korea or Taiwan, will assume that only with its own nuclear weapons can they ensure their own safety.
In early 2022, Putin joined the leaders of China, France, Britain and the United States, declaring that if "nuclear war" erupted, no one would win and such a war should not have happened. Also. Most analysts agree that Putin may use nuclear weapons only if Russia or Putin himself feels threatened.
