Tbong Khmum Governor Inspects Mekong River Flood Situation and Impact of Nearly 2,000 Hectares of Rice Crops
(Tbong Khmum): The Mekong River has risen continuously, causing some houses and agricultural crops of people in three districts of Tbong Khmum province to be inundated.
On the morning of October 5, 2022, Dr. Cheam Chansophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, and Ms. Meng Van Danin, accompanied by the Deputy Governor, led the provincial working group and district authorities to inspect the flood situation and flooding of the Mekong River. Affect the rice crop of the people in Krouch Chhmar district, Tbong Khmum province.
On that occasion, Dr. Cheam Chansophoan expressed his deep regret for the damage to the rice crop of the farmers and some infrastructure that made it difficult for people to travel in three districts: Kroch Chhmar district. Tbong Khmum and Orang Ov district.
The provincial governor also instructed all residents to take care of their health and be very careful of young children who are afraid of drowning in various ways that could cause loss of life, and advised local authorities to invite people. Residents who have lost their homes to temporary shelters will have to wait until the water recedes to return to their homes, and security forces will be deployed to ensure their safety.
Please be informed that as of October 5, the water level of the Mekong River in Tbong Khmum Province was only 13.81 meters high for 2022. This is the second year that the end-season floods have caused the flooding of rice fields in the Mekong Delta.
