(Preah Vihear): Some low-lying areas in Preah Vihear province continue to be affected by floods, rains and runoff from Thailand, causing flooding of villages and crops and making life difficult for people.
On the morning of October 5, 2022, Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear Province and Chairman of the Secretariat of the National Committee for Disaster Management, and Mr. Kim Virak, Secretary General of the National Committee for Disaster Management, together with relevant officials in the province, inspected the situation. The flood will bring donations from the Royal Government to the people who are affected by the floods.
During the inspection of the flood situation, both Mr. Kim Rithy and Mr. Kim Virak expressed their condolences to all the affected people for the effects of the floods. Mr. Kim Rithy highlighted the attention of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross.
He informed the affected people that Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit have always advised to take care of the affected people and arrange for the disaster management officer and the Red Cross to prepare food for the people to solve the problem. Difficult during this flood.
During the inspection of the flood situation and distribution of gifts in the backyard, Mr. Kim Rithy as well as Mr. Kim Virak advised people to be very careful about safety, especially to take care of young children not to play in the water that can endanger life.
Please note that the people who received donations now are 29 families in Chamkar Sramov village (Obak point), Pal Hal commune, Preah Vihear city, Preah Vihear province. Of these, 23 families received donations at the shelter and 6 families were brought directly to the flooded houses.
