He said that the implementation of agreements such as the RCEP agreement, the ASEAN trade agreement, the free trade agreement between Cambodia and China, as well as the free trade agreement between Cambodia and Korea, has made the import of goods from the country. As a Partner to the Agreement for a Certificate of Origin (CO), Cambodia must favor tariff rates to what is negotiated.
He added that in this case, Cambodia will suffer from the loss of customs duties, but from another perspective related to the trade or export of Cambodian goods that used to go out to pay taxes will be. Preferential with duty or at a lower tax rate, which boosts exports.
He added that although Cambodia may now be less profitable than its agreement partners, he believed that Cambodia would be able to attract more investors in agriculture, industry and other sectors to produce goods for export. International under the Free Trade and Export Agreement, with preferential tariffs from the EBA or GSP.
