Woman Arrested After Fraudulently Requesting Password to Use SATHAPANA Bank Customer Account
According to the information from the authorities, after receiving the notification from the customer about the loss of money in the account, Sathapana Bank immediately started the investigation procedure with the competent authorities and led to the arrest of the suspect and Continuing to find other conspirators.
According to authorities, the suspect was arrested on October 5, 2022. The suspect fraudulently asked for an OTP password and took control of a SATHAPANA Bank customer account on September 9.
With the arrest of the suspects, SATHAPANA Bank would like to thank and commend for the attention paid by the competent authorities to seek justice for the Bank's customers.
SATHAPANA Bank has once again reminded its customers that there are now a number of scams in the form of impersonation of family members, bank employees or rewards, requiring customers to provide personal information or provide an OTP. Sent to customer's phone number. This can cause customers to lose money from their account unknowingly, so be careful and avoid sharing any confidential information.
Please note that in case of any suspicion, SATHAPANA Bank customers can inquire at SATHAPANA Bank branches near you (currently 170+ nationwide) or through the 24/7 customer service phone number. (023/081) 999 010. Minister of Information Supports and Donates $ 2,000 to the Organizing Committee of the 9th Cambodia Book Fair from 9 to 11 December 2022 at the National Library
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of October 5, 2022, Mr. Hok Sothy, Director of Sipar, led the 9th Cambodia Book Fair Organizing Committee to report on the organization of the Cambodia Book Fair, which will take place from 9th to 11th December 2022 at the National Library in Daun Penh, Phnom Penh, and ask for recommendations and cooperation from Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information.
Mr. Hok Sothy informed that Cambodia Book Fair is a socio-cultural event organized annually at the National Library by the Cambodia Book Fair Commission in collaboration with the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, Ministry of Information, Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, Cambodian Library Association, Book Publishers Association. In Cambodia, many other partner organizations and institutions.
Due to the Kovid-19 crisis, the exhibition was suspended in 2020 and 2021. But this year, as the situation in Kovid-19 has eased a lot, the committee has decided to reschedule the book fair, which is planned to have 140 book booths, and hopes to have as many participants as in 2019 for three days. The exhibition has about 180,000 participants.
The theme for the 9th Cambodia Book Fair is "One Day to Read, One Day to Know" in order to promote writing and writing, as well as to promote the book industry, so that publishers can have the opportunity to do business selling books. Also.
Minister Khieu Kanharith has expressed his support for the resumption of the 9th Cambodia Book Fair after a two-year absence from the 19-year outbreak of Kovid.
According to the plan to organize the 9th Cambodia Book Fair, Mr. Khieu Kanharith has contributed $ 2,000 to the event and also plans to bring some books of the Ministry of Information to the exhibition. 70% of mine clearance work in Tbong Khmum province under Samdech Techo project for mine action
(Tbong Khmum): On October 5, 2022, Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Deputy Chairman of the Mine Authority, inspected the demining activities under the Samdech Techo project for mine action "Provide safe land, create a smile" and meet with forces. Demining of the National Center for the Management of Peacekeeping Forces, Demining and Remnants of War (NPMEC) and residents in Choam Kravien commune, Memot district, Tbong Khmum province.
The Senior Minister confirmed that the demining work under the Samdech Techo project for mine activities in Tbong Khmum province "Provide safe land, create a smile" achieved about 70% of the plan to clear a total area of 4,687,317 square meters, equivalent to 90 minefields. Detected and destroyed 76 anti-personnel mines, 15 anti-tank mines and 1,080 unexploded ordnance.
He added that today's demining and demining work is the result of the efforts and attention of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister in solving the problem of landmines and explosive remnants of war. Remaining after the war, these resources came from inspiring the National Movement for Mine Action in 2025 by Samdech Techo.
On that occasion, the Senior Minister conveyed the greetings and greetings from Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Samdech Kittiprittbandit to the demining force, border police force and all the people who participated in this program.
The inspection and discussion were accompanied by Mr. Kun Rathmony, Deputy Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, Representative of Dr. Cheam Chansophoan, Leader of the Mine Authority, Mr. Sem Ratana, Deputy Director General of NPMEC, Representatives of Departments around the province and local authorities at all levels.
