(Phnom Penh): Cambodia, which used to import cars exclusively from abroad, but under the leadership of the current head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, has made many investors decide to invest in the car industry in Cambodia, which makes the sector more prosperous. The use of new cars in Cambodia has increased significantly, which is a good sign for the car market in Cambodia.
Speaking at a press conference on the results of tax collection on existing tax-free vehicles in the country on October 5, 2022, Dr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise. The new car market in Cambodia has shown strong growth in recent years, boosting imports of new cars and locally assembled components for a significant increase in sales.
He said that the trend of using new cars is increasing, while the price of new cars is also affordable due to the establishment of local car assembly plants, and new cars imported from Thailand are taxed at zero.
Dr. Kun Nhim encouraged and encouraged Cambodians to use new cars, reduce the use of used cars, because old cars can cause a lot of costs such as high fuel consumption and high repair costs.
