(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, confirmed that the General Department of Customs will propose to the management to delay the implementation of the law on tax collection on duty-free right-hand drive vehicles. Registered in the existing country, while on October 8, 2022 will expire.
Mr. Kun Nhim confirmed that "we plan to propose to the management to review and decide on the delay and how long I will meet with the management and ask for opinions."
Mr. Kun Nhim said that the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia has discussed the option or request to the management to request an extension to the owners of the remaining 3,000 right-hand drive vehicles may seek funding to pay taxes. Applicable only for registered vehicles.
The General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia hopes that the management will provide concessions to give right-hand drive owners time to raise funds to pay taxes. At present, there are 3,838 registered vehicles that have not yet come to fulfill their tax obligations.
Mr. Kun Nhem emphasized that if there is no solution to the delay, for the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, there is no choice but to implement, which means that right-hand drive vehicles are prohibited goods, can not pay taxes or fines. Because it is illegal.
Mr. Kun Nhim also said that the tax is not expensive because the right-hand drive vehicles that have been registered have already received a lot of concessions in favor of not having to change the steering wheel, which costs one unit. Adjustments between $ 2,500 and $ 5,000.
According to Kun Nhim, both the first and second campaigns of the General Department of Customs and Excise collected about $ 100 million, while the total number of vehicles that were taxed and registered was about 18,000. Accessories.
It should also be noted that the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to collect tax on existing duty-free cars in the country of refuge under various license plates from September 2021 and ending on June 30, 2022.
From September to December 31, 2021, left-hand drive tax-free vehicles can pay tax with a 10% tax preference. Right-hand drive vehicles also receive a 10 percent tax concession. The right-to-left steering wheel must be completed by June 30, 2022.
Owners of duty-free right-hand drive vehicles are required to register as existing vehicles in the country by July 31, 2022. After registration, the General Department of Customs and Excise has until October 08, 2022 to complete. Tax and duty obligations. But this time may be further delayed.
Nearly 10,000 existing duty-free right-hand drive vehicles in Cambodia have been registered, of which 5,976 are right-hand-drive duty-free vehicles in Cambodia that have paid $ 19.7 million in tax and excise duties. .
The Embassy of Indonesia and the Indonesian Association in Cambodia jointly donate blood to the National Blood Transfusion Center to celebrate the 77th anniversary of the founding of the Indonesian National Army
(Phnom Penh): The Office of the Deputy Attorney General of the Embassy of the Republic of Indonesia in Cambodia, together with the Indonesian National Association, voluntarily donated blood to the National Blood Transfusion Center on the occasion of the 77th anniversary of the founding of the Indonesian National Army. (October 5, 1945 - October 5, 2022).
The ceremony was held on October 5, 2022, led by Colonel Moch Rizal, Indonesian Military Attaché to Cambodia, with the participation of Indonesian Embassy officials and some Indonesians living in Cambodia.
"The blood donation is not only for any Indonesian festival, but if a hospital in Cambodia needs blood to help the victims, please provide immediate information," he said. "Holding the embassy, the embassy will call on the people of Indonesia as well as embassy officials to donate blood, so this blood donation is not just a national holiday."
In response, Mr. Sok Po, President of the National Blood Transfusion Center, thanked the Indonesian Ambassador to Cambodia, as well as the Military Attaché, as well as Embassy officials and the people of Indonesia for donating blood to the National Blood Transfusion Center. .
The President of the National Blood Transfusion Center also expressed hope that Cambodia-Indonesia relations will continue to strengthen their long-standing friendship.
Please be informed that, in addition to donating blood, the Office of the Deputy Attorney General of the Embassy of the Republic of Indonesia in Cambodia also organized friendly sports competitions with military units under the Ministry of National Defense, including: Commander-in-Chief, Army Jing, Water Jing, Air Jing and Command Bodyguards, Special Forces Command, 70th Brigade, Immigration Police Force and some other military units.
