Mr. Kong Vibol led the delegation to attend the ASEAN CEO Meeting to focus on digital technology, strengthen special tax management and towards a carbon-free social environment
The meeting focused on two main agendas: 1. Management system and monitoring of special taxable goods and second. Towards a carbon-free social environment.
Mr. Kong Vibol presented and shared Cambodia's experience related to Cambodia's tax measures introduced in the management of tax collection, especially the use of digital technology, as well as the challenges and measures. Continue to increase management, tax collection and / or promotion policies, as well as carbon offsets.
* International implementation of monitoring management system for special taxable goods
Speaking at the ASEAN CEO Meeting, Kong Vibol said that a good source of national income to promote sustainable economic growth would not be possible without proper tax policies or internal taxes, laws and regulations. There is an update and a strong fiscal administration.
He added that the General Department of Taxation, which is the staff of the Ministry of Economy and Finance of the Royal Government of Cambodia, has paid great attention to the management of internal tax collection, reform and further institutional development. Social and environmental issues.
He added that advances in technology have accelerated the pace of economic change in recent years, and the fiscal administration must catch up and keep up with the changes.
Efforts to modernize taxes are at the heart of our revenue collection strategy (RMS), and the use of technology to fulfill core and support functions for tax revenue management began in 2014.
As a result, success is reflected in improved tax collection management and tax revenue growth, as well as playing a key role in combating illicit trafficking.
Due to the challenges of illegal business between some countries, in order to solve this problem, the governments of the countries concerned need to seek dialogue and cooperation to find solutions, measures or means.
The General Department of Taxation requested the cooperation of the Thai side on the sharing and exchange of data through technology in order to combat illegal trade and prevent the loss of tax revenue for both countries.
As for the challenges we are facing, cases like Cambodia, which has a long border with neighboring countries (Long Border), thus increasing the chances of illegal smuggling to evade taxes such as special taxes and value added taxes. He hopes that the Thai government, as well as the governments of other ASEAN countries, will work together to address this issue.
Mr. Kong Vibol is confident that ASEAN will continue to move forward in solidarity and resilient cooperation to overcome all challenges and build a more inclusive ASEAN community. The General Department of Taxation of Cambodia is pleased to provide future cooperation with the aim of promoting and strengthening the effective management of tax collection and the fight against tax evasion.
Earlier this week, the British Foreign Office summoned the Chargé d'Affaires, Iran's top diplomat in Britain, to question the crackdown on protesters that erupted after the death of Mahsa Amini during her detention. . The British ambassador to Tehran was recalled on Tuesday.
"The British side has issued a unilateral statement indicating that it does play a role in the scenario of the ongoing unrest against Iran," noted the Western European policy chief of the Iranian Foreign Ministry. London is interfering in Iran's internal affairs based on its false and provocative interpretations. "Tehran will consider possible options in response to any unusual actions by the United Kingdom."
Amini, a 22-year-old Kurdish Iranian woman, was arrested on Sept. 13 by moral police in Tehran for dressing inappropriately. She was later reported dead while in custody on September 16.
