Separately, alms given to 5 other Sangkat administrations, including: Sangkat Toul Tum Poung I, Sangkat Toul Tum Poung II, Sangkat Boeung Trabek, Sangkat Phsar Doeum Thkov and Sangkat Tumnup Teuk of Khan Boeung Keng Kang. Case, 5 cases of orange juice, 150 cans of milk, 150 bags of tea, 150 kg of sugar, 5 cases of pure water and a budget of 2,000,000 Riels. Commentary: If the sponsorship of the Bassac Theater is the same as the sponsorship of this classical art concert, it will grow again
(Phnom Penh): Bassac is a traditional Khmer art that was very popular in the past, but now it seems to be declining. The decline was seen as lower support for the Bassac Theater compared to the sponsorship of the concert. However, the Royal Government of Cambodia, with the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts as its staff, has been working hard to preserve this beautiful ancient art.
In fact, on the morning of October 3 and 4, 2022, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts launched the opening ceremony of the 2022 National Bassac Theater Festival under the theme "Culture of Peace" under the chairmanship of Dr. Phoeung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts.
The program aims to preserve and promote the art of bassac, a priceless national cultural heritage, at the Department of Performing Arts Theater, with the presence of many bassac artists from the capitals and provinces. Who applied to compete in their ability to direct the story, the art, the way of writing and the ability to perform.
Mr. Nhet Tim said, "If the sponsorship of the Bassac Theater is the same as the sponsorship of the Bassac Concert, there will be a resurgence." "When we do not have the support and interest of philanthropists, we lose the resources (successors) who want to preserve this ancient art."
"Traditional art is less popular with the audience as well as philanthropists, with less interest in our traditional art," he said. Thus, the next generation of artists do not want to create new students.
Mr. Nhe Tim added that when there is a lack of support, there is not only a lack of human resources, but also a lack of costs to form a theater group. In fact, today, bassac theater needs modernization, such as lighting techniques, speakers and other stage equipment, all of which require cost.
The bassac is both spoken and sung and accompanied by bassac music. The play is influenced by Chinese and Vietnamese operas.
"In China, the Beijing Opera cannot be visited without buying tickets a year ago," she said. A ticket is not cheap, at least $ 500. The Beijing Opera is considered a World Heritage Site. Guess only China does not have a smartphone? They look at the same smartphone. Why do people still want to buy tickets, still want to see the Beijing Opera at least once? This is because of fame. ”
He said, "(There is a supply) that gives the theater person the strength to train the younger generation, the younger generation, he also works hard, seeing that first of all, what he does is valuable in society, contributes to the maintenance of the field. The second national culture provided a livelihood. If he knows and he can not earn money, he will give up that sector.
Chheang Chhada Pheak, Acting Director of the Department of Performing Arts, said that 10 groups of bassacs had applied and 5 groups had been selected for the finals. The 10 groups of bassac artists who applied to participate in the competition are: Phnom Penh 1 group, Kandal 3 groups, Kampong Speu 1 group, Kampong Chhnang 1 group, Kampong Cham 1 group, Banteay Meanchey 1 group, Tbong Khmum Province 1 group. 1 group and Kep province.
Prizes for 5 teams include:
Kep Bassac Raksmey Cultural Theater troupe expressed their happiness for the victory. The troupe thanked the Governor of Kep Province and the Director of the Department of Culture and Fine Arts of Kep Province for making the group a success.
Despite finding the winner, the jury still sees some shortcomings that need to be addressed, such as writing, directing (short, concentrated, not long), martial arts and costumes. In the future, the main committee will request the Ministry of Culture to have a workshop and training course on the bassac form to learn, understand and strengthen the capacity of bassac artists.
He added that in helping to think, help and share responsibility, young people who are the successors of bamboo and successors also have roles and responsibilities to learn, understand, love, respect, train, protect and promote the cultural heritage of Khmer ancestors.
People who follow the Bassac Theater Festival nationwide on the Ministry of Culture's Facebook page also expressed their appreciation and enthusiasm for the event. They also requested more rural bassac performances and sponsored a bassac troupe.
(Siem Reap): Mr. Tin Ponlok, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, said that ASEAN has been developing a strategy for socio-economic development after the outbreak of Kovid 19 to be resistant to external threats such as epidemics, climate change and geographical issues. Politics, including the environment and natural resource management, play an important role in regional economic development.
Mr. Tin Ponlok made this statement on the occasion of his visit to represent the Minister of Environment Say Sam Al on the occasion of presiding over the official opening of the 33rd ASEAN Environmental Ministers' Meeting and related meetings. Invitation from the leaders of ministries and institutions of 10 ASEAN countries, together with representatives of the ASEAN Secretariat and many national and international guests on the morning of October 5, 2022 in Siem Reap.
At the same time, Mr. Tin Ponlok stated that the governments of ASEAN member countries have been focusing on environmental work, green economy development, smart cities, sustainable infrastructure, etc. At the same time, ASEAN leaders have been rehabilitating all-round economies, focusing on sustainable production and consumption, along with the circular economy.
It should be noted that on behalf of the ASEAN Chair, which has set a strategy under the theme "ASEAN Solves Common Challenges", Cambodia is strengthening regional cooperation with all stakeholders to address regional and global environmental issues.
Seven strategies have been put in place for environmental work: environmental education, environmental management, coastal cities, sustainable management of chemicals and water resources, climate change, and conservation of natural resources and biodiversity.
