(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia on October 5, 2022, confirmed that the period of 9 months of 2022, from January to The General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia cracked down on about 510 duty-free vehicles nationwide.
This statement was made on the occasion of Dr. Kun Nhem's participation in the press conference to present the results of the tax collection work on existing tax-free vehicles in the country, which is the last permission of the Royal Government for right-hand drive vehicles. All types of taxes and duties without the need to change the steering wheel this morning, October 5, 2022.
"In the first nine months of 2022, we cracked down on about 510 vehicles, including 482 left-hand drive vehicles and 28 right-hand drive vehicles," said Dr. Kun Nhim.
At the same time, Dr. Kun Nhem said that the right-hand drive car that is in the campaign or the stage of permission to enter the registration, the officials of the General Department of Customs issued a paper for the owner of the car to register in the car to stay When the customs officer complied, he showed the document that it was registered.
Dr. Kun Nhem said that if the officials of the General Department of Customs stopped the car for compliance and it did not have the paper and no tax, the car is a car offense, the General Department of Customs and Excise to crack down on legal procedures. Effective.
In addition, Dr. Kun Nhim claimed that the crackdown was continuing, which was like a torrential downpour that could not be relaxed, especially right-hand drive vehicles, which have a long border with Thailand and many corridors. If left unmanaged, they can be left astray and lose the right path.
Dr. Kun Nhim stated that along the border, the General Department of Customs and the Cambodian Customs have deployed additional forces, and the General Department of Customs also has a network to provide information to prevent the import of right-hand drive vehicles into Cambodia. .
According to the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, 28 right-hand drive vehicles were seized in the first nine months of the crackdown. Come pay taxes later.
He emphasized that the revenue collection for the national budget in both the first and second campaigns of the General Department of Customs and Excise collected about $ 100 million, while the total number of vehicles that were taxed and registered was about 18,000 units. Public Administration Regulation Promotes Participation in the Public Administration Sector in Cambodia
