Within the framework of the signing of this memorandum, Strategically partnered with IFA, a financial and accounting professional education and training institution, with the aim of broadening and deepening public awareness for financial and accounting vocational training institutions in the field of public administration operations. Legal standards related to the benefits of the public administration sector.
This cooperation will also provide opportunities for students to increase their knowledge and gain direct work experience with the regulatory authority, as well as to give priority opportunities to the officers of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport. Aiming to increase capacity and additional knowledge, especially related to finance.
Dr. Kun Nhim's statement made at the press conference shows the results of the tax collection work on existing tax-free vehicles in the country on October 5, 2022.
He pointed out that goods that are subject to tax evasion, such as refrigerators, air conditioners, televisions, telephones, as well as cosmetic products, which the state must pay attention to in the implementation of the suppression and prevention of tax evasion to prevent Loss of customs revenue and prevention of inequality in doing business in Cambodia.
He also said that in order to prevent tax evasion of mobile phone products, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications has been working on this, which in the future, imported phones have to pay the correct tax to be able to connect the system with mobile operators. Unpaid tax will not be able to connect with SIM card.
The start of strengthening and cracking down on tax evasion on these products is aimed at strengthening customs revenue collection for the national budget, while customs revenue may be reduced as Cambodia implements free trade agreements.
