Deputy General Commissioner of the National Police instructs private security agencies to increase their attention, cooperate with law enforcement forces and report immediately when they see a crime or suspect a crime
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, instructed and reminded all private security agencies to pay more attention to cooperate with the competent forces and local authorities and to report immediately when any crime or Suspect any illegal activity occurs both in the target area and other targets.
On the occasion of the closing ceremony of the 42nd Private Security Agency Training Course on the evening of October 4, 2022, Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi confirmed that the National Police General Commission, which has the Private Security Management Department as its staff, has been taking care of Ensure that all private security agencies have the capacity, professional knowledge, ethics to promote this sector to grow continuously.
The Deputy Commissioner of the National Police stated, "When you see or suspect any illegal activity, whether in your standing position or not, immediately report to the competent authorities or to the department directly. "Phone numbers to work together to prevent and crack down on crime in a timely manner."
In addition, Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi also introduced and instructed some important work, including:
* First: Request private security agents to have the appropriate attitude to participate in the work, adhering to what is right after training, respect the qualifications as a private security agent: must be disciplined, ethical, use security uniforms Private and adequate facilities.
* Second, private security agencies not only work for companies or institutions, but also play an important role in maintaining security, safety, public order, especially the protection of property and lives of citizens.
* Third: To establish cooperation with the authorities and local authorities: good citizens and good people, an important support force to the competent authorities, good cooperation, timely response.
* Fourth: Jointly participate in the implementation of the policy of the Royal Government, especially the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats.
* Fifth: Directors of private security companies and institutions (continue to support the training) by sending private security agents to attend the course.
* Sixth: All participants must apply the knowledge gained from this study and continue to expand their knowledge, intelligence, creativity and high responsibility in fulfilling their roles.
He stated that the training is aimed at meeting the needs of capacity building to become a qualified and qualified private security agent for participation in the maintenance and protection of stability, security, safety, order and age. People's lives as well as improve the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats.
