(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khuon Sona, President of the Council of Judges of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, this morning, October 4, 2022, opened the trial of the case in which the Anti-Corruption Unit (ACU) arrested two defendants. Pol Chetra, a 33-year-old man, and Pol Rany, a 49-year-old woman, are sisters.
The younger brother was arrested by the Anti-Corruption Unit on charges of "initiating bribery" in accordance with the provisions of Article 28, Article 605 of the Penal Code and Article 32 of the Anti-Corruption Law. Pol Rany, 49, was arrested by the ACU on charges of "bribery" under Articles 28, 29, 30 of the Penal Code, Article 605 and Article 32 of the Anti-Corruption Law.
In front of the courtroom, which was represented by Vong Savath, two of the defendants' lawyers, the woman also claimed that she had handed over the $ 100,000 to a drug police officer named Chea Chamrong and left it in the room. There are 4 to 5 people. The money was $ 96,000 and 16 million riel in exchange for the release of her brother.
Defendant Pol Chetra testified before the court that he had already been sentenced to five years in prison for drug trafficking and was arrested again in connection with the same drug, and that he owed $ 100,000 to call the police. Calling her to get it is to get rid of it, when she comes back, she will pay her back later.
After a full morning of hearings, the presiding judge presented the bribery case to the verdict on October 11, 2022.
Please be reminded that six suspects were remanded in custody by the Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on May 2, 2022 in connection with drug trafficking and illegal possession of firearms for four different purposes. One of the suspects, Pol Chetra, was found guilty of bribery by the ACU.
