Samdech Techo Hun Sen asks Cuba to consider boosting cooperation with Cambodia in the field of health as the country produces 19 Kovid vaccine (Video inside) (Phnom Penh) Operates with Cambodia in the health sector as the country produces 19 Kovid vaccines.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's request was made during a bilateral meeting with Mr. Marro Cruz at the Peace Palace on the evening of October 4, 2022, while the Prime Minister of Cuba paid an official visit to Cambodia.
Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's personal assistant, confirmed to the media that during the meeting, the Prime Minister of Cuba thanked Cambodia for its warm hospitality during his visit.
He said the Prime Minister had briefed on the general situation in Cuba, including the management of 19 Kovid diseases and the Cuban economy, and expressed his willingness to strengthen and expand relations and cooperation between the two countries. On the basis of existing relations, promote the implementation of all signed memorandums, including education, health, culture and other fields.
He agreed with the Prime Minister of Cuba and praised Cuba's efforts and success in producing vaccines.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth stated that "Samdech Techo asked Cuba to consider promoting cooperation with Cambodia, especially in the field of health and other areas, including sports, investment and information."
He also thanked the Cuban government and people for their past assistance to Cambodia, especially at the time when Cambodia had just been liberated from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, where Cuba had provided health and other support to Cambodia.
The signing ceremony took place at the Peace Palace after the bilateral talks between Samdech Techo and Manuel Marero Cruz, including:
1: Cooperation and Cultural Exchange Program between the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts of Cambodia and the Ministry of Culture of the Republic of Cuba for 2022 to 2027
2: Agreement on Cooperation in the Field of Physical Education, Culture and Sports between the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the National Institute of Physical Education and Entertainment of the Republic of Cuba
The two documents were signed during a visit by Cambodian Prime Minister Manuel Marquez Cruz to Cambodia at the invitation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
During Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit to Cuba on September 24, 2022, the two countries also signed three documents, including:
1: Memorandum of Understanding on Health Cooperation between the Ministry of Health of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Ministry of Public Health of the Republic of Cuba.
2: Cooperation plan between the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Cuba for 2022-2025.
3. Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation between the National Institute of Diplomacy and International Relations of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the RAÚL ROA GARCÍA Institute of International Relations of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Cuba.
