(Phnom Penh): The Anti-Drug Department cracked down on drug trafficking, arrested two suspects and confiscated nearly 2 kilograms of drugs.
The crackdown was carried out on the orders of Brigadier General Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General, and Brigadier General Mak Chito, Deputy Commissioner General of the Anti-Drug Crime Plan, under the direct command of Lt. Gen. Lek Vannak, Director of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes.
This operation took place on September 29, 2022 at 13:10 Special Forces (A5) of the Anti-Drug Department led by Lt. Gen. San Sothy, Brigadier General Meas Hort, Lt. Gen. Chhouk Kea Director Deputy Department and Lieutenant Colonel Simaroth, Deputy Director of Office K5.
In addition, with the participation of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police and coordinated by Mr. Ou Sopheak, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, investigated and cracked down on drug trafficking at two different targets:
Target 1: Along the road R6 (Boeung Kak) in Srah Chak commune, Daun Penh district, Phnom Penh, arrested one suspect and about 100 grams of drugs.
Target 2: At the point along Street 261 in Sangkat Toek Laak 3, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh, arrested one suspect and a large package of drugs.
