Cambodia will host the first edition of the 32nd Southeast Asian Games or the 12th ASEAN Para Games on May 5, 2023. Cambodia has started a 300-day countdown to the SEA Games on July 8, 2022.
On the occasion of presiding over the opening of the 41st General Assembly of the Olympic Council of Asia (OCA) held at the Sokha Hotel on the morning of October 4, 2022, Samdech Techo proposed: "I call To the member countries of the Olympic Council of Asia, please provide support in all forms as possible for the organization of the 2023 SEA Games and ASEAN Para Games in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia stated that the organization of sports-related events at the international level also inspires and encourages the general public to love and support sports more and also to promote the sports reputation of each member country. Becoming more famous as well as the international marketing of the participating countries on the international stage.
In addition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also requested the Olympic Council of Asia to increase the diversification of sports activities in member countries to promote sports in Asia and increase the integration of sports to the economy, especially tourism. The sport is considered a kind of green tourism to strengthen friendship and solidarity, which contributes to building sustainable peace in the region.
It should be informed that the Southeast Asian Games with 11 countries participating is held every two years. So far, the event of the Southeast Asian Games, or SEA Games, has been going on for 64 years. Due to the political crisis and war as well as the limited economic situation, Cambodia has never hosted this tournament.
The hosting of the 2023 Southeast Asian Games is another historic event for Cambodia. Cambodia can not host this tournament if Cambodia lacks sports infrastructure and lacks financial resources.
