Speech by Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the Opening Ceremony of the 41st General Assembly of the Olympic Council of Asia
The following is the full text of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech at the opening ceremony of the 41st General Assembly of the Olympic Council of Asia:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the Olympic Council of Asia for its trust and support in hosting the 41st General Assembly of the Olympic Council of Asia in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that sports play an important role in diplomacy and international relations. The organization and participation in the Games reflects the strengthening of friendship, solidarity, relations and close cooperation between the States and the people of all participating countries.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that sports is also an opportunity to provide change in many areas, both the technique of organization and experience in sports, which is the cultural heritage, tradition and traditional martial arts of each nation.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the organization of sports-related events at the international level also inspires and encourages the general public to love and support sports more and also to enhance the sports reputation of each member country. Famous as well as the international marketing of the participating countries on the international stage.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this peace and success creates favorable conditions for Cambodia to host major international events as well as family reunions for the 45-nation Olympic Council.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen Encourages Discussions and Shares Good Practices in the General Assembly of the Olympic Council of Asia Concerning the Organization of Major Sports Events, Management and Technical Development of Sports to Improve Sports In Asia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen Asks the Olympic Council of Asia to increase the diversification of sports activities in member countries to promote sports in Asia and increase the linkage of sports to the economy, especially sports tourism. Considered a kind of green tourism to strengthen friendship and solidarity, which contributes to building sustainable peace in the region.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that Asia should examine why the sport of our continent is still weak, especially football, which even the semi-finals are difficult to reach.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urges the strengthening of sports ethics by mentioning the stampede incident in Indonesia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on the member countries of the Olympic Council of Asia to provide support in all forms as possible for the organization of the 2023 SEA Games and ASEAN Para Games in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
