According to the Polish diplomat, the settlement will officially close the painful pages of the past and help boost bilateral ties. In September, Poland's lower house of parliament voted in favor of the $ 1.2 trillion claim from Berlin.
In connection with a claim from Warsaw, the German government argued that Poland had waived its right to claim damages under a 1953 agreement with East Germany, and that the issue had been settled. All under the 1990 Treaty of German Unification, signed by West and East Germany, as well as by the United States, the Soviet Union, Britain, and France.
However, Poland insisted that the 1953 waiver was signed under pressure from Moscow and that it was barred from participating in the 1990 treaty negotiations. On September 1, 1939, Nazi Germany leader Odof Hitler launched an invasion of Poland, and two days later France and Britain declared war on Germany, marking the beginning of World War II.
The Prime Minister of Cuba Manuel Marquez has arrived in Cambodia for a three-day official visit. (Photo inside) (Phnom Penh) This afternoon, October 4, 2022, to pay a three-day official visit to strengthen and expand bilateral relations and cooperation.
During his visit to Cambodia, Manuel Marro Cruz will pay homage to His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, at the Royal Palace. The Prime Minister will also pay a courtesy call on Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, and Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly.
A statement from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs stated that the Prime Minister of Cuba will hold bilateral talks with Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the two Prime Ministers will preside over the signing ceremony of a number of documents that will further enhance bilateral cooperation. In sports, education and culture, as well as other fields.
During the official visit, Manuel Marro Cruz will also lay a wreath at the Independence Monument and at the shrine of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, the "King of Cambodia", the former King of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The Foreign Ministry noted that the visit of Manuel Marro Cruz will reaffirm the long-term and friendly relations between Cambodia and Cuba, as well as highlight the need to further strengthen and expand cooperation for the benefit of Better for both countries and peoples.
Cambodia and Cuba are committed to further deepening long-term relations and cooperation between the two countries as three memoranda of understanding were signed during Samdech Techo's recent visit to Cuba.
