Samdech Techo Hun Sen Recommends 4 Points to Contribute to the Promotion of Sports and Good Preparation for the Upcoming Major Sports Events (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia 4 points to contribute to the promotion of sports and good preparation in the upcoming major sporting events to be highly successful.
In 2023, Cambodia is supported to chair the SEA Games and the ASEAN Para Games and will host this major international sporting event in the Kingdom of Cambodia. The organization of this sport is possible due to the factors of peace and success in the fight against Kovid 19.
Speaking at the opening ceremony of the 41st General Assembly of the Asian Olympic Council in Phnom Penh on October 4, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said:
In order to contribute to the promotion of sports and to be well prepared to organize a large sporting event to be highly successful, I would like to encourage the following key points:
First: Today, with the active participation of member countries with many years of experience in the field of sports, I would like to encourage discussions and share good practices in this General Assembly related to the organization of sports events. Major management and development of sports techniques to make sports better in Asia.
Second, the Olympic Council of Asia calls for more diversification of sports activities in member countries to promote sports in Asia and increase the linkage of sports to the economy, especially sports tourism. A kind of green tourism to strengthen friendship and solidarity, which contributes to building sustainable peace in the region.
Fourth, I would like to call on the member countries of the Olympic Council of Asia to provide support in all forms as possible for the organization of the 2023 SEA Games and ASEAN Para Games in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Samdech wished the General Assembly of the Olympic Council of Asia today a fruitful and successful result.
