This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen opens the 41st General Assembly of the Olympic Council of Asia
(Phnom Penh): On Tuesday morning, October 4, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the opening ceremony of the 41st General Assembly of the Olympic Council of Asia (OCA) held at Sokha Hotel.
The 41st General Assembly of the Olympic Council of Asia was originally scheduled to be held in China, but due to the postponement of the 2022 Asian Games in China being postponed to 2023, the Olympic Council of Asia authorized Cambodia to host the event. .
Vath Chamroeun, Secretary General of the National Organizing Committee of the 32nd SEA Games (CAMSOC), said that hosting the Asian Olympic Council General Assembly is a rare opportunity for Cambodia to seek the full support of International on Cambodia's sports policy, which is preparing to host the 32nd SEA Games and the 12th ASEAN Para Games 2023 and the hosting of the 2029 Asian Youth Games.
Mr. Vath Chamroeun claimed that by hosting this General Assembly, Cambodia will benefit from the international community, such as helping to spread Cambodia through the international media to the world.
In addition, this event will also facilitate communication between the National Sports Federation of Cambodia and the International Sports Federation, the International Olympic Movement in order to strengthen the development of national sports in Cambodia. In particular, further promote the global sports movement to see the potential of Cambodia.
Mr. Vath Chamroeun said, "This is a good time for the international community and the Olympic Council of Asia to see the potential of Cambodia in sports, economy, especially the key factors of Cambodia's shadow of peace, which is taking steps to develop in all areas." "Sectors from one stage to another, while the goal of safety from Kovid 19 has also been raised internationally."
The Olympic Council of Asia is a member of the National Olympic Committee of 45 countries in Asia, including the National Olympic Committee of Cambodia. The National Olympic Committee of Cambodia became a member of the 1994 Olympic Council of Asia.
