(Phnom Penh): On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Vice President of the Mine Authority, stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has always highly valued the friendly relations and cooperation between Cambodia and Germany for the common benefit of the people and the two countries. Two
He said this on the evening of October 3, 2022 as a guest of honor and addressed the celebration of the 32nd German National Day, which was held at the residence of the German Ambassador in Phnom Penh.
He added that Cambodia has always valued friendly relations and close cooperation with Germany, which has grown in all fields based on mutual respect, common goals and common interests of the people and the country. Both.
He added that since 1994, for 28 years, Germany has supported Cambodia's socio-economic development in the areas of demining, education, culture, good governance, rural development, energy, social protection and decentralization to make a significant contribution to reducing poverty. Poor in Cambodia.
As for the economic sector, the two countries continue to enjoy strong and growing trade relations, while Germany is Cambodia's largest export market among EU member states with a bilateral trade volume of more than 1 billion dollars. In recent years.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the Senior Minister requested that Germany continue to support the work of demining and resolving the issue of explosive remnants of war in order to achieve the goal of a landmine-free Cambodia 2025 in accordance with the National Strategic Plan for Mine Action 2018-2025.
