Rape, rape and death threats cases in Prey Veng province since 2016, completed in Phnom Penh in 2022 after the Phnom Penh Armed Forces cracked down
(Phnom Penh): At 17:30 on October 2, 2022, people provided information through the telephone number 1291 of the Phnom Penh Gendarmerie Operations Command, with a woman reporting that she saw the suspect Who raped her in Prey Veng province in 2016 and 2017 in the compound of Bayon TV station Stung Meanchey, Sangkat Stung Meanchey 1, Khan Meanchey.
Immediately after receiving the information, the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie Anti-Human Trafficking Office, in cooperation with the Meanchey District Gendarmerie, used professional measures to arrest the suspect and send him to the Phnom Penh Gendarmerie Command.
Through the professional measures of the Phnom Penh Military Police, the woman described that she was raped by the suspect, Ing Pharath, 36, a construction worker, in 2016 and 2017 in Prey Veng province and threatened to kill and defame her. Public.
He later filed a complaint with the Prey Veng Provincial Court, but the suspect fled Prey Veng province and disappeared. During the suspect's escape in 2019, the investigating judge of Prey Veng Provincial Court issued an arrest warrant for him and handed him over to the court, but authorities did not find the suspect.
Until 2020, the President of the Trial Chamber of Prey Veng Provincial Court has ordered the arrest and detention of Ing Pharath for a period of seven (seven years) for rape and public defamation. Judicial police officers are still unable to find the accused.
Just arrived on October 2, 2022, he found the perpetrator in the Bayon TV station Stung Meanchey also reported to the Phnom Penh Military Police through the emergency number 1291 to arrest the suspect immediately.
