Taking the opportunity of the Cuban Prime Minister's visit to Cambodia, which is considered to strengthen the relationship and cooperation between the old friends, Fresh News would like to highlight the history of relations and cooperation between Cambodia and Cuba.
For bilateral relations, Cambodia and Cuba established diplomatic relations on April 15, 1960. In 1970, Cuba recognized the Government of National Unity of Cambodia, led by King Norodom Sihanouk. In 1979, Cuba reopened its embassy in Phnom Penh.
Cuba is an old friend of Cambodia and a great supporter of Cambodia's revival after the overthrow of the genocidal regime on January 7, 1979.
Cuba is a good friend of Cambodia, Cambodia has always remembered the merits Cuba has done to the country and the people of Cambodia in the poorest and most miserable times. But relations and cooperation between Cambodia and Cuba have been deeply ingrained in the last two decades.
In order to boost relations and cooperation with old friends, from September 23 to 25, 2022, Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen recently paid an official visit to Cuba at the invitation of President Miguel Diaz-Canel. .
During his official visit, Samdech Techo met with Cuban Parliament Speaker Esteban Lazohinandes, paid a courtesy call on former Cuban President Raul Castro and Fidel Castro, and visited the Fidel Castro Center and the Center for Engineering and Technology. Bio and invited to lay a wreath at the Jose Marti Memorial. Samdech Techo also met with Cambodian students.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also proposed to organize a visit by a group of agricultural technicians to study agricultural in Cambodia, especially rice. Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia covers all the expenses for this research study.
During Samdech Techo's visit, the two sides also discussed strengthening and expanding cooperation in the fields of health, education, sports and culture, as well as regional and international issues.
From 15 to 16 July 2019, Mr. Ouch Borith, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, paid a visit and attended a political consultation in Havana.
On September 23, 2017, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon met with Cuban Foreign Minister Prono Rodriguez Parilla during the 72nd session of the United Nations General Assembly.
The main products that Cambodia exports to Cuba are: shoes, animal skins, mixed leather and textiles, etc.
Although economic relations between Cambodia and Cuba are not very good, the two countries also have cooperation in many other areas, such as cooperation in the fields of health, education and sports and agriculture.
Based on health cooperation since the 1980s, Cuba has provided scholarships to 36 Cambodian medical students to study in Cuba.
In terms of education, from 1980 to 2021, 144 Cambodian students and civil servants received scholarships to study for postgraduate and higher education in Cuba through the selection and transfer examinations of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports of Cambodia.
As of August 2022, there are 6 Cambodian students studying in Cuba.
