Lifting health bans on foreigners entering Cambodia will be a favorable factor for attracting tourists and investors
(Phnom Penh): Tourism experts and businessmen in Cambodia see the decision to remove health measures for foreigners entering Cambodia as another favorable opportunity to attract international tourists and foreign investors to Cambodia at the same time. The Royal Government has set out key strategies to attract an estimated 7.5 million international tourists to Cambodia by 2028.
Thuon Sina, President of the Asia-Pacific Tourism Association of Cambodia, said that the removal of the additional barrier is a great convenience for international travelers and the private sector compared to other countries. This will encourage as well as encourage more tourists to Cambodia.
He added that if the current global crisis can be controlled or not another crisis, Cambodia will be able to achieve at least 50% of the tourist attraction strategy set by the Royal Government.
Oknha Lim Heng, Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, said that while Cambodia has implemented free trade agreements, it has attracted foreign investment in Cambodia, and the Royal Government's decision to open up health measures will become Another mechanism to attract more investors as well as foreign tourists to come to Cambodia to learn about investment opportunities in Cambodia.
He said that the opening up to Cambodia as usual proves that the leadership of the Royal Government has defeated 19 Kovid.
He added: "We look at the global context today. Kovid vaccination has been vaccinated in almost every country, which has been gradually opened up abroad, but not as openly as Cambodia. Cambodia has the potential that government leaders can. "Overcoming by almost 100% vaccination, which we expect, even if infected, does not cause a high risk of death, which is one point we do not have serious concerns."
