Minister of Culture: Khmer Bassac's performance drops due to lack of support, in China, tickets to the Beijing Opera cost at least $ 500 amid strong support
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Phoeung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts, on October 3, 2022, stated that the development of bassac theater has slowed down and this is due to lack of support.
Speaking at the opening ceremony of the 2022 National Bassac Theater at the Department of Performing Arts Theater, Ms. Phoeung Sakona called for the support of the Bassac Theater from the masses, especially the youth, so that Bassac Theater can flourish as in the past.
Bassac Theater, originally named Treung Khlok Theater, originated in Kampuchea Krom, Basak District, Preah Trapeang Province. During the 1930s, Trung Khlok was performed in Phnom Penh and some provinces along the Bassac River and became very popular, initially called the Bassac district, but later abbreviated as theatrical. Bassac and is still famous today.
She believes that the rise of smartphones is not the reason for the decline of Bassac, but because there is no momentum of support, because in China, even though people have a lot of smartphones, the momentum of support for Peking Opera. There was a resurgence of activity.
"We lack human resources, we lack materials, equipment and infrastructure." This is according to the Minister of Culture.
Ms. Phoeung Sakona considered that the National Bassac Theater Festival 2022 under the theme "Culture of Peace" is an important platform for dissemination to the public at all levels, visit and gradually learn about the many forms of Khmer art that require Participate in caring, protecting and promoting.
