General Chhum Socheat: So far, more than 20,000 remains of the Vietnamese army during the war in Cambodia have been found
(Phnom Penh): General Chhum Socheat, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of National Defense, confirmed to Fresh News that from 2002 to 2022, cooperation in the search for the remains of the Vietnamese People's Army in Cambodia has been Found a total of 23,074 remains, all of which were found by six regional armies.
He claimed that the six military zones, including the Special Military Zone found 2007, the 1st Military Zone found 2241 elements, the 2nd Military Zone found 8153 elements, the 3rd Military Zone found 4171 elements, the 4th Military Zone found 2794 elements, the 5th Military Zone found 3708 Item.
The Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of Vietnam signed an agreement on August 28, 2000 on the search, gathering and repatriation of the remains of Vietnamese volunteer soldiers who were sacrificed during the Cambodian war.
The general added that after the discovery until now, the remains of the Vietnamese People's Army were handed over to the Vietnamese side by the Cambodian side.
