More than 40,000 people participated in the Water Festival in Oddar Meanchey
(Oddar Meanchey): After missing for two years due to the outbreak of Kovid 19, on October 1, 2022, Oddar Meanchey Provincial Administration re-organized the Water Festival at Boeung Snor in front of Provincial Hall to bring Entertaining and entertaining the people as well as preserving the traditional customs of the ancestors.
The Water Festival, Ok Ambok, Moon Worship and Lantern Floating Festival are held for two days. In addition to boating, there are also concerts at night to entertain the people. For two days, there were a lot of people in the province and from other provinces to enjoy. According to the information, the two-day festival was attended by about 40,000 people.
Speaking at the closing ceremony of the Water Festival on the evening of October 2, 2022, Mr. Pen Kosal, Governor of Oddar Meanchey province, expressed his happiness with people from all over who came to visit the grand ceremony.
The provincial governor highlighted that this gathering and fun was possible because Cambodia, under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, had overcome the epidemic of Kovid 19. In particular, vaccinations have become widespread throughout the country.
"Overcoming the Kovid 19 pandemic has allowed our country to resume economic activity in all areas. "Under the high attention of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the people can do business normally and have a prosperous life without having to worry about the Kovid crisis as before." This is the emphasis of Mr. Pen Kosal.
However, on that occasion, Mr. Pen Kosal continued to call on people to continue to pay attention to the fight against Kovid 19 by adhering to the measures of the Ministry of Health, especially to continue to receive vaccines as promptly. .
Mr. Pen Kosal praised all the water players who for two days released their energy to make people happy. Especially trying to win trophies for their team with pride. The provincial governor instructed all athletes to continue to train better to prepare for the race in the coming years.
The provincial governor also gave incentives to the boats that participated in the competition. In that, the boat that won the first place received a trophy and a budget of 8 million riels, the second place received a trophy and a budget of 6 million riels and the third place received a budget of 4 million riels. Separately, the player who did not win received an incentive of 500,000 Riels.
