Sweden has re-authorized the export of war equipment to Turkey in a concession to Ankara that threatens to block Nordic NATO membership. This is according to the release by AFP on Sunday, October 2, 2022.
Ankara has called for the lifting of sanctions imposed in 2019 following the Turkish offensive in northeastern Syria, while Sweden applied for NATO membership in mid-May.
The Strategic Product Monitoring Service said in a statement that the government has assessed Sweden's membership in NATO as the best way to keep Sweden and its people safe.
"Sweden's application for NATO membership has significantly strengthened the defense and security policy arguments for approving the export of war material to other member states, including Turkey," Swedish authorities said. .
