(Phnom Penh): In order to avoid flooding of roads and villages while the sky continues to rain every day, on the morning of October 2, 2022, Mr. Khim Sun Soda, Governor of Kambol District, led the officers to inspect And put machinery to restore the canal along National Road 4, which is full of all kinds of garbage, especially the grass that grows near the canal, causing the water to flow slowly and stop flowing.
The district governor told Fresh News Agency that the canal along National Road 4 was very important to prevent flooding and flooding of houses along the road. In the past, he led the force to carry out regular rehabilitation work for one or two months, placing machinery once from the border point of Ang Snoul district, Kandal province to the border of Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Khim Sunsoda said that only for a short time in the canal full of garbage and grass, especially French grass has grown near the canal, causing the water to flow slowly or can not flow at all due to the fertile soil. This French weed grows the fastest in just one or two months, covering the canal and causing the water to clog and flow slowly, so it needs to be restored regularly to avoid flooding of roads and villages. .
At the same time, the Governor of Kambol District also called on all residents living on either side of National Road 4 or those in other places to keep the garbage properly so that the garbage truck can take it away. Do not throw rubbish into ditches or sewers, and when it rains, it will block the flow of water and flood the village road.
