Ms. Chea Serey: CBC has a huge role to play in providing financial services in Cambodia towards digitalization and advanced data analysis
Ms. Chea Serey's remarks were made during the celebration of the 10th anniversary of the establishment of KREDIT BURO, the Cambodian Credit Bureau, with the participation of Ms. Ouk Maly, Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia.
Ms. Chea Serey stated that the presence of the CBC for the past 10 years has contributed to the significant growth of the financial sector and the credit market, not only helping the people of Cambodia to have access to a wider and more credible loan. Growing every year, customers who get these loans not only get business credit, but also have the ability to buy the necessary equipment to use.
She stated that in a short period of time, CBC has expanded into a modern and fully developed information sharing system to share credit information and provide many additional services. In addition, the CBC not only maintains a history of negative information, but also a wealth of positive information in order to encourage the responsible use of credit by borrowers.
"Although the CBC has evolved rapidly, it continues to grow its vision because the CBC has a big shoulder on the Cambodian financial services, which requires us to look forward to the future," she said. "Digital capture and advanced data analysis to enable financial institutions to make informed decisions."
Mr. Oeur Sothearoth, Executive Director of CBC, stated that for the past 10 years, CBC has been working to establish a credit data management nursery in Cambodia and has assisted 181 CBC member financial institutions, raising awareness of The financial health of the client is also a priority.
He said that in order to increase the ease of use of financial services, CBC has set up digital programs for the public to check their financial health.
Ms. Ouk Maly congratulated the organization on the 10th anniversary of the establishment of the Credit Bureau of Cambodia. She said the CBC plays an important role in supporting responsible, efficient and fair credit to reduce risk to banking and microfinance institutions.
On that occasion, there was also the official launch of a digital property appraisal partnership between CBC and Vtrust, which will make it easier for CBC members to use the real estate appraisal database to provide loans.
