Three monks robbed, arrested a monk, arrested
(Kampong Speu): The Inspectorate of Bor Seth District, Kampong Speu Province, on October 1, 202, yesterday arrested three monks who robbed a phone and a suffix from a monk.
The robbery took place at Wat Svay Char, Stok Commune, Kong Pisey District, Kampong Speu Province at 7:30 on September 30, 2022. The victim monk, Vat Sok Viet, 20 years old, lived at Wat Thom Mongkul in Trapeang Phlong village, Pheary Meanchey commune, Bor Seth district, Kampong Speu province.
According to John Sophit, Bor Seth District Police Inspector, on the night of September 30, 2022, he was abducted by a group of suspects who stole an iPhone and 20,000 Khmer Riel when he was summoned. Exit the pagoda. The monk confirmed that he had been beaten, causing his face to bulge and his eyes to bruise.
The inspector said that immediately after receiving the complaint, the specialized force launched an investigation to identify the suspects and arrested three monks for questioning, including:
First: Phon Makara, 16 years old, Second: Doeun Vandeth, 16 years old, and third: Roeun Theara, 14 years old, who is a vegan at the above pagoda, came to the inspectorate.
