As Cambodia and the world began to experience the spread of Kovid 19, a number of countries and flights closed, and a large number of businesses, especially tourism, were severely affected. During this difficult time, this group of entrepreneurs generated nearly $ 6 million (US $ 5.6 million) in cash for their business in one year from September 2021 to September. 2022.
Chheang Sideth With such success, it has enabled the group's small and medium-sized enterprises to continue to overcome business closures in the context of the Kovid, which may be the best sign for Cambodia's socio-economic development.
He said that if more than 100 entrepreneurs close their businesses, it will have an additional level of socio-economic impact on the existing impact, as enterprises as well as small and medium-sized businesses are the backbone of the national economy. Continuing this business is to create jobs for full-fledged Cambodians who are in dire need of income to support their families in the context of Kovid.
BNI Super is a group of potential business owners who have raised nearly $ 6 million in cash for team members through the use of the US business system to strengthen their business reach international standards. In the United States and the world.
