(Phnom Penh): Cambodia is ready to host the 33rd ASEAN Environmental Ministers' Meeting and related meetings in Angkor, Siem Reap Province from October 3 to 7, 2022.
The meeting will also discuss the ASEAN Joint Position on the Draft ASEAN Joint Declaration on Climate Change and Biodiversity.
In addition, the ASEAN + 3, ASEAN, China, Japan and South Korea will hold a meeting to review the progress of the implementation of cooperation agreed upon by ASEAN member states within the five-year strategic framework and further strengthen cooperation. Partner between ASEAN Plus 3 to better meet the needs of the regional framework on the environment.
There will also be an ASEAN-US Senior Officials Meeting on Environment and an ASEAN-EU Meeting to discuss the environment and climate change to further strengthen and expand regional cooperation with the United States and Europe.
The results of these meetings will then be submitted to the ASEAN Environment Ministers' Meeting for review and approval in 2023.
Please note that on October 5, the opening ceremony of the ASEAN Senior Officials Meeting and the 33rd relevant meeting in Siem Reap officially.
