Interior Ministry spokesman: 64 people arrested for criminal and drug offenses on September 30
(Phnom Penh): At least 64 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on September 30, 2022 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News on October 1.
General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 64 suspects, 28 were arrested in 18 criminal cases and 36 were arrested in 16 drug cases.
At the same time, he called on all citizens to implement the slogan "3 do not 1 report", which means "do not be involved, do not intervene, do not exempt in various crimes and help report drug offenses and other crimes. "Arrested at the local level to the authorities. Detained 6 people intended to cross the border to Thailand illegally
(Banteay Meanchey): On the night of September 30, 2022, under the command of Major General Sithi Loh, Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner, Lieutenant Colonel Suong Sao, Commander of the 815th Border Police Battalion, in cooperation with the military, arrested six workers. People who intend to cross the border illegally to work in Thailand.
According to Mr. Suong Sao, the 5 Chambok police force, led by Brigadier General Bun Kun, Chief of the Border Guard Police of the 815th Battalion, in cooperation with the Armed Forces of the Deputy Division of Mamalai District and the Secondary Division of Poipet City, prevented Six people (2 females) were smuggled across the border to Thailand at Lvea village, Boeung Beng commune, Malai district, Banteay Meanchey province.
