Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that since the implementation of the cash support program for poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid 19 from June 2020 to September 2022, there have been 10 rounds. The Royal Government has spent more than $ 800 million.
Samdech Techo confirmed this during the meeting with people who volunteered to move construction from the Angkor resort area of nearly 3,000 more families on Saturday morning, October 1, 2022.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated: "And I would like to order that the Cambodian People's Party in the upcoming election does not make promises about the elderly, the elderly have a salary, children have a salary, but the government "The CPP has been doing this for years. Out of 700,000 families, the elderly, the children, among them, pregnant women will receive more money."
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also set a policy to provide equity cards (poor card type 1) to people who moved from other areas to the Run Ta Ek area for 10 years.
"The CPP has no promises, but has been implementing a package of issues for both the elderly and pregnant women, which has been implemented for years, with a budget of more than $ 20 million for pregnant women. "In the Run Ta Ek area, no matter who has a car or a motorbike, everyone is considered poor and has to hold a poor card for 10 years together." This is an additional emphasis of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
The provision of equity cards and the implementation of cash to poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid 19 is made without discrimination on the basis of political affiliation, but is extended to all families who are considered to be in genuine poverty. .
Law enforcement forces regularly monitor and monitor the traffic of citizens on the expressway on the day of the test launch
(Phnom Penh): After launching the test run of the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway on October 1, 2022, the traffic police force and inspection team regularly patrolled to see the movement of people on Cambodia's first expressway.
According to the Department of Traffic Police and Public Order, the mobile patrol and intervention team of the Department of Traffic Police and Public Order and the regular team on the security camera system monitored the test trips of people on the expressway. Fast.
The department confirmed that through the security camera, the intervention team saw the motorcycle traveling on the expressway, the authorities also stopped to educate, not explaining that the expressway does not require motorcycles under 600cc to travel. And asked him to leave this road as well.
In addition, the intervention team also towed a car that had a problem and needed intervention to get off the road. In this regard, please confirm to the people who use this expressway that the authorities are constantly monitoring this trip to help intervene in case passengers need any emergency assistance. In case of need, citizens can contact the phone number displayed and advertised as well.
Please be informed that Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway has a length of 187.05 km, which connects Village 1, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh to Village 1, Sangkat 3, Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province on the morning of October 1. This 2022 has started to give people a free trial for one month from this morning.
The Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway is the first expressway and the most important strategic corridor in Cambodia, reducing travel time from Phnom Penh to Sihanoukville from five hours to just two hours and Reduce logistics costs as well.
