Samdech Techo Hun Sen made this announcement during a meeting with people who volunteered to move from the Angkor resort area to live in Run Ta Ek Natural Village on October 1, 2022.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Prime Minister announced that Samdech Techo not to dismantle the pagoda in the Angkor resort area to another place, that is, Samdech Techo decided to keep the pagoda that was established before to remain the same. While some monasteries have been around for hundreds of years, such as North Angkor Wat and South Angkor Wat, they date back to the 16th century.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister appealed to these 35 pagodas not to build more stupas or graves, especially for people from outside. Excess cases are only allowed for the left / right sutras or monks in those pagodas.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also announced a strict ban on the construction of Buddhist pagodas, mosques, Christian churches, Chinese temples or hermitages, huts, statues or any other beliefs in the Angkor resort area. .
The Head of the Royal Government also issued an order to the APSARA Authority and the Siem Reap Provincial Administration to be responsible for this work before the Minister of Culture and Fine Arts to the Prime Minister and to the Royal Government.
Samdech Techo also ordered the Siem Reap Provincial Governor, the Provincial Unity Command and the Provincial Department of Cult and Religion to cooperate in effectively monitoring this work.
In addition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also asked the vendors in the pagoda to be clean, tidy, organized in their business base to increase the beauty and attractiveness for tourism.
