After traveling on the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway, many people expressed their happiness and admiration with the praise that this road is really beautiful and easy to Save a lot of time and reduce the cost of gasoline.
"I am very happy to see that Cambodia is starting to have beautiful, wide and convenient roads, and after traveling more than 100 kilometers on the expressway, Ms. Chhun Him said," "I think this road was good in the past, now it is closer than before, I was excited after riding on this road, which has a beautiful view, the road is clean, fast and safe."
Ms. Chhun Him added that traveling on the expressway not only provides convenience for travel, but also reduces fuel costs and saves a lot of time. She also claimed that even though the road started charging, it still continued to ride on this road.
Unlike Ms. Chhun Him, as a driver, Mr. Ouch Tharith stated that traveling on this expressway is very easy, as he can drive at a constant speed of 100 kilometers per hour. Provides comfort for the driver and really very convenient due to the use of less time, less fuel, and on the road there are clear signs on the road with the right lanes, easy to drive as well.
Ms. Chea Chansrey Leak also expressed her happiness after seeing the wide and beautiful expressway that has never been seen before and confirmed that she will continue to ride on this road despite spending money. She also thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, for his efforts to help build more and better roads to make it easier for people to travel.
Please also note that the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway has a length of 187.05 km, which started construction on March 22, 2019. This road connects Village 1, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh to Village 1, Sangkat 3, Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province.
