In a get-together with the people who moved to Run Ta Ek Natural Village, Samdech Techo Prime Minister affirmed that Cambodia is not a descendant regime like North Korea, but depends on the people. This means that people voting is not against Cambodian law.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has been the Prime Minister for almost 40 years. Samdech Techo has been elected Prime Minister at a young age of 32 and has served as Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs at the age of 27.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also stated that for the upcoming 2023 election, Samdech is still in the position of the Prime Minister's candidate for a change of leadership, which is after the election. For the position of Prime Minister, Samdech works until he no longer wants to do, and for the preparation of people to take turns is normal for the next generation.
Please be informed that Cambodia is a liberal, multi-party democracy where the leaders of the country must be elected by the people. In contrast, in a communist country like North Korea, leaders are only elected through the media.
In fact, Kim Jong Un, now an influential North Korean leader, was appointed senior leader by his father in 2011. Kim Jong Un is the son of Kim Jong Il and the grandson of former North Korean leader Kim Il Sung.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia also stated that the preparation of Dr. Hun Manet as the candidate for the future Prime Minister of the Cambodian People's Party is a pre-arrangement to avoid any eventual problems.
Dr. Hun Manet was elected by the Extraordinary Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party on July 16-17, 2022 as the future Prime Minister. The election in this party has caused a great deal of congratulations from the people's leaders who support the CPP.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Mr. Hun Manet has to go through two stages to become the Prime Minister, in which he needs votes from the people to become the Member of Parliament, and another stage if Mr. Hun Manet is appointed by the King. The monarch as prime minister must match the cabinet to seek the trust of the National Assembly.
