This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued to meet with nearly 3,000 families volunteering to relocate from the Angkor resort area.
(Siem Reap): On the morning of Saturday, October 1, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, continued to meet with 2,751 other families who volunteered to relocate their houses and structures from the Angkor resort area. The area is under the control of APSARA Authority. The meeting will take place in Run Ta Ek Natural Village in Banteay Srei District, Siem Reap Province, where the Royal Government provides land to people in exchange for demolition.
According to the report of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, the operation to preserve Angkor as a human resource in the world has achieved the measurement and extraction of land plots occupied by people in the Angkor resort area in 114 villages, 24 communes / sangkats and 5 cities / districts equal to 97,855 plots of land with an area of 29,174 hectares.
At the same time, a total of 3,868 families who volunteered to demolish illegal structures from the Angkor resort area and other areas under the control of the APSARA Authority were selected to relocate to the Ronta Ek Development Zone. People volunteered and dismantled about 400 illegal stalls, sheds and houses in the Angkor resort area.
General Kheng Someth, Commander of the Hun Sen Siem Reap Techo Engineering Corps, said that he had deployed a total of more than 200 machines and a force of more than 1,000 men to operate on the site of the Run Ta Ek Natural Village.
The report shows that the clearing of land in Run Ta Ek Natural Village has reached more than 431 hectares, equivalent to more than 76% of the total area of 566 hectares. Construction of 20 km of red gravel road, construction of 2 new school buildings equal to 24 rooms and 1 office building and library equal to 3 rooms achieved 15%.
Construction of health centers includes: 1 general ward, 1 maternity ward and 1 doctor's dormitory, 15%, 8 markets, 5%.
The preparation of a water supply system from Angkor Market along National Road 66 to the location of the 17-kilometer Run Ta Ek Development Zone is underway.
Construction of 5 telephone antenna towers, 2 of which are scheduled to be completed in the first week of November 2022 and 3 more are planned to be built in a row.
The first phase of the grid in Zone 1 and Zone 2 of the Run Ta Ek Development Zone has achieved about 5 percent. The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has trained in agriculture and distributed chickens, ducks, fish and vegetables to the people.
When the Royal Government began to improve and rehabilitate roads in Siem Reap, as well as prepare the banks of the Siem Reap River by the end of 2020, Mr. Bun Chhay, along with more than 500 other people living on the road and river food, was also facilitated by the authorities to move out. Provide policy land in Run Ta Ek village, about 20 meters by 30 meters.
Mr. Bun Chhay and people affected by other projects also volunteered to live in the new village, about 24 kilometers from Siem Reap.
With the evacuation of Siem Reap, the authorities have also prepared infrastructure such as roads, water and electricity to support the lives of the people.
Mr. Bun Chhay and his family built a decent house while the other half land was leased to a Christian clerk. Mr. Bun Chhay and his family, as well as other residents, have been living in the new village for almost two years.
Living in Run Ta Ek village, Mr. Bun Chhay expressed his satisfaction and happiness in his new life, even though he was a little far from the city, he got his own land and felt much fresher compared to the narrow road.
