Samdech Techo Hun Sen has decided to take forest land in Run Ta Ek commune, Banteay Srei district, Siem Reap province to provide 20 meters by 30 meters per family for people to volunteer to move houses and structures from Angkor and other areas. Under the control of APSARA Authority. The land in the area is about 24 km from Siem Reap city and is currently degraded forest land.
In addition to allocating land for housing, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also managed to set up infrastructure systems such as roads, water, electricity, schools, hospitals and markets to make life easier for people. In order to build houses and infrastructure, clearing and clearing of forests in this area requires.
General Kheng Someth received an order from Samdech Techo Hun Sen to clear the forest, prepare the land and build infrastructure in the Run Ta Ek development area as soon as possible.
In order to fulfill the order of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, General Kheng Someth, also known as Lok Ta Phnom 100, deployed his forces very quickly. General Kheng Someth told Fresh News that he had deployed a total of more than 200 vehicles and a force of more than 1,000 to launch an operation to transform Prey Run Ta Ek into a beautiful village.
In this operation, General Kheng Someth led the operation force directly, regardless of the holiday. Currently, the machinery and forces are operating very actively.
General Kheng Someth expressed the expectation that the forest clearing, land preparation and infrastructure construction could be completed in a short period of time as Samdech Techo wanted so that people could build houses and move in soon.
The first phase of the grid in Zone 1 and Zone 2 of the Run Ta Ek Development Zone has achieved about 5 percent. The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has trained in agriculture and distributed chickens, ducks, fish and vegetables to the people.
