(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Muong Sothea, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, has issued some important guidelines to the Economic Crimes Police to improve the inactivity, gaps in the implementation of professional procedures, combined with the growth of Modern technology that requires officials to have the resources, skills and expertise to do those tasks appropriately according to the actual evolving situation.
Lt. Gen. Muong Sothea's introduction was made at the closing ceremony of the "Intellectual Property Crimes and Investigation Procedures Against Money Laundering" organized by the Department of Economic Crimes under the auspices of ThaiLiki and Gibbins. 103 participants from the Department of Economic Crime and the Capital-Provincial Police Commissioner.
This refresher course aims to strengthen and increase the professional capacity of law enforcement officers, which is the main factor in accordance with the strategic plan of the General Commission of the National Police and the action plan of the Department to prevent and suppress crimes in a timely and effective manner. .
In order to respond to and in accordance with the content of the current refresher course, Lt. Gen. Muong Sothea advised all participants to continue to pay attention to the implementation of some points better, including:
* Strive to continue to implement the direction and annual strategic plan of the Ministry of Interior as well as the General Commission of the National Police
* Continue to increase efforts to investigate, investigate and crack down on crime, production, import of illegal drugs, counterfeit and expired food, unhygienic use of banned chemicals that affect the well-being of the people.
* Efforts to increase research, investigation and crackdown on all types of smuggling crimes to contribute to increase national budget revenue
* Continue to make efforts to find all measures to prevent and suppress natural resource crimes
* Must continue to work to strengthen the quality and efficiency of crime data management, with a system to receive information and respond to incidents related to crime suppression reports in the capital-province (via the website, email, online, web, etc ..)
* Have a regular life meeting program by urging subordinates to promote professional ethics and study and understand the laws and regulations that serve research and investigation, especially to strengthen the implementation of discipline in accordance with Regulation No. 006 of the General Commission. National Police
* Strive to continue to develop human resources in the economic police force by conducting short-term and long-term training courses on-site both in the overall training system and on a local basis.
* There must be good unity in the ranks of the forces as well as in the whole unit.
During these two days, Lt. Gen. Deputy Commissioner General believes that all trainees will gain new knowledge and good experience to carry out their duties and share this knowledge to colleagues and thanks. The team that organized this refresher course smoothly and successfully completed it.
