In order to protect the Angkor resort area from being inscribed on the World Heritage List, Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to launch a hot campaign last August to prepare the land, especially to dismantle the irregular and illegal structures at the Angkor resort. And areas managed by APSARA Authority.
Recognizing the intention to preserve the reputation of the Angkor site on the UNESCO World Heritage List, residents of the Angkor site and the area controlled by the APSARA Authority have volunteered to demolish their buildings.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has decided to provide land compensation policy in Run Ta Ek Natural Village in Run Ta Ek Commune, Banteay Srei District, more than 25 kilometers from Siem Reap City, with each family receiving 20 meters by 30 meters of land for housing and other crops. .
In addition to providing land for housing, Samdech Techo has managed to build infrastructure, including roads, electricity, water, markets, schools and hospitals. Samdech Techo also instructed the engineering team to clear the forest to prepare the people's village.
As of the beginning of September, more than 1,000 families have volunteered to move out of the Angkor area and seize land in the Run Ta Ek Natural Village. Some residents have already allocated their plots.
The people who received the land in Run Ta Ek Natural Village were all happy with Samdech Techo's management and arrangement for their new village. People who have already been allocated plots of land have started to come down and prepare land for housing and other crops.
During the preparation of the village, the villagers faced some difficulties in preparing the land of the Kat villagers because the newly cleared forest land was uneven, with some places high, some low and some places flooded when it rained. Because the road is fenced.
