Senior Minister Kun Kim: Disaster situation in Cambodia is not serious as the floods caused by the effects of Hurricane Nuro have decreased (Video inside) (Udom Meanchey): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management confirmed that The catastrophic situation in Cambodia is not yet serious, as the flooding caused by the effects of Hurricane Noru has greatly reduced and the Royal Government is in full control.
