China will introduce city-specific property policies to support the implementation of monetary policy, Bloomberg reported, citing a statement issued Thursday by the People's Bank of China. Special loans are meant to ensure the completion of a real estate project and a reasonable increase in loan size.
The statement summarized the decision of the quarterly meeting of the Monetary Policy Committee chaired by Governor Yi Gang, which met on September 23.
The slump in the housing market more than a year ago has continued to drag down China's economy, which has added to the damage to economic growth caused by the already zero Kovid policy.
Although China's economy appears to have recovered during the April-June period, the closure of Shanghai, Jilin Province and other major economic centers has almost boosted GDP. The downturn and many economists are lowering their expectations for full-year growth.
China's central bank said in a statement released on Thursday that it would advise commercial banks to provide financial support to protect the interests of homebuyers and support the development of a healthy housing market. Good. According to Bloomberg.
