Spokesman of the Ministry of Cult: Only the role of advisor to the clergy does not receive the title of "Excellency or Lok Chumteav"
(Phnom Penh): A person appointed as an advisor to the Board of Priests does not receive the title of "Excellency or Lok Chumteav" unless the person appointed has a separate Royal Decree. This is according to Mr. Seng Somony, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Cult and Religion.
Mr. Seng Somony's statement was made at the press conference of the Royal Government Spokesperson's Unit on September 29, 2022, after some misunderstanding about the nickname "His Excellency or Lok Chumteav". Role as an advisor to the presiding priest or advisor to the high priest.
Mr. Seng Somony claimed that in the past, some crooks used the title "His Excellency or Lok Chumteav" in connection with the role of Samdech Sangkha's advisor to misuse it with malicious intent to deceive others under various images.
He further explained that in the case where the King issues a Royal Decree appointing a position with the title of "His Excellency or Lok Chumteav", then when the Sangha Council announces the position of advisor to the Sangha Council, then that person has the title "Excellency or Lok Chumteav." In particular, for those who do not have a royal decree, they do not automatically receive the title of "Excellency or Lok Chumteav" by the priest.
The Finnish government has said the move will lead to a significant reduction in cross-border traffic after nearly 17,000 Russians crossed the border into the country over the weekend.
Foreign Minister Pekka Haavisto told a news conference that "the entry of Russian citizens (for tourism purposes) into Finland endangers Finland's international relations," explaining that the ban was made in accordance with the law. Talks with Ukraine and neighboring countries.
However, he emphasized that entry into the country for family visits as well as for work and study would still be allowed.
With this decision, the Finnish government has joined other EU member states on the border with Russia, which have already blocked Russian tourists. The European Union has banned all flights from Russia, leaving only rail and road transport links.
