(Phnom Penh): After a two-year absence due to the 19-Kovid epidemic, on the morning of Thursday, September 29, 2022, the Royal Government of Cambodia re-organized the "Interfaith Forum Against Human Trafficking". The forum was chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and was attended by many other relevant officials.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen delivered a speech for about 1 hour and 30 minutes, the following are the main contents of Samdech Techo:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that working as the Prime Minister has no right to get sick, no right to complain. This statement came after Samdech was very busy with work both abroad and in the country.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Cambodian People's Party from the beginning until the implementation of religious harmony, making all religions can live together. Religious and ethnic differences are not a barrier to living together.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that former US President Donald Trump built a border fence to prevent human trafficking. Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that in the United States, Europe and the Middle East, there is a serious crisis, refugees and opportunities for trafficking for criminals.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that human trafficking is a global problem that requires the unification of all countries to fight.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the past, Cambodia was a place where people fled abroad because of the war.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodians were also deceived into working abroad.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that Mr. Amat Yasya was arrested in the past for human trafficking.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that during 2006-2007, he was lucky enough to open a Taiwanese representative office in Cambodia to handle the preparation of about 5,000 Cambodian women to Taiwan.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that human trafficking to Cambodia is because Cambodia is peaceful and there are some other problems.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng for his efforts to crack down on human trafficking.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that there is no need for the Prime Minister or the Minister of the Interior to shout to stop the game, let's make it rain.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that religious denominations play an important role in preventing and preventing human trafficking through the education of the members of each religion.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that after the attack on the US commercial building, Cambodia cooperated well with the United States and other countries to prevent terrorism until the arrest of those involved in terrorism.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that although Cambodia is not a target for terrorist attacks, we must work together to prevent Cambodia from becoming a haven for terrorism.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen decides to make August 20 the National Interfaith Day against Human Trafficking. Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructed all religious denominations to hold various gatherings on August 20 to educate and fight against human trafficking.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reprimands the company that won the lottery business license, if the lottery is opened, the business will be closed immediately.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructs the authorities to crack down on gambling to find the mastermind.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on all to fight against corruption so that Cambodia does not become a place of crime, money laundering and human trafficking.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his belief that cracking down on gambling will contribute to reducing human trafficking and increasing security, security and social order.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on people to continue to receive the Kovid 19 vaccine, do not underestimate the epidemic.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the world is full of problems and complexities. Europe used to use gas and protect forests, now they cut down trees for firewood.
