Norway, Poland and Denmark inaugurate Baltic gas pipeline as Russian gas pipeline damaged
The leaders of Norway, Poland and Denmark attended an inauguration ceremony on Wednesday to celebrate the opening of a new pipeline to transport gas from the Norwegian plateau to Poland via Denmark. This is according to the release by eauronews on Wednesday, September 28, 2022.
Norway's Equinor has signed a 10-year agreement to supply 2.4 billion cubic meters per year, or 15 percent of Poland's annual consumption.
The Baltic pipeline will be a major transit route for gas from Norway via Denmark to Poland and neighboring countries. It will be able to import up to 10 billion cubic meters of gas annually from Norway to Poland and 3 billion cubic meters from Poland to Denmark.
