Kandal Provincial Administration Holds a Meeting to Gather Experiences on Cracking down on Illegal Gambling and Serving Citizens in Lvea Em District
(Kandal): On September 28, 2022, Mr. Nuth Puth Dara, Deputy Governor of Kandal Province, chaired a meeting to review and draw on the experience of cracking down on illegal gambling in the past and to set the direction to continue the crackdown on gambling. Addiction, combating human trafficking, labor trafficking, sex work, land dispute mediation, and providing services to people in Lvea Em district.
The meeting was attended by the chairmen of district councils, district governors, relevant departments, district governors, district offices, armed forces, commune chiefs and 15 police chiefs in Lvea Em district.
During the meeting, Mr. Nuth Puth Dara instructed the meeting on the important work to be implemented such as:
* Continue to pay attention to the strict implementation of the high order of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, to crack down on illegal gambling, unlicensed pawnshops or misappropriation. From legal principles.
Let the District Administrative Unity Command lead all armed forces to continue to monitor, control, crack down and prevent them from happening at the district level. Illegal pawn shop gambling is a source of all kinds of thefts and robberies, so cracking down on gambling and illegal pawn shops is also a factor in reducing these crimes.
All civil servants of the Armed Forces should not be involved in or intervene in these cases, which is against the law, and must cooperate in reporting in order to lead a complete crackdown at the local level.
The suppression of human trafficking, labor trafficking and sex trafficking, drug offenses in any form must be eliminated. The district administration should cooperate in monitoring and researching locally so that there is no location where human trafficking or sex and drug trafficking is embedded.
* Regarding the settlement of land disputes in the district, the district administration has done a good job in resolving the remaining issues for the local people. Procedures and procedures of the District Cadastral Commission for land that does not have a title deed in case of unresolved cases shall be sent to the Provincial Cadastral Commission for further resolution.
* Provision of services to the people at the district level, there is a OWSO in the district, and at the commune level, there is a OWSO mechanism with the service price list and the period of service as determined by the people. Implement the OWSO effectively and disseminate the price list and service period to local people.
* For the registration of birth certificates, birth certificates, marriage certificates, and death certificates, the Commune / Sangkat Councilor would like to send the commune to the back of the house in order to bring the service closer to the people and make the people happier. To the leadership of local authorities.
* Identification card, residence book, family book, Mr. Inspector, Chief of Post, please continue to urge the people as soon as possible. Acting Chairman of the Senate, Mr. Sim Ka, sent a message of condolences to Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly on the death of the senior disciple of Buddhism.
