(Banteay Meanchey): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's staff on disaster work, on Wednesday afternoon, September 22, 2022, continued to inspect the flood situation in Banteay Meanchey province.
According to the provincial report, five districts in Banteay Meanchey province are facing floods. It affects more than 7,000 families.
The five districts affected by the floods include Serei Sophorn, Mongkul Borei, Phnom Srok, Preah Net Preah and Malai districts.
During the inspection, Senior Minister Kun Kim traveled by boat and water to the flooded houses. The Senior Minister also brought food donations from the Prime Minister to distribute to the flood victims.
Senior Minister Kun Kim brought a message from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross.
The Senior Minister also expressed his condolences for the impact as well as the damage to people's crops from the floods. However, the Senior Minister informed the people that Samdech Techo Prime Minister has already advised to be ready to help the people to repair the damage after the water recedes. The thing to take care of now is to stay healthy and save lives from the floods.
