(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, urged the local commune / sangkat officials to speed up the provision of services to the people through the OWSO mechanism if there is any delay or delay to explain Tell people the reason clearly so that they do not have to wait or be disappointed.
Mr. Chhit Sophat, Chief of Sangkat 1, Sihanoukville, explained in front of the Governor of Kouch Chamroeun Province that in the case of providing services through the OWSO at Sangkat 1, the officers follow the procedure. Some delays are due to the large number of applications for all forms of citizens, as Sangkat 1 is being declared a jurisdiction and the number of officers is limited. In particular, to say that you give money fast is not the case.
The chief of Sangkat 1 continued that in the past, the administration of Sangkat 1 also invited Mr. Unhat to confirm what he said in the pack of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, in which Mr. Unhat stated that he was upset with the provision of services. Late and that no commune official is required to pay $ 100 to do so quickly.
Mr. Unhat has now received the marriage certificate, in which he also made a contract acknowledging the mistake of providing false information.
After listening to the explanations and explanations, the Governor of Kouch Chamroeun Province reminded the local officials of the commune / sangkat to speed up the provision of services to the people through the OWSO mechanism and to check which documents Citizens need to be able to not delay for a long time, must try to resolve the procedure quickly.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun continued to advise that all services that are missed are not provided to the citizens immediately, the officials must explain to the citizens to know the reasons and to set a clear time for the people to accept not to miss the time.
The provincial governor added that he did not have a ban on freedom of expression, but asked to state what was true.
At the same time, the provincial governor also assigned the working group of the provincial administration and the administration of Sihanoukville to assist in the provision of civil registration services, which are in high demand in Sangkat 1 as soon as possible.
The provincial governor added that for any commune / sangkat that has been declared as a judging area, it is necessary to add materials and officials to help complete the work quickly to meet the needs of the people.
He also stated that the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration launched the OWSO mechanism in 29 communes / sangkats throughout Preah Sihanouk Province on August 1, 2022 to address public services to the people. At the grassroots level, with quality, transparency and credibility, reduce time, eliminate corruption and inactivity at the grassroots level. Mr. Seng Teang brings gifts from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to the family of triplets in Svay Rieng province
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Seng Teang, Personal Assistant of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and his wife, on September 28, 2022, brought the charitable donations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to distribute to the people. People who gave birth to triplets are the grandchildren of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit.
Mr. Seng Teang and his wife handed over the gift to the family of three twins at a house in Ang Svay village, Prasot commune, Svay Teap district, Svay Rieng province. The charitable donations include 5 million riels, 50 kilograms of rice, 2 large boxes of milk, 5 kilograms of sugar, 2 sarongs and 2 scarves.
On that occasion, Mr. Seng Teang conveyed the deepest condolences from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to the families who received the triplets, the third family of 390 twins, received gifts from Samdech Techo. And Samdech Kittipritthbandit.
Mr. Seng also stated that Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit always send greetings to people everywhere in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo's personal assistant also said that from 1999 to the present, more than 23 years ago, 390 families gave birth to three or four twin babies and received a lot of donations. Charity from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to help support the difficulties and shortcomings in daily life, especially raising three twins to be the grandchildren of both Samdech after giving birth.
Mr. Seng Teang continued that all these donations are not gifts from the Royal Government, donations from the Cambodian Red Cross or the party that serves political activities, instead, all these gifts are gifts from a sincere heart. With the high consideration of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, who have realized the real difficulties for people who have given birth to three or four twin babies.
The parents of the triplets, Mr. Prum Vichet and Ms. Srey Sina, expressed their deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit for always helping the people in all circumstances. Especially for the suffering people, there is always the presence of both Samdech to intervene at all times and without any discrimination.
