Of the 140 families, 82 live with relatives and many more are staying on boats and some live on the shelves of their homes.
He said that the district authorities, in cooperation with the commune authorities, have prepared many small and large boats waiting to rescue them to safety when the water level rises.
He said that today the water level rose by about 9 stocks and will be able to rise further depending on the weather, however, the authorities have already prepared food tents waiting to receive them at a safe place. Also.
He said that when people can no longer live on the shelves of their homes, the authorities must transport them to safety immediately.
The district governor added that most of the flooded houses were relocated from the floating houses to live on land according to the instructions of the provincial authorities since 2017. Two or three years ago, the water was not as big as this year.
