(Phnom Penh): From Banteay Meanchey province, during the inspection of flood situation and impact, Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management, said that floods caused by rain have affected four provinces. Severe condition. The four provinces are: Banteay Meanchey, Oddar Meanchey, Kampong Thom and Siem Reap.
The senior minister said that Banteay Meanchey province affected 5 cities, 26 communes. Affected 7,491 families, evacuated 297 families to safety. Affected 26,723 hectares of paddy fields and flooded 1,023 hectares of mixed crops. 41 schools and 22 pagodas were flooded.
Oddar Meanchey province affects 4 cities, districts, 8 communes and Sangkats and affects about 520 families. About 97 hectares of rice and 326 hectares of mixed crops were flooded.
Kampong Thom province affected 9 cities and districts, affected about 3,091 families and evacuated about 242 families.
