Commentary: Cyber security protection must not have two standards
BEIJING, Sept. 27 (Xinhua) - China's National Computer Virus Response Center and 360 Technology Co., Ltd. released a second investigation report on the incident of a northwestern Chinese industrial university being attacked online from abroad.
The latest report reveals more important details of more than a thousand cyberattacks on Northwestern industrial universities inspired by the US National Security Agency (NSA) Office of Special Invasion Operations (TAO). Through these details, you can clearly see the path and process of the US National Security Agency (NSA) stealing cyber secrets.
Over the past 10 years, the US National Security Agency (NSA) has launched cyber-attacks on 403 targets in 47 countries and regions, according to a report released by Chinese cyber-enterprises this year. All over the world, including China, Britain, Germany and France. But little is known about how the US National Security Agency (NSA) instigated the cyber-attack.
