(Phnom Penh): His Excellency Yim Nola, Senior Minister in Charge of Special Missions and Chairman of the Economic, Social and Cultural Council, and Lok Chumteav expressed their deepest condolences on the death of Rev. Tun Thi, who is the mother-in-law of His Excellency Deputy Prime Minister. Wednesday, the 3rd day of the month of Assoch in the year of Karl Chatva Sak, BE 2566, which is on September 28, 2022 at 00:18 pm at the age of 90 years old due to old age.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kong Vibol, Deputy Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Taxation, on September 28, 2022, stated that in the first nine months of 2022, the General Department of Taxation collected more than 95 tax revenues. Percentage of the national budget law plan equal to more than $ 2.680 million.
"So far, more than 95 percent of the tax revenue has been collected in the first nine months of 2022, and the General Department of Taxation has three months left to collect the tax," said Kong Vibol.
According to the plan in the national budget law, the General Department of Taxation to collect tax revenue in 2022 amounted to $ 2.8 billion, while in the first nine months of this year, tax collection was more than 95%, equivalent to more than 2,680. Million dollars.
Mr. Kong Vibol stated that the increase in tax revenue collection was due to the reform of the tax system in all areas, including the provision of services to taxpayers, and the provision of good registration services, as well as good audits. Both debt management and resolving issues that make it easier for all taxpayers to pay taxes.
At the same time, Mr. Kong Vibol also encouraged all small businesses to register to pay taxes properly to avoid tax evasion, because when small companies do not pay taxes properly, large companies will be able to There is a problem.
At this point, he said that when small companies do not come to register to pay taxes properly, there will be problems for large companies, especially large companies from abroad who want to invest in Cambodia by both companies. That thinks there is no equality in paying taxes.
He said the General Department of Taxation did not increase tax rates or create new taxes, only provided more tax incentives during Kovid 19, and that some companies did not pay taxes. Although the company has collected value added tax.
It should also be noted that the program on "Fiscal Update and Audit of the American Chamber of Commerce" aims to share important information from the General Department of Taxation to the private sector in order to comply with current regulations and policies of the General Department of Taxation.
Cambodia invites Jamaica to Sea Festival later this year to discuss tourism cooperation
The invitation was made during a bilateral meeting between Mr. Tuk Sokhom, Undersecretary of State for Tourism and Mr. Edmund Bartlett, Minister of Tourism of Jamaica on Tourism Cooperation between the two countries during the Cambodia Expo in Tokyo, Japan on September 23. 2022.
Mr. Thok Sokhom shared his experience in the fight against Kovid-19 in Cambodia, referring to the re-opening of international tourists on March 17, 2022, which Cambodia received a dramatic increase of nearly 1 million international tourists in 8 years. Early 2022 Development and implementation of a framework for the implementation of protocols, mechanisms and mechanisms for the region and subregion, including: ASEAN, Greater Mekong Subregion, ECM CLMV or CLV.
He added that the only way to solve this problem is to strengthen international cooperation and cultivate human resources.
Mr. Tok Sokhom stated that he would apply for permission from Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism of Cambodia.
