Guest Speaker: Representatives from the Ministry of Cults and Religions: Samdech Techo Hun Sen sends condolences to Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly on the death of Rev. Tun Thy
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the afternoon of September 28, 2022, sent a message of condolences to Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly, Chairman of the Council for the Rehabilitation of Agriculture and Rural Development, on the death of Rev. Tun Thi.
Samdech Techo's condolence message reads as follows: "My wife and I have just received the sad news about the death of the senior Buddhist supporter Tun Thi, who is the mother-in-law of His Excellency at 00:18 on Wednesday night. 3 Born in the month of Assoch in the year of Karl Chatva Sak, BE 2566, which is on September 28, 2022 at the age of 90 years old due to old age.
In this sad time, my wife and I would like to express our deepest condolences for the loss of our most cherished mother and grandmother, with deep devotion to all our children, grandchildren and great-grandchildren. The Supreme Master Ching Hai, a Buddhist supporter, has contributed to the support and promotion of Buddhism in the field to this day.
My wife and I would like to dedicate our prayers to the soul of the Supreme Master Ching Hai, the Buddhist supporter Tun Thi, to be born as soon as possible, not to be hungry. ”
