Svay Rieng Provincial Governor Orders 8 Municipalities to Crack Down on All Kinds of Illegal Gambling
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Men Vibol, Governor of Svay Rieng Province and Chairman of the Provincial Unity Command, ordered the 8 municipal administrations to continue to prevent and crack down on all forms of illegal gambling business in their jurisdiction without a license from Royal Government.
Such order by Mr. Men Vibol and Chairman of the Provincial Unity Command in the meeting to review the work results of the third quarter and the work direction of the fourth quarter of 2022 of Svay Rieng Provincial Administration on the morning of September 28, 2022 .
During the meeting, the provincial governor commended and thanked the competent forces, the chairman of the Municipal and District Administrative Unity Command and all relevant authorities for paying attention to strengthening security and safety for the people on the occasion of the festival. Kan Ben and Pchum Ben, especially the participation in dissemination to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and vaccination to local people in the province.
The provincial governor also set out some important directions and points as follows:
* First: Continue to encourage workers who have not been vaccinated to get vaccinated, especially the third dose, fourth dose and fifth dose.
* Second, the Municipal / District Administrative Unity Command must be ready to prepare safe places and prepare all kinds of equipment to evacuate people in the event of natural disasters that may occur, such as floods and rain during the rainy season this year.
* Third: The Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, all municipal authorities must continue to monitor the flood situation due to rain and the impact on people's agricultural products.
* Fourth, the Provincial Department of Agriculture must prepare rice seeds for distribution to families affected by drought and floods.
* Fifth, the district commissioner must inspect the construction of slums without permission and the business of splitting plots, the business of flats for sale must be encouraged to apply for the law in accordance with the law on the management of real estate development business, not allowed to sell before asking The law does not allow it.
* Sixth: Authorities at all levels must strengthen the prevention of drug trafficking, distribution and use at the local level.
* Seventh: Continue to increase the dissemination of road traffic laws and tighten law enforcement, especially the practice of wearing helmets and regularly inspecting trucks carrying workers to prevent possible accidents.
It should be noted that this meeting also reviewed and summarized the results of the implementation of the work of the Provincial Administrative Unity Command for the third quarter of 2022. Police crack down on 4 suspects, confiscate some drugs and 2 firearms in Prek Prosop district, Kratie province
(Kratie): Police in Kratie Province arrested four suspects in connection with drug trafficking and use, as well as confiscated a large amount of drugs, two firearms and some exhibits.
The operation was carried out by the Kratie City Police Inspectorate in collaboration with the Provincial Anti-Drug Bureau and the Prek Prosop District Police Inspectorate under the command of Major General Ou Sobona, Provincial Police Commissioner, with the coordination of Mr. Ky Bunnara, Provincial Prosecutor. In the afternoon of September 27, 2022 in Kampeng village, Prek Prosop commune, Prek Prosop district, Kratie province.
According to the Kratie police report, the four suspects are as follows:
First: Name: Ris, Female, 38 years old, Second: Name: Pei Srey Mom, Female, 50 years old, Third: Name: Ty Kin, Male, 60 years old, All three of them live in Kampeng Village, Prek Prosop Commune, Prek Prosop District, Kratie Province. Name: Mat Spirin, Male, 33 years old, Residence: Toul Cham Village, Prek Prosop Commune, Prek Prosop District, Kratie Province.
The four suspects, along with exhibits, are currently being held in custody at the Kratie City Police Inspectorate to build a case file.
