Citizens continue to steal through wire fences on both sides of the expressway, officials advise to stop activities to avoid punishment according to law
(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Seng Sokong, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Public Works and Transport, this morning, September 28, 2022, led the Ministry's technical officers and representatives of construction companies to inspect and instruct people to stop cutting barbed wire fences. Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway to cross and transport livestock. The senior official warned that if these activities continue, there will be legal challenges.
During the inspection and meeting with the people, Mr. Seng Sokong called on the people to stop this illegal activity immediately.
With the inspection and guidance to the people, Mr. Seng Sokong also met with the construction company to find a suitable solution between the company and the people. According to the official, some residents cut the fence as a gateway to the house on the expressway to let the cattle graze and cut the grass and intend to enter the restricted area surrounded by the fence to gather dangerous All the time.
In the spirit of resolving for the people, the Ministry and the company agreed to facilitate the clearing of existing roads for them and introduced the impact of traffic accidents that could take the lives of them and the road users.
Please be informed that regarding the issue of people cutting the barbed wire on both sides of the expressway, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, also asked Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior to intervene to local authorities to educate people. Stop stealing wire fences on both sides of the expressway to prevent animals from crossing.
Please note that the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway will be free for one month from October 1 to 31, 2022, with a speed limit of 60 km. Up to 120 kilometers per hour.
The Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway has a length of 187.05 km, which started construction on March 22, 2019. This road connects Village 1, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh to Village 1, Sangkat 3, Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province.
The Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway Project is the first expressway project and the most important strategic corridor project in Cambodia, reducing the travel time from Phnom Penh to Sihanoukville Port from five hours to just two hours. Only and help reduce the cost of logistics.
