Chinese Embassy Hosts 100th Anniversary of the Birth of King Norodom Sihanouk
(Phnom Penh): The Chinese Embassy in Cambodia this morning, September 28, 2022, organized the 100th Anniversary of the Birth of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, His Majesty the King Father, Independence, Territorial Integrity and Unity. Khmer nation, His Majesty the King.
The event was held at the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia under the chairmanship of Mr. Wang Winthean, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia and was attended by many distinguished guests.
The program features a documentary video describing the good relations between Cambodia and China under the auspices of His Majesty King Bhumibol Adulyadej after meeting with former Chinese Prime Minister Zhou Enlai at the Ban Dong Conference, as well as gradually building friendships. Between the two countries in the past.
In the video screened on the left, which has the image of Angkor Wat, Khmer, and on the right, the image of the Great Wall of China, also describes the closeness and mutual support between the two countries on the regional stage and The international community, especially the current fight against Kovid 19, is led by Prime Minister Hun Sen and President Xi Jinping.
Mr. Wang Winthean said that the coffin is a beloved character of the Cambodian people and a friend who is loved by the Chinese people. In the past, he bonded a strong bond for the two countries until now, which is as hard as steel, unbreakable.
He also said that today, especially during the 19-year-old Kovid, as a good friend, China has so far provided 42 million doses of Kovid vaccine to Cambodia. Cambodia, through the King and Queen Mother and the Prime Minister, also provided a lot of assistance to China.
Before the end of the program, Mr. Wang Winthean took the guests to visit the Chinese Embassy, especially a park with the inscription "Cambodia-China Friendship Park" and explained the reasons for the park.
Please be informed that Prince Norodom Sihanouk was born on October 31, 1922 in Phnom Penh, Cambodia. He was the eldest son of Samdech Norodom Suramarit and Queen Sisowath Kosama. He was chosen by the French, then a colony of Cambodia, to ascend the throne on April 3, 1941, at the age of 18, after the death of King Monivong.
