US prepares $ 1.1 billion in arms aid to Ukraine
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The United States is preparing a new $ 1.1 billion military aid package for Ukraine to help fight Russia, and may be announced in time, US officials said on Tuesday. Coming soon. This is according to the publication by Reuters on Wednesday, September 28, 2022.
The US official, speaking on condition of anonymity, added that the military package would be announced in the coming days as the latest arms embargo for Ukraine fighting Russian forces in the east.
The new aid package is expected to use funds from the Ukraine Security Assistance Initiative (USAI), which is appropriate for Congress, to allow the Biden administration to buy weapons from US companies rather than from existing US stockpiles. The package will include the HIMARS missile system, accompanied by various types of anti-aircraft, drone and radar systems, as well as spare parts, training and technical assistance.
Since the outbreak of the war, the United States has provided more than $ 15 billion in military aid to Ukraine to fight Russia.
