President of the Court of Appeal and the Attorney General of the Court of Appeal in Phnom Penh chaired a meeting to strengthen law enforcement cooperation between judicial police officers and the court
(Takeo): On the morning of September 28, 2022, Mr. Seng Sivutha, President of the Phnom Penh Court of Appeal, and Mr. Ouk Savuth, Attorney General of the Court of Appeal, presided over a meeting on "Strengthening Law Enforcement Cooperation between Police Officers. Justice and the Court ”at the court and the prosecutor of the Takeo Provincial Court.
Also present were Mr. Chea Chea, Deputy President of the Court of Appeal, Deputy Prosecutor General, Deputy Judge, Advisor and Working Group of the Court of Appeal and the Prosecutor General of the Phnom Penh Court of Appeal, Mr. Aak Phalla, President of Takeo Provincial Court and Mr. Ek Chheang Huot, Prosecutor. First, Takeo Province and Mr. Judge, Deputy Prosecutor, Deputy Secretary of the Court and Prosecutor of Takeo Provincial Court and many other stakeholders.
In this meeting, there are three main objectives: first: to strengthen law enforcement cooperation between the judiciary and the prosecution with judicial police officers, and second: to strengthen the roles and responsibilities of judicial police officers in the suppression of crime and Building a case to the court and third: address the challenges in the implementation of legal procedures.
Speaking at the meeting, Mr. Seng Sivutha stated that in this meeting, due to the peace factor and the situation of Kovid-19 is in a relaxed state, and expressed his appreciation to all judicial police officers and authorities of Takeo Provincial Court who participated. Collaborate to perform the work well and successfully for the nation and the people, especially the people of Takeo province, effectively and responsibly.
He also mentioned the experience in performing the work in the past, both the content of the law, the technique and the attitude of law enforcement. He emphasized that the judiciary and the judiciary are national institutions responsible for the administration of justice and the provision of prompt justice services to the people, based on the principles of the law in force, in order to achieve success and gain the trust and confidence of the people. Law enforcement agencies.
He added that as a law enforcer, "understand, apply, be beneficial to the parties and get justice, if misunderstood, implement wrong, the parties get injustice." At the same time, he also advised all judicial police officers to pay attention to thorough and thorough examination and avoid lack of management during the performance of their duties.
Mr. Seng Sivutha instructed and instructed the Provincial Court and the Takeo Provincial Prosecutor's Office and all judicial police officers in all areas and expertise on five important points, including:
In addition, Mr. Ouk Savuth, Prosecutor General, instructed the judicial authorities and judicial police officers to pay close attention to juvenile cases by complying with child-friendly procedures and in accordance with the law, especially paying attention to repression. On local drug offenses in Takeo province.
During the meeting, the members of the whole meeting raised questions, suggestions and challenges in enforcing the law, and the delegation explained, explained and resolved the whole meeting successfully with the spirit of solidarity and acceptance. High responsibility.
