Japanese PM asks Samdech Techo Hun Sen to support Japanese company doing business in Cambodia while Toyota to set up factory in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): In a meeting with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the morning of September 28, 2022, Mr. Kishida Fumio, Prime Minister of Japan, informed Samdech Techo Hun Sen about the ongoing work to strengthen cooperation. On the economic sector between the two countries.
At the same time, the Prime Minister of Japan also asked Samdech Techo Prime Minister to support Japanese companies to do business in Cambodia, while Japan will soon establish a Toyota plant in Cambodia. This was confirmed by Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister after the meeting.
During the meeting, Mr. Kishida Fumio also raised the issue of bilateral cooperation between Japan and Cambodia, focusing on security.
He also stated that his visit to Cambodia in November 2022 to attend the ASEAN-Japan Summit will continue to strengthen cooperation with Cambodia, especially to show the cooperation between the two countries. To the people of both countries.
The Prime Minister also confirmed that he is looking forward to receiving the visit of the Prime Minister of Japan to Phnom Penh in November to continue the cooperation between the two countries.
Please be informed that as of August 2022, the Council for the Development of Cambodia has approved 149 Japanese investment projects with a total investment capital of approximately $ 2.9 billion.
