The premiere of the song "Life of a Pagoda Boy" will be presided over by Ms. Phoeung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts. The event was also attended by distinguished guests as well as many artists.
The movie "Life of a Pagoda Boy" lasts more than 30 minutes. The movie song "Life of a pagoda boy" reveals the life of Samdech Techo from his childhood, his parents and the village came to send their destiny to the monks in the temple in Phnom Penh for service.
It should be noted that Samdech Techo Hun Sen was born on Tuesday, August 15, 1952 in Peam Koh Sna commune, Stung Trang district, Kampong Cham province.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen grew up and studied in the village district until 1964, living in Wat Neak Voan in Phnom Penh to continue his education at Indra Devi High School when he was only 12 years old.
Twelve-year-olds receive high care from their parents, but due to the lack of schools in the district, their parents are forced to send Hun Bonal (Samdech Techo's birth name) to stay at the pagoda. Phnom Penh to seek knowledge as capital for life.
Life as a poor farmer's son came to study in Phnom Penh, which is full of civilization, making Hun Bonal face many pressures in life, both eating and studying. In addition, Hun Bonal was also insulted by the children of officials and the children of some wealthy people in Phnom Penh. This life experience of being insulted makes Samdech Techo always educate his children to be humble and not to insult the poor.
The song "The Life of a Pagoda Boy", written by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, is a testament to his life of struggle in Samdech's life and also contributes to his success and fame. Today, too. If Samdech did not struggle and overcome all the difficulties in his childhood, then Samdech Techo could not seek knowledge to support his life as famous as it is today.
