The Asian Development Bank (ADB) is ready to provide more financial support to Sri Lanka as the Indian Ocean nation struggles with its worst economic crisis in years. More than seven decades. According to Reuters.
The announcement comes after the ADB reached an agreement this month on $ 200 million in emergency loans to secure food and livelihoods for Sri Lankans after the disaster. Months of major consumer shortages sparked protests that forced the country's president to step down.
