(Kampong Thom): Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, and his team on the afternoon of September 27, 2022, inspected the condition of National Road No. 6, which was affected by floods about 5 km in Stoung district.
During the inspection, the provincial governor urged officials and authorities to pay more attention to the people and infrastructure affected by the floods, and the provincial Department of Public Works and Transport and relevant authorities are clearing the sand to prevent erosion. National Road No. 6 is more than 4 kilometers long.
At the same time, the provincial governor confirmed that the flood has not yet evacuated people to live in a safe place, disrupting the lives and travel and loss of time in the daily business of the people. Only on behalf of the Disaster Management Committee, the class has prepared food to be distributed to the people in the future.
Mr. Nguon Ratanak pointed out that the impact of the current rainy season rice crop is about 8,000 hectares for the second phase of the flood.
Mr. Chou Kolla, Department of Public Works and Transport of Kampong Thom Province, confirmed that the sand dredging to hold the land due to the continuous heavy rainfall could cause the road to be damaged and eroded in the lower part, which is difficult to repair and can reach. Travel when the water recedes.
He said that the section of National Road completely flooded between km 220 to 224, depth 0.20 meters to 0.40 meters, in addition to National Road 6, the Department of Public Works also suspended two other roads: Provincial Road No. 264D Located in Banteay Stong Commune, Stong District and Provincial Road No. 264G in Ta Treal Village, Prolay Commune, Stong District.
