Moscow says it will not seek the extradition of Russians who have fled to neighboring countries to escape conscription.
MOSCOW, Sept. 27 (Xinhua) - Moscow said on Tuesday that it would not ask for the extradition of Russians traveling abroad to escape conscription plans to fight in Ukraine. Thousands of military veterans have crossed into neighboring countries. This is according to the release by AFP on Tuesday, September 27, 2022.
The statement said the Russian Defense Ministry had not sent any request to the Kazakh authorities, Georgia or any other country for the forced repatriation of Russian citizens and did not plan to do so.
Neighbors have seen large numbers of Russians arrive since the draft law was announced last Wednesday. On Tuesday, the Central Asian country Kazakhstan said about 98,000 Russians had entered the country since Wednesday. The Russians also traveled to other neighboring countries, such as Georgia.
