(KPL) The National Assembly of the Republic of Korea (ROK) on Tuesday, September 27, 2022, has ratified a Free Trade Agreement (FTA) with Cambodia, which will enable Cambodia's second bilateral free trade agreement to enter into force. 60 days after the Royal Government of Korea officially notified Cambodia.
Korea also signed a free trade agreement with Cambodia in October 2021.
"The Korean government will notify Israel and Cambodia of the completion of all domestic procedures for the entry into force of the FTA," the Ministry of Commerce, Industry and Energy said in a statement.
The Ministry of Commerce expects a free trade agreement between Cambodia and Korea to further boost Cambodia's exports to Korea, such as garments and textiles, footwear, bags, spare parts, electronics, rubber and agricultural products.
The Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement is Cambodia's second bilateral trade agreement after the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement entered into force in January 2022, simultaneously with the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement. The 15-nation RCEP includes the 10 ASEAN members and five free trade partners: Australia, China, Japan, South Korea and New Zealand.
