In June 2022, the World Bank projected Cambodia's economic growth in 2022 to be 4.5 percent, but has now increased Cambodia's economic growth rate in 2022 to 4.8 percent.
For the Royal Government of Cambodia, for 2022, economic growth is projected to reach around 5.4%, based on the growth of foreign demand and the return of both domestic and foreign investment. Outbreak of Kovid-19 disease.
Growth in East Asia and the Pacific, with the exception of China, is projected to reach 5.3 percent in 2022, up from 2.6 percent year on year, according to the World Bank's East Asia and Pacific Economic Update. 2021.
China, which previously led the region's economic recovery, is projected to grow only 2.8 percent, down sharply from 8.1 percent in 2021.
"The economy is recovering in most of the countries in East Asia and the Pacific," said Manuel Lafero, World Bank Vice President for East Asia and the Pacific.
"Along with preparing for the global economic downturn, regional countries should also look at domestic intervention policies that hinder long-term development," she said.
According to the report, growth in East Asia and the Pacific was largely driven by a recovery in domestic demand following the easing of restrictions on Kovid-19 and on export growth.
