Wang Yi, a member of the State Council and Minister of Foreign Affairs of China, announced that China has launched a domestic legal agenda to adopt the "gun protocol".
BEIJING, Sept. 24 (Xinhua) - Chinese Foreign Ministry Spokeswoman Jiang Yu's Regular Press Conference on September 24, 2013 China has launched a domestic legal agenda to ratify the "gun protocol".
This is an important step that China has taken to actively implement global security initiatives and safeguard international and regional peace and stability, demonstrating China's commitment to supporting multilateralism and implementing its vision of a common destiny. Humanity.
The purpose of the "Gun Protocol" is to establish international standards for the production, export, import, and control of firearms, in order to promote and enhance international cooperation in the suppression of organized transnational crime.
