Abe Shinzo, 67, was shot dead by a 41-year-old gunman on July 8 while participating in an election campaign in Nara, Japan.
Mr. Abe is a longtime good friend of Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Cambodia. During his tenure as Prime Minister, Abe worked closely with the Royal Government of Cambodia to strengthen bilateral relations between Cambodia and Japan, including upgrading bilateral cooperation to a strategic partnership in 2013. .
Abe is widely recognized and praised for his ability to drive Japan's progress and its active contribution to peace, stability and prosperity in the region and the world.
Abe's death has left the Cambodian leadership and people deeply saddened.
Samdech Techo considers Abe's death to be the loss of a friend who used to help Cambodia in difficult times.
In a condolence letter issued shortly after Abe's death, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed deep shock and grief over Abe Shinzo's death. Samdech Techo expressed his deepest condolences.
He emphasized that Abe was a prominent Japanese statesman who was widely recognized and praised for his leadership in advancing Japan and its active contribution to the nation. Peace, stability and prosperity in the region and the world.
