The meeting was attended by ministers and leaders in charge of tourism of the G20 countries, 24 guest countries, as well as nine relevant international organizations and communities, including the World Tourism Organization (UNWTO). Development partners and some of the largest international organizations in the world.
In his speech, the Minister shared his experience of the Royal Government of Cambodia's tourism restoration efforts and highlighted some of the priorities for the restoration of the ASEAN tourism sector, which was set out by the ASEAN Tourism Ministers Meeting led by Cambodia during the ASEAN Tourism Forum 2022 (ATF2022). ) In Sihanoukville, in which the Minister raised and highlighted:
First: The Cambodian experience
1. For more than two years now, the Royal Government of Cambodia, under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, has been working to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and effectively address the impact by enacting health and administrative rules. Economic and social interventions in a proactive spirit.
2. The Prime Minister's determination to make vaccination a key strategy has made Cambodia one of the countries with the highest vaccination coverage rates in the world and has gained community immunity. The basis for reopening the country since the end of 2021 has been the reopening of economic and social activities, including the opening of international tourists and other fully vaccinated travelers.
3. Currently, Cambodia is actively and successfully implementing the roadmap on the restoration of tourism in Cambodia 2020-2025, which has 3 stages:
Second: ASEAN Tourism
2. The Minister stressed that ASEAN is actively implementing the ASEAN Tourism Restoration Plan after the Kovid 19 Crisis, which was launched in 2021.
3. ASEAN is developing the ASEAN Framework for Sustainable Tourism Development after Kovid 19 to develop the ASEAN region as a leading sustainable tourism destination.
5. ASEAN prioritizes hygiene and safety, and in early 2022, the ASEAN Tourism Ministers' Meeting in Sihanoukville adopted the ASEAN Guidelines on Hygiene and Safety in Tourism Services, accompanied by the implementation of the ASEAN Safety Travel Label "Safety and Security". "Safe and Warm."
Minister Thong Khon requested the G20 countries and development partners to support and cooperate with ASEAN to help develop ASEAN tourism in line with the above priorities.
The Minister also invited a delegation to the G20 Tourism Ministerial Meeting to visit Cambodia and the 2023 SEA Games in Cambodia.
It should also be noted that tourism is considered by the G20 countries and major world organizations as a priority sector to be included in the national and global development agenda in the context of post-19 crisis recovery.
