Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructs the Minister of Health to work with Cuba to examine the possibility of importing or producing vaccines against cancer and diabetes (Video inside) (Havana, Cuba): During an official visit to Cuba, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia. Take a visit to the Center for Genetic Engineering and Biotechnology, an institute founded by former Cuban President Fidel Castro.
The institute's administrator informed Samdech Techo that Fidel Castro had worked hard to establish the center to help Cuban intellectuals conduct scientific research in the fields of agriculture, health and capacity development.
Cuba is the largest island nation in the Caribbean and is a key part of the Gulf of Mexico, the perfect geographical and strategic location for connecting Central America, South America and the Caribbean to the United States. America.
Cuba has abundant natural resources, lasting peace, and almost complete physical infrastructure left by the Spanish colonies and pre-revolutionary governments, and has a reputation for exporting sugar, a record high in the Human Development Index. To export human resources and so on.
Fidel Castro established the Center for Genetic Engineering and Biotechnology to increase research and contribute to the further development of Cuba. The center has grown in quality in science, engineering, genetics and biotechnology, especially in the field of health research through the development of vaccines against cancer, diabetes, and measles 19.
After listening, the Prime Minister assigned Mr. Mam Bunheng to work with this center to cooperate on the import or production of cancer and diabetes vaccines to Cambodia, because Cambodia has a high birth rate. Both of these diseases are high.
The leadership of the Institute has accepted Samdech Techo's request and will continue to cooperate with the Ministry of Health of Cambodia.
It should be noted that during Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit to Cuba, the two countries have signed a memorandum of understanding between the Ministry of Health of Cambodia and Cuba to cooperate in the field of health.
