Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister accompanying the Prime Minister, said that during this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded of the good relations between the two countries, especially after the revolution of Cuba, and this relationship began especially between former President Fidel Castro. And former King Samdech Norodom Sihanouk, the King.
The Cuban President stressed that Cambodia and Cuba support the pursuit of peace as well as justice in the world, which is the basis of Cuba-Cambodia relations. The President of Cuba acknowledged and praised the courage of the Cambodian People's Party, as well as the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia in the fight to defend Cambodia's independence and sovereignty.
The President said that the Prime Minister's visit to Cuba was at a time of economic turmoil, but it was a good sign of friendship and solidarity. The visit of Samdech Techo Prime Minister reflects the historical significance of the relationship between the two countries.
The President considered the visit of Samdech Techo Prime Minister as an important witness of the further strengthening of bilateral relations, reflecting the strong ties between the two countries, while the Prime Minister of Cuba will visit Cambodia in the near future. This.
The two countries will have a number of agreements on health, education and exchanges, training, experience of diplomats, and other areas that we can expand, he said.
The President also thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for supporting the fight against all injustices that countries can do to Cuba. Not only do we recognize Cambodia's role as chair of ASEAN this year, but we also recognize Cambodia's support for Cuba's regional and international integration.
The President added that Cuba is very pleased with Samdech Techo's current visit to Cuba, as it has helped to improve relations between the two countries, as well as the people of the two countries.
In response, Samdech Techo Prime Minister thanked the President for the warm welcome to Samdech and the delegation. Samdech Techo stated that Samdech really respects what the President said, especially regarding the friendship between the two countries.
The Prime Minister said that Cambodia and Cuba are geographically far apart, but it is not an obstacle for Samdech's visit to Cuba, nor is it an obstacle for the Cuban Prime Minister to visit Cambodia. .
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that Cambodia and Cuba will remember the work they have done together for a long time. Especially helping each other in 1979, 43 years ago. Samdech Techo underlined that at that time, Samdech paid a visit to Cuba, when he was the Minister of Foreign Affairs to organize the visit of the Head of State of Cambodia to attend the Non-Aligned Movement meeting.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that without the help of Mr. Fidel Castro, the Cambodian seat in this non-aligned movement is the same as the situation at the United Nations, but with the help of HE Fidel Castro, the Cambodian seat in Non-aligned movement must be left vacant.
The Prime Minister also said that he regretted that he did not visit HE Fidel Castro when he fell ill and died.
The Prime Minister also said that the relationship between Samdech and Fidel Castro seems like a father and son. At this time, Samdech has many memories, especially the relationship between Samdech and Mr. Fidel Castro, which has been negotiated and discussed a lot.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen says that the Cambodian people have not forgotten what Cuba did to help Cambodia during the difficult times after the liberation from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
Samdech Techo stated that at that time, Cuba helped Cambodia in the fight against imperialism and the Khmer Rouge genocidal regime. Samdech Techo reminded that in 1979, Cuba helped Cambodia a lot and still remember that at that time Cambodia had Cuba sugar, Cuban orphanage and also Cuban ferry.
Regarding diplomatic cooperation, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that he would like to see the promotion of diplomatic consultations between the two countries.
The Prime Minister also raised the issue of sanctions on Cuba. Samdech Techo confirmed that Cambodia has also experienced foreign sanctions. In the past as well as now, some countries have imposed sanctions on Cambodia as well as individuals and companies in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo highlighted that the use of sanctions is currently a hot topic. In the aftermath of the war in Ukraine, sanctions against Russia from the United States and the European Union affected not only Russia but also many countries not involved in the war.
He stressed that the unilateral sanctions have pushed up energy prices, high inflation and affected many countries in the world.
Regarding ASEAN affairs, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that Cuba has some friends who are members of ASEAN, such as Cambodia, Laos and Vietnam. Therefore, Cuba can work with ASEAN by sector according to this part of the cooperation.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that Cuba has already been a party to the Southeast Asia Cooperation Treaty, so what Cuba is interested in will make ASEAN more valuable.
Finally, Samdech Techo Prime Minister brought greetings and wishes from the King of Cambodia and invited His Excellency the President to visit Cambodia at any convenient time.
The President of Cuba considered Samdech Techo a close friend and thanked him for his remarks. What Samdech mentioned reflects the history of the friendship between the two countries and also reflects the Samdech's recent visit.
The President also highlighted his commitment to strengthening relations and cooperation in various fields with Cambodia by continuing to promote common interests in the international arena. He emphasized that Cuba and Cambodia will continue to work on technical as well as mutually beneficial fields.
The President also thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for his visit to Cuba to strengthen ties and cooperation between the two countries.
