Samdech Techo Hun Sen Celebrates the 29th Anniversary of the Promulgation of the National Constitution
Samdech Techo stated that starting from the Paris Peace Agreement of October 23, 1991 on a joint solution to end the historical crisis in Cambodia, which then on May 23-28, our country held elections again. First, under the auspices of the United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization (UNTAC). After the election, the national constitution was also made in history in 1993.
On September 24, 1993, in the Great Temple of Deva Vinich in the Royal Palace, His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, the former King Father of the Royal Coffin, he signed the Royal Decree promulgating the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Official.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated, "September 24 is the birthday of the 1993 Constitution, which in 2022 is the 29-year-old Constitution of Cambodia." The Constitution is the supreme law of the Kingdom of Cambodia. ”
Samdech Techo further stated that all laws and decisions of state institutions must be in accordance with the Constitution. He added that some of the most important points clearly stated in the Constitution are as follows: "Cambodia must strictly abide by the constitutional monarchy, liberal democracy and pluralism."
The Cambodian Constitution stipulates the principle of separation of powers: 1: the legislature, 2: the executive, 3: the judiciary, and also adopts the fundamental rights of the people and the rule of law.
