Pakistani PM thanks Samdech Techo and Cambodian people for flood relief
On that occasion, in addition to the cordial greetings, the Prime Minister of Pakistan also thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Cambodian people for their financial support to Pakistan during the floods.
It should be noted that the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia donated about 50,000 US dollars on September 5 to help solve the difficulties of Pakistan, which suffered severe floods.
Timor-Leste President thanks Samdech Techo Hun Sen for helping Timor-Leste become a member of ASEAN
While on a working mission in New York, USA on September 23, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Ramos Horta met to discuss a number of issues. In particular, strengthening relations and cooperation in various fields between the two countries.
In this meeting, Samdech Techo and the President of East Timor all expressed their pleasure to meet again. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also congratulated Ramos Horta on his election victory.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also raised the issue of Timor-Leste's application for ASEAN membership. The Prime Minister emphasized that in the past 10 years, since Cambodia chaired ASEAN in 2012, Samdech has worked hard to promote Timor-Leste to become a member of ASEAN. So far, Samdech Techo hopes that there will be support for East Timor to join ASEAN, which can be announced by the end of 2022 and will become a full member in 2023.
The news made the President of East Timor and his delegation very excited and thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for his efforts to facilitate Timor-Leste's ASEAN membership. Mr. Ramos Horta said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen is like the owner of East Timor.
In addition to the above issues, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Ramos Horta also discussed the strengthening of trade and investment between the two countries.
The East Timorese president expressed hope that relations and trade between East Timor and Cambodia would improve. The president also stressed that he would look into importing more goods from Cambodia.
The President also expressed hope that during his visit to Cambodia in the third week of October, he would work to improve trade, agriculture and other sectors.
In response, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that the Cambodia-Timorese bilateral relations have improved due to mutual trust. The Prime Minister stressed that economic relations between the two countries are still limited, but Cambodia and Timor-Leste still hope to expand.
Regarding this trade, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also mentioned the free trade agreement that Cambodia is making with China and South Korea. In this regard, Samdech Techo wants Cambodia and East Timor to examine the possibility of free trade together to expand trade and investment.
In this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Ramos Horta also discussed the opening of direct flights between the two countries to facilitate trade and investment relations.
