Samdech Techo Hun Sen: The Threat to Humanity: Vulnerability to Climate Change (Video inside) (United States): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the night of September 23, 2022 The threat to humanity is the vulnerability to climate change, with the need to change the process of tackling climate change now, without waiting for tomorrow.
This statement was made on the occasion of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech at the 77th United Nations General Assembly in New York, USA on the night of September 23, 2022 (Cambodian time).
"The threat to humanity is our vulnerability to climate change," he said. "We need to change the process of dealing with the weather now, not waiting for tomorrow."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that for the past 50 years, the government has been warned to change our production and consumption patterns to avoid this disaster. But unfortunately since then we have only seen more biodiversity loss, more soil degradation and more fresh water scarcity.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that our joint actions must focus on global efforts to avoid impacts to promote climate resilient development.
In addition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that our commitment to bring global temperatures down to 1.5 degrees Celsius requires financing and technology transfer to facilitate meaningful change in efforts to avoid And adapt.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that we need to pay more attention to digital policies with an environment and a favorable regulatory framework that leads to more investment in digital infrastructure because it is important for Connect the growing digital gap and create new sources of growth.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that the promotion of green economic development is an indispensable part of supporting sustainable socio-economic development through the expansion of cooperation in building green infrastructure, promoting energy transition and The use of green technology.
The 77th Session of the General Assembly of the United Nations General Assembly was held under the theme "The turning point of irreversible change: revolutionary solutions to interconnected cell problems". Along with the key points, the issue of Myanmar was also raised by the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
"Indeed, the situation in Myanmar is alarming, which could have a direct impact on the security and stability of the region as a whole, but we must recognize that this crisis is complex," he said. "With a deeply rooted cause."
Please be informed that the Royal Government of Cambodia has always informed the world of its efforts as the ASEAN Chair to help Myanmar return to normalcy through the implementation of the ASEAN Five-Point Agreement and the challenges that Cambodia encounters.
Fifth, the special envoy and delegation will visit Myanmar to meet with all stakeholders.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen Informs the United Nations General Assembly of Cambodia's Success in Combating Kovid 19 and Thanks to All Friends for Providing Vaccines (Video inside) (United States): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia Tell the UN General Assembly about Cambodia's success in the fight against Kovid 19 and thank all friendly countries for providing the vaccine.
"Over the past two years, the Royal Government of Cambodia has made proactive efforts to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 by introducing health measures, social and economic interventions, and Administrative measures. "The government has identified the Kovid-19 vaccine as a key strategic measure."
"As a result, Cambodia has become one of the countries with the highest global population coverage of Kovid-19 vaccine, especially the achievement of strong" community immunity, "he said. And be able to fully reopen the country by the end of 2021, as well as restore all socio-economic activities in a new normal trajectory.
He expressed his sincere gratitude to all our friendly countries for providing Kovid-19 vaccine to Cambodia through bilateral and multilateral frameworks.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also thanked all friendly countries for providing Kovid-19 vaccine to Cambodia through bilateral and multilateral frameworks.
The Prime Minister stated that over the past two years, the Royal Government of Cambodia has made proactive efforts to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 by introducing health measures, social and economic interventions and administrative measures. And the Royal Government of Cambodia has identified the Kovid-19 vaccine as a key strategic measure.
Countries that supply vaccine assistance to Cambodia include: China, Japan, the United States, the United Kingdom, Australia, Poland, the Netherlands, Hungary, Italy, and Spain. As of August 18, 2022, Cambodia has received a total of 74 million doses of vaccine.
