About 500 families affected by floods in two provinces evacuated
(Oddar Meanchey): At least 500 families in Banteay Meanchey and Oddar Meanchey provinces have been evacuated due to floods.
After conducting flood inspections in three provinces: Siem Reap, Oddar Meanchey and Banteay Meanchey, Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management on September 23, 2022, said that after the forecast According to the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, five provinces were affected by the floods, including Kampong Thom, Preah Vihear, Siem Reap, Oddar Meanchey and Banteay Meanchey.
Senior Minister Kun Kim said that out of the five provinces, the situation in Kampong Thom and Preah Vihear provinces has been declining and flowing into the Tonle Sap Lake, but the other three provinces have been affected by infrastructure and people's homes.
At the same time, the Senior Minister stated that on behalf of the staff of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister and Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, led a professional officer to directly inspect the difficulties, damage or evacuation of people to safety. In fact, only two provinces were evacuated: Oddar Meanchey and Banteay Meanchey, with more than 200 families evacuated from each province.
Senior Minister Kun Kim calls on the people in the inspected provinces to pay close attention and vigilance, especially to request the Department of Water Resources to immediately inform the people before opening their sluice gates as this problem may cause Sink in the shortest possible time.
He added that although the circumstances were not serious, the National Committee for Disaster Management was ready with all 16 disaster search and rescue units to respond to possible incidents, especially floods. The rain that Cambodia always faces every year.
In addition, the Senior Minister instructed all Capital-Provincial Disaster Management Secretaries to pay close attention to this situation and to immediately report to the Disaster Relief Force in case of intervention beyond its capacity to ensure Rescue people in time.
Minister Thong Khon Instructs Tourism Department to Prevent Gambling in Tourism Business
(Phnom Penh): In order to join the Royal Government in preventing gambling activities throughout the country, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, announced the directors of the 25 capital-provincial tourism departments to cooperate in preventing gambling activities in tourism businesses within their jurisdiction. Its to revive.
