On the morning of September 23, 2022, Mr. Khleang Huot, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, who was in charge of direct operation in Tuol Kork district to inspect the pawnshops suspected of receiving illegal pawns, returned 8 motorbikes to the original owners after checking the documents. See, they are the real owners.
According to the interrogation of the victims who came to pick up the motorcycles, it is said that some of them lost their motorcycles for up to 5 years and suddenly found them at an illegal pawn shop which the police confiscated. They expressed great joy after a long despair in finding their motorcycle that had been stolen or robbed in the past.
Through this case, the authorities appealed to people who have lost their motorcycles do not despair and must continue to verify the identity of their motorcycles when the authorities advertise because they may not find their motorcycles.
It should be informed that in the operation to check the location of the suspected illegal pawn, the police found more than 1,000 motorcycles without proper documents and took them to save to find the owner.
