(Phnom Penh): The National Social Security Fund cooperates with the Khmer Nationality Identity Card Department of the General Department of Identification to facilitate the continuation of the inspection, settlement and issuance of Khmer Nationality Identity Cards for workers and members of the Khmer National Union who do not have a Khmer Nationality identity card in Cambodia. The base of Svay Rieng province lasts for 2 days from September 22-23, 2022.
Lt. Gen. Sok Prang, Deputy Director of the Khmer Nationality Identity Card Department, told Fresh News this morning, September 23, 2022, that in collaboration with the National Social Security Fund, he led the working group of the Department of Expertise. Facilitate the settlement and issuance of Khmer identity cards to workers from other provinces to work in factories in Svay Rieng province.
According to Major General Sok Prang, the legal requirement for those who need to obtain a Cambodian identity card is to have relevant documents and go to work in his hometown, but to facilitate this work, the Department of Cambodian Nationality Identity Arrive at the location of the factory where they are working to alleviate difficulties.
The Deputy Director of the Khmer Nationality Identity Card Department, who led the intervention team to carry out this work directly, claimed that during one day yesterday, September 22, 2022, the working group issued ID cards to the workers of the members. More than 100 people and will continue on September 23 for another day.
Please be informed that the issuance of Khmer identity card does not require people to pay the service fee.
Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin calls on the authorities to facilitate and facilitate the people on the occasion of Pchum Ben and various trips
(Tbong Khmum): Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, called on the authorities everywhere to facilitate and facilitate the people on the occasion of Kan Ben and Pchum Ben, as well as family reunions. Original.
Such an appeal by Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin was made on the occasion that Samdech, along with his sons, daughters, grandsons, granddaughters, members of the National Assembly, leaders, government officials and Buddhists at the foot of the pagoda, celebrated the 13th Kan Ben at Wat Thkov in Ponhea Krek district, Tbong Khmum province, on the morning of September 23, 2022, according to the Buddhist tradition.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin and all Buddhists offered candles, incense and flowers to Preah Rattanatray, counted the number of bowls, and brought gifts, food, drink, and offerings to the monks to dedicate the merits to the ancestors. The ancestors and relatives of the seven clans and dignitaries, heroes, warriors who sacrificed their lives for the cause of the nation and the people, may all their souls go to death.
Pchum Ben is one of the largest festivals of all time for Buddhists. Every year, when the day of Pchum Ben is celebrated, all relatives, whether near or far, always go to meet, especially the parents in the hometown to prepare food and soup to give. The monks who live in the pagoda. These are the habits that Cambodians have been doing for a long time.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin wished all the people happiness and prosperity to every family. All travel near and far on the occasion of Pchum Ben is safe, respecting all traffic laws and being neutral to each other.
