The Secretary-General of the United Nations expressed his pleasure at a working meeting with Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the United Nations Headquarters in New York on September 22, 2022.
Antonio Guterres praised Cambodia's commitment to this peacekeeping mission, and he was pleased with Cambodia's past activities.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen is the Cambodian leader who decided to send Cambodian forces to peacekeeping operations under the United Nations umbrella in 2006. Samdech Techo once emphasized that the decision at that time was the most difficult decision because it would face many responsibilities if the decision led to danger for the forces.
It should be noted that in the above meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Secretary-General of the United Nations discussed a number of other issues as well.
