He added that this is another historic achievement of the Cambodia-UN Joint Court and a historic day for the Cambodian people, especially the victims of the Khmer Rouge regime, who received a new verdict and a day. History for the international justice system as well. UNDP Governor Delighted in Progress in Cambodia and Pledges to Continue Supporting Cambodia's Development
The UNDP Governor expressed his appreciation for Cambodia's progress as well as his continued support for Cambodia's development work during a working meeting with Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the United Nations Headquarters in Phnom Penh. New York, USA on September 22.
UNDP is one of Cambodia's key development partners. Through development programs, UNDP has contributed much to support the development of human resources, the economy and many other sectors.
Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, said that in the above meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked UNDP as well as other UN agencies that have supported Cambodia, especially the policy to promote development goals. Millennium and the Sustainable Development Goals.
In particular, Mr. Achim Steiner said that he closely monitored the development of Cambodia. He has clearly seen the development and progress in Cambodia so far, and UNDP continues to support Cambodia, especially on development.
During this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen outlined some priority tasks that require the necessary support from UNDP. That includes demining as Cambodia pushes for a Cambodian mine-free policy by 2025 and climate change as Cambodia chairs ASEAN to launch the ASEAN Green Agreement.
In response to Samdech Techo's request, Mr. Achim Steiner stated that he fully agreed with Samdech Techo's statement. He also stressed that UNDP will continue to assist developing countries, especially in the area of finance, and promote strategies to attract maximum investment. Regarding demining and unexploded ordnance, UNDP is pleased to have partnered with Cambodia to address mine action in Cambodia.
Regarding the ASEAN Green Agreement, the UNDP Governor said that for developing countries, this work is not an obstacle, but work must pay special attention in the ASEAN region.
He stressed that the green policy, what needs to be done is to promote how the green economy is the key to the overall economic framework. On that occasion, Mr. Achim Steiner also highlighted that UNDP has experience as well as working with many countries around the world, so this wise and effective policy is to promote this work together.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen invited the UNDP Governor to visit Cambodia at any convenient time. Chbar Morn City Administration Continues to Crack Down on Online Cockfighting Locations, Detains 2 Owners and Seizes Some Materials
