(Kiev): Officials in four regions under the control of the Russian army in eastern and southern Ukraine on Tuesday announced that they will hold a referendum to Become part of Russia in the face of strong condemnation from Ukraine and the West.
But why is Russia rushing to hold a "referendum on swallowing up Ukrainian territory"? Russia has not yet been able to fully control the four areas, with the Russian army controlling 60 percent of the Donetsk region.
* Intention to escalate the war? Call for a referendum by officials in four regions under Russian control in eastern and southern Ukraine Russia has suffered heavy casualties in the Khartoum region, which has drawn criticism from local nationalists in recent weeks.
Moreover, signs that Putin wants to escalate the war in Ukraine became clearer after Russia's parliament on Tuesday passed a new law that would criminalize defectors. Defeat or refuse to comply with orders during conscription and the imposition of martial law. The new law has led to speculation that Putin could declare war on Ukraine and deploy troops across the country if he wishes.
At the same time, the Russian president reiterated his commitment to nuclear weapons, saying that Russia was ready to use all means possible in the event of a threat to Russia's territorial integrity. Putin also expressed support for plans for a referendum on Russian-occupied territories in eastern and southern Ukraine.
