The following is the announcement of Phnom Penh Capital Administration: Samdech Techo Hun Sen attended the statement of the Head of State and Head of Government at the 77th General Assembly of the United Nations
On September 22, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, attended the 77th General Assembly of the United Nations General Assembly.
Phnom Penh is now declared a demining city, Phnom Penh has 126 minefields and a total of 204 victims.
(Phnom Penh): Under the correct and skillful leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the Mine Authority, Samdech has paid close attention to demining to prevent further threats to human life, as well as Bringing peace to the whole country On the afternoon of September 22, 2022, Phnom Penh was officially declared as a demining city.
The announcement ceremony was presided over by Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, and attended by Mr. Ly Thuch, Senior Minister, First Vice President of the Cambodian Mine Action Management Authority. Mr. Mean Chanyada, Deputy Governor, Representative of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, including many other stakeholders.
Ms. Kittisangha Bandith stated that Phnom Penh, 43 years ago, was full of pain by going through the war and becoming a ghost town born from the devastation of the war, leaving desolation, orphans, loneliness and ruin. It went through many stages until it was developed as it is today and was nicknamed the Mineless City.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch also said that the threat of landmines and unexploded ordnance was complex and left a lot of grief for the people and hindered further development activities. Mine to be completed by 2025 according to the high recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
People start to rush out of Phnom Penh to the provinces, authorities and authorities together to facilitate traffic for people at Chroy Changvar Bridge
