On behalf of Mr. Chea Khema, Daun Penh District Governor, Mr. Chap Dina would like to thank all the police forces who worked hard almost 24 hours a day without fear of fatigue.
UNICEF vows to work with the Cambodian government to increase funding for sub-national administrations and build the capacity of local officials
This statement was made by Ms. Ferguson Youssef during her participation in the awarding ceremony of the Social Services Award for Sub-National Administration for 2020-21 under the chairmanship of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Acting Prime Minister of Cambodia, in the afternoon. September 22, 2022 at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
At the same time, Ms. Froof Yuzit expressed her satisfaction with the results of the joint efforts between UNICEF and the Ministry of Interior, the average budget analysis for social services at the capital-provincial level from 2020 to 2022 is about 10%. Of the development budget, which increased by 3% in 2017.
She also praised the initiative to increase the capital-provincial budget allocation for social services to 10 percent from the 5 percent rate set in 2018 by the Ministry of Interior in consultation with the Ministry of Economy. And finance. It is hoped that further discussions between the two ministries will reach an agreement on a 20 percent budget for development at the commune level soon.
"We are committed to working with the Ministry of Interior to continue advocating for increased funding for sub-national administrations, contributing to capacity building at all levels, particularly "On the need and capacity gap at the municipal, district, Khan and commune levels."
Ms. Frogoff Youssef added that UNICEF has a long history of cooperation with the Royal Government of Cambodia in all fields, including supporting decentralization and deconcentration and public financial reform. She was pleased to know that the contribution of the budget for social services to the sub-national level has increased.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng thanked UNICEF for supporting the project to provide social services at the sub-national level with equality, environment and equity. Decentralization and deconcentration reforms in Cambodia have been supported by the public from all walks of life and are also providing significant benefits to economic and social development.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng agreed with the Director-General of UNICEF regarding the budget analysis to the sub-national administration, adding that despite the impact caused by Kovid 19, the Royal Government did not withdraw in the reform and Sub-national administrative support as well.
At the same time, Samdech Krala Hom stressed that "the main issue is the will of the sub-national administration to perform its duties responsibly. In the past, the health sector and some other sectors have also been transferred to the sub-national administration, and we recognize that if the transfer of authority to the health sector is not timely, the fight against Kovid 19 disease of the provincial administration will surely meet. "It will be difficult."
According to Mr. Prak Sam Oeun, Director General of the General Department of Administration of the Ministry of Interior, the social service award program for sub-national administration is divided into two categories: social service star award with 3 stars, 2 stars, 1 star and zero star. And Social Services Championship, 1st and 2nd place for Capital, Province, 1st, 2nd and 3rd for Municipal, District and Khan Administration and 1st to 5th for Commune / Sangkat Government.
Telecom regulator of Cambodia advises to stop providing additional services to consumers in the form of "loan scheme"
(Phnom Penh): The Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia (TCC) has issued a statement stating that based on the letter No. 809 of the Royal Government of Cambodia dated September 22, 2022 of the Office of the Council of Ministers of the Royal Government. In principle, all mobile service providers in the Kingdom of Cambodia are required to stop providing additional services to consumers in the form of "loan plans".
For the loan scheme that users are already connected to, all mobile service providers must continue to validate until the users run out of the amount borrowed, set October 19, 2022 as the date. Finally.
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian and Vietnamese sides agreed to further strengthen cooperation in the field of employment and vocational training.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng hopes that during the tenure of Mr. Nguyen Huay Tang's mission, the relationship between the two countries will further develop cooperation in all fields, especially in the field of employment and vocational training.
The Ambassador replied that he would continue to work more closely on employment and vocational training with Cambodia.
At the same time, the Ambassador also invited Minister Ith Sam Heng to lead a delegation to visit Vietnam in the near future to strengthen cooperation in the field of employment and vocational training of the two countries to grow.
Minister Ith Sam Heng has confirmed that he will lead a delegation to visit Vietnam later this year. He said he would send a technical team to review the progress of the implementation of the Memorandum of Understanding, share best practices and discuss challenges with the Vietnamese Ministry of Labor, Disability and Social Affairs.
It should be noted that on March 21, 2017, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training of Cambodia and the Ministry of Labor, Disability and Social Affairs of Vietnam signed a Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation in the field of labor for a period of 5 years.
The issue of Jerusalem is the source of a long-running conflict between Israel and Palestine that both sides see as their capital. Israel occupied East Jerusalem in 1967 and annexed it in 1980.
Most countries have chosen to locate their embassies in Israel in Tel Aviv until a two-state solution is reached.
But in 2017, former US President Donald Trump broke with tradition by announcing that Washington would move its embassy to Jerusalem, much to the chagrin of the Palestinian people. The United Kingdom is one of 128 countries that have voted to condemn US action in the UN resolution.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth brings alms and suffixes to monks at 2 pagodas in Ou Raing Ov district, Tbong Khmum province on the occasion of the 12th Ben
(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group on Oreang District, Tbong Khmum Province, on September 22, 2022, led the Royal Government Working Group on Oreang Ov District, together with local government officials. And the people participated in the 12th Ben at Wat Preah Theat Basrey and Wat Mean, Ou Raing Ov District, Tbong Khmum Province.
Please note that Wat Preah Theat Basrey is located in Preah Theat Thmor Da Village, Preah Theat Commune, Ou Raing Ov District, Tbong Khmum Province. The location of the temple of Preah Theat Basrey or the temple of Preah Theat Preah Srey is probably in the style of Koh Ker in the 10th century.
On either side of the entrance to Wat Preah Theat, there are two later temple foundations built of laterite on the right hand side, called Vihear Kuh temple, on the left hand side, called Prasat Preah Chol Nirvana, and other temple foundations north of the pagoda. Today, all the foundations of the temple have been torn down and some new construction has been completed.
