(Phnom Penh): EU Ambassador to Cambodia Carmen Moreno has said that investing in education is the most powerful investment that any country can make to promote economic growth and employment, as well as opportunities in the 21st century. 21 and digital transformation have given us the need to revolutionize education, focusing on quality and equity, and the adoption of digital tools.
Ms. Carmen Moreno said this on September 21, 2022, as the EU Delegation to Cambodia, together with the Embassies of the Czech Republic, France, Germany, Hungary and Poland, organized the first European Scholarship Fair - Opportunity Higher education in Europe for young Cambodians who wish to pursue higher education in Europe and seek scholarships.
The event is also organized to celebrate Cambodian academic staff and students who have received scholarships under the EU's "Erasmus +" program. In the last three years, the EU has provided scholarships to partner students and higher education staff. Nearly 200 in Cambodia to pursue a bachelor's or master's degree, or to provide teaching and training at European universities.
Dr. Som Ratana, Undersecretary of State for the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, said that scholarships to study in Europe, funded by the EU Erasmus + program or by generous bilateral programs of EU member states, are a great support. To increase the knowledge of Cambodian graduates so that the country can benefit from ASEAN integration and the fourth generation industrial revolution.
(Colombo): Consumer prices in Sri Lanka soared to 70.2 percent in August as the island nation continues to be in its worst economic crisis in decades. . According to Reuters.
The National Consumer Price Index (NCPI) rose 70.2 percent last month from a year earlier, Reuters reported citing data released by the Sri Lankan Census and Statistics Department on Wednesday. An increase of 66.7 percent in July.
Food prices rose 84.6 percent, while non-food items rose 57.1 percent.
The Central Bank of Sri Lanka (CBSL) said in August that inflation would fall again after reaching a peak of about 70 percent as the country's economy slumped.
Sri Lanka's economy contracted 8.4 percent in the second quarter from a year earlier, the biggest quarter-on-quarter decline in fertilizer and fuel shortages.
ADB lowers China's growth forecast, lowers outlook for Asia
The Asian Development Bank (ADB) has cut its growth forecast for China and downgraded its outlook for developing Asia amid rising interest rates, a protracted war in Ukraine and its bases. Beijing's Kuwait Zero Politics. According to Bloomberg News.
The occasional recurrence of Kovid-19 and the closure of major cities has weakened China's economic growth, which the ADB says will outpace other Asian economies. Developed for the first time in more than three decades.
India's growth forecast for this year has been cut to 7% from 7.2% due to inflation and monetary tightening. Strong domestic demand in Indonesia and the Philippines is contributing to the improvement of Southeast Asia's economic outlook by 5.1%. According to Bloomberg News.
