(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Acting Prime Minister, on the afternoon of September 22, 2022, presided over the announcement of the winners of the Social Services Award for Sub-National Administration for 2020-21.
The event was held at Sokha Phnom Penh Hotel with the participation of the Ministry of Interior, UNICEF Representative in Cambodia, along with Mr. Prum Sokha, Minister of Public Function, Governor of Phnom Penh, Governor, Governor, District, Khan, Commune Chief and Sangkat Representative and partner representatives Development as well as civil society organizations.
According to the report of Mr. Prak Sam Oeun, Director General of the General Department of Administration of the Ministry of Interior, said that the Ministry of Interior has received and summarized the indicator score form completed by each concerned administration, found that 417 commune administrations 61 municipal, district and Khan administrations and 7 provincial and municipal administrations participated in the Social Services Award for Sub-National Administration.
* Commune / Sangkat Administration: There are 2 three-star ratings, 126 two-star ratings, 233 one-star ratings and 56 zero-star ratings, for a total of 417 Commune / Sangkat Administration
* Municipal, District, Khan Administration: 21-star rating, no two-star rating, 21 one-star rating, 36-star rating, and 4 zero-star rating, total 61, Municipal, District, Khan, Total 61, Municipal, District, Khan
* Capital-Provincial Administration: Three-star rating, no two-star rating, three-star rating, three-star rating and one zero-star rating, for a total of seven Capital-provincial administrations.
The results of the above star award show that only 2 commune administrations received three star rating, while other levels of administration, including municipal, district, khan and provincial administrations, did not receive the three-star rating for social services. Which makes it difficult to continue to identify and award social services championships at all levels of administration.
The Capital and Provincial Administration has received a total of seven star ratings, including three three-star ratings, two two-star ratings, one one-star rating and one zero-star rating.
The report states that the winners of the Social Services Championship are as follows:
1st: Champion Award for Social Services, Capital and Provincial Administration * Siem Reap Provincial Administration ranked 1st * Kandal Provincial Administration ranked 2nd
2nd: Champion Award for Social Services, Municipality, District Administration, Khan * Takhmao Municipality Administration of Kandal Province, 1st place * Khan Meanchey Administration of Phnom Penh, 2nd place * Khan Kampoul Administration, 3rd place
