Authorities call on residents to be extra vigilant as eight districts in Siem Reap province are affected by floods
(Siem Reap): The Secretariat of the Siem Reap Provincial Disaster Management Committee said that after a series of rains from September 17 to 21, the floods affected 150 villages in 31 communes. The eight districts are: Srey Snom, Kralanh, Chi Kreng, Angkor Chum, Varin, Puok, Sot Nikum and Prasat Bakong.
A total of 2,906 families were affected, 1,760 houses were submerged and 29 houses were flooded, and 4 families were evacuated on their own. For other people have not yet reached the level to be evacuated.
According to the forecast of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology from September 21-29, 2022, the effects of the low pressure system (ITCZ) can cause flooding, while some areas are already flooded. During this time. The Secretariat of the Provincial, Municipal, District, Commune and Sangkat Disaster Management Committee continues to be ready to monitor and prepare for disaster relief or other incidents.
Authorities continue campaign to crack down on illegal gambling sites and inspect pawn shops in Chbar Ampov district
(Phnom Penh): Under the order of Mr. Cheng Monira, Chbar Ampov District Governor, Mr. Nhean Chansophea, Deputy District Governor, continued to lead the police force to inspect the pawnshops and crack down on illegal gambling sites in the district.
The campaign took place on the morning of September 22, 2022, inspecting two different locations and found 92 motorcycles. The first location is Dara Rithy Phonsop Pawn Shop. The owner of the shop, Chan Bunthen, has a valid patent tax and license in Doeum Chan village, Chbar Ampov II commune. Suspected as a motorcycle involved in the crime.
Location 2: Ramanet Prek Pra Pawn Shop, the owner of the shop named Nhoc Theara, has a valid patent tax and license in Preah Ponlea village, Sangkat Prek Pra, found 66 motorcycles with relevant documents.
As a result of the inspection of the pawn shop, the joint force recorded and completed the procedures and returned the motorbike that the owner took as collateral to the pawn shop owner.
At the same time, the Deputy District Governor advised the pawn shop owners to be very careful of those who use various means as collateral, especially to check the relevant documents related to those means thoroughly first, if correct. Waiting to receive a mortgage. In case of suspicion of abnormality, it must be reported to the authorities immediately to take action.
