The Chinese Embassy in Cambodia organizes a farewell ceremony for a group of Cambodian students who can return to study in China after the situation of Kovid 19 has eased
The farewell ceremony was organized by the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia and was attended by a group of students representing 23 provinces, who will return to study in China after the situation in Kovid 19 has eased. The first step is for 350 students to obtain visas to study in China under the auspices of the Chinese government, the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia and the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
Hun Bunrath, a student who has to study medicine in China for six years, told Cambodia-China Friendship Radio that Chinese scholarships are very important for all young Cambodians because they can greatly reduce the family burden and can go. Study in a country with a wide range and international quality, which allows us to gain a lot of knowledge to contribute to the development of the country to be more advanced.
Voice: "I would like to thank the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia for helping me to study in China again, and also thank the Ministry of Education, especially the Chinese government scholarship ... I would like to thank "The friendship between Cambodia and China is long-lasting and more developed than before, which provides many benefits to young Cambodians, such as the opportunity to study in China and have the ability to work in Cambodia."
Ms. Chan Sivly, a student who has to study finance for 4 years in China, said that she was very excited to attend the Chinese Embassy's farewell program for Cambodian students to study in China because That such a program has long been missed due to the condition of Kovid 19.
Voice: "I would like to wish the Cambodian-Chinese friendship to last longer and help train the next generation of Cambodian children to know more about the culture, civilization and knowledge from abroad to develop the country."
She also stated that the Chinese scholarship has really helped many Cambodian students, in addition to easing the burden of the family, also encouraged students to have the courage to accept their own development more and return from China is able to help develop Your country will help spread knowledge to the next generation.
Voice: "We will not forget that in early 2020, after the first discovery of a new virus in Wuhan, China, Cambodian students there did not rush to evacuate, but chose to stay with teachers and friends. Join their class. "Through this, we can see the bright future of Sino-Cambodian friendship."
Wang Wentian stressed that the Chinese and Cambodian governments have always paid close attention to the return of Cambodian students to China. Although the new epidemic is not over, China has decided to allow Cambodian students studying in China to return to school and resume classes as soon as possible.
Voice: "When you study in China, you can not only learn from textbooks, but also experience Chinese culture, taste Chinese food, and more importantly, feel the friendship between China. And Cambodia. "I wish you all success in your studies and a bright future."
"On behalf of the Chinese Ambassador, on behalf of the Ministry of Education, I would like to express my once again thank you and thank you to the Chinese government, Chinese leadership, as well as all Chinese universities for accepting Cambodian students and providing warmth to Cambodian students. Going to school gives a lot of priority to Cambodian students. ”
"Please be informed that in China, there are 1,700 Cambodian students who study in 27 provinces and cities in more than 100 universities in China, most of them have bachelor's, master's and doctoral degrees and study various disciplines such as engineering, law, economics and economics." Others are very skilled. ”
On that occasion, Mr. Pit Chamnan, Acting Minister of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, and HE Wang Wentian, Ambassador of the People's Republic of China to Cambodia and a group of students took a souvenir photo at the Cambodia-China Friendship Park on the grounds of the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia. In a very happy atmosphere.
