Fourth: ECCC Recognized internationally as a model tribunal for prosecuting crimes and massacres, it has gradually become a model court that some countries have considered as a model for establishing similar courts in Post-war peace framework or internal conflict.
Fifth: The success of the ECCC Considered a collective success, including: the entire Cambodian people, the Royal Government, the United Nations and the international community, and should be promoted to serve as a model court for prosecuting serious crimes and future massacres. On the international stage, and especially at the regional level, to contribute to strengthening the international criminal justice system.
