General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 43 suspects, 21 were arrested in 11 criminal cases and 22 were arrested in four drug cases.
Dr. Men Sam An Leads a Ministry Delegation to Pay Respect to the Late Mr. Chiep Sivorn, Member of Parliament for Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, this morning, September 22, 2022, led a delegation of the Ministry to pay tribute to the late Mr. Chiep Sivorn, Member of the 5th Committee of the National Assembly and Representative of Phnom Penh constituency.
Mr. Chiep Sivorn, Member of the Fifth Committee of the National Assembly and Member of Parliament for Phnom Penh Constituency, passed away on September 20, 2022 at 21:20 at the age of 77 due to illness.
The Honorable Dr. Men Sam An considered the death of Mr. Chiep Sivorn as the loss of her husband, father, father-in-law and grandfather, a devout and pious man, and the loss of an important patriot who contributed to the development of the country. To grow forever.
The body of Mr. Chiep Sivorn was laid to rest at the Royal Royal Mortuary at 101, Street M07, Sangkat Prek Leap, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh from September 21 to 25, 2022.
Mrs. Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An dedicated the merit to the soul of Mr. Chiep Sivorn to go to his death.
