(Kandal): Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the National Working Group in Muk Kampul District, called on Buddhists and people across the country to maintain peace and development. All sectors under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister and do not be deceived by the deceptions of some unjust opposition groups that lead to the disintegration of the nation.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth made this appeal on the morning of September 22, 2022, on the occasion that he and Mrs. Vu Sopheak Tevy, as well as their families and colleagues of the National Working Group in Muk Kampoul District, including the people of Prek Anchanh Commune, Muk Kampoul District, were invited to attend. Kan Ben 12th turn at Wat Rattanak Bopharam in Prek Anchanh commune, Muk Kampoul district, Kandal province.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth, along with his family and colleagues, donated alms to the monks, along with a number of suffixes for continuing to build various achievements in the pagoda, and donated some funds to the committee of Acha Ta Chi, Yai Chi, and the participating Buddhists.
Please be informed that Pchum Ben is one of the biggest festivals of all for Buddhists and this festival lasts for 15 days, from the 1st of Roach to the 15th of Roach. This is celebrated by the Cambodian people of Buddhism every year.
According to the records of the history of the Khmer festival, the celebration of this festival is to pray for the blessings of Kosal Phal Bon to the parents and relatives of the seven children who have passed away so that they can come and receive Kosal Phal Bon to be born in death.
On the other hand, the Cambodian people believe that all the rich people, ancestors or relatives who committed sins while they were alive, and when they passed away, did not know what nationality they were or if they were born as ghosts. Receive this merit from them as well when the ghosts are released for 15 days on the day of Kan Ben. Death news! Husband of Lok Chumteav Nhem Morakot, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Women's Affairs, dies at 70 of heart attack
