Ministry of Social Affairs organizes religious ceremony on the occasion of Kan Ben for drug victims
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, during the Kan Ben Ceremony on September 22, 2022, organized a blessing ceremony for drug victims living in the National Center for Treatment and Rehabilitation. Rehabilitation of drug addicts in Kraing Thnong, Phnom Penh.
During the Kan Ben and Pchum Ben seasons, Cambodians often bring food to the monks at the pagoda. However, for drug victims who are receiving treatment, it is not possible to leave the pagoda like normal people.
As a consideration for drug victims to participate in the Kan Ben and Pchum Ben ceremonies, the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation has organized a blessing ceremony for monks at the National Center for Treatment and Rehabilitation. Direct drug addiction in Kraing Thnong, while there are hundreds of victims in this center.
He added that drug victims are victims who deserve the same attention as the general population. This arrangement is also to dedicate merit to the relatives of all drug victims.
He also advised all drug victims to seek medical treatment and treatment in order to return to the community with their families and rebuild their lives. President of the Constitutional Council wants to see the Ministry of Education and the Ministry of Interior help spread the Constitution more widely
(Phnom Penh): Dr. M. Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council, wants to see the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and the Ministry of Interior participate in disseminating the Constitution to the public more widely.
He said this on the occasion of the Constitutional Council held a meeting to celebrate the 29th anniversary of the promulgation of the Cambodian Constitution on the morning of Thursday, September 22, 2022 at the conference hall of the White House Chamkarmon.
The 1993 Constitution is an invaluable treasure of the Khmer nation that every Cambodian has an obligation to respect. Wherever the values of the Constitution go, there are the values of the rule of law, democracy and human rights, which are the key components in building and developing the modern state.
Mr. Im Chhun Lim stated that in the process of building a society of the rule of law in Cambodia, attention should be paid to building the legal framework, institutional framework, and procedures for disseminating and enforcing the law. In relation to the dissemination of the real actors in this work is the state dissemination mechanism, with the participation of all other inter-actors in society.
