Former Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia: King Norodom Sihanouk I Know!
The former ambassador expressed his deepest condolences and described his achievements and aspirations for national independence, Cambodia's development and the strengthening of good Sino-Cambodian relations in Cambodia. On the occasion of the 100th anniversary of the birth of His Majesty the King on September 15, with the full content as follows:
"The Royal Ceremony of the 100th Anniversary of the Birth of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk was held in Beijing, People's Republic of China on September 15. Distinguished guests, top leaders who attended the event praised the great achievements of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk in demanding independence, development of Cambodia and the strengthening of good Sino-Cambodian relations.
Adherence to independence and territorial integrity is the main principle for building his country. At the beginning of the early days, when he fought the colonists in the struggle for independence and later fought against the new imperialism to defend independence, he always adhered to the principle of not giving up and never giving up on the goal of demanding "Independent" and "neutral, peaceful" always.
From 1955 to 1970, the "Sangkum Reastr Niyum era" was a period of great progress and prosperity of Cambodia. In addition to effective policy reforms, he also initiated economic, financial and trade reforms, strengthened state governance, and measures to boost the production and export of agricultural products such as rice and rubber. Etc.
He also paid attention to education, health, telecommunications and other areas that are important to the daily lives of the people, especially the implementation of effective measures to develop agricultural products and improve livelihoods. Better farmers, such as distributing land to landless people and helping them improve production techniques by setting up rural housing improvement commissions and providing financial support.
He later initiated the Geneva Conference on Laos and the Indochina Three-Party Summit. He actively participated in strengthening the friendship between the peoples of the three Indochina Peninsular countries against foreign aggression and achieved complete victory and great achievements in history.
Eighty years ago, Samdech Sangkhareach Chuon Nath wrote a poem for His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, with the meaning of the poem: To have mastery over his soul and destiny, leaving the legacy and legacy of Mohanakor from Generation after generation must have a strong will like a temple stone, must remember the glory of the Angkorian era, must firmly believe in their homeland, overcome all obstacles to lead the country to prosperity.
This poem later became the national anthem of the Kingdom of Cambodia and has been sung to this day. And this is the most sincere admiration and respect of the Cambodian people to him.
Fifty years ago, my Cambodian friends and I always sang a song together. The meaning of the song is: Oh! China, you are a great power that can be great, but you are polite, no matter how big or small, you know how to protect equality, independence, freedom, peace, humanity ……….
This is the song "Sronoh China" written by King Norodom Sihanouk when he visited China in the early 60s. Knowing and full of deep affection for China, he described China as a "second homeland", with great kindness and deep love for many Chinese people.
On this occasion, I would like to express my deepest respect and love for this close and great friend. "
