The Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway is nearly 200 kilometers long and cost more than $ 2 billion. This road is a huge investment for Chinese companies and it will take a long time to get their capital back.
During the final inspection of the construction of the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway on September 21, 2022, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol highlighted many obstacles and complexities during the study phase of the expressway construction. In particular, the budget to build this road.
According to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Chinese investors do not have a large budget. Of that, the company has about 30 percent, equivalent to 600 million US dollars, and has to borrow from the bank about 70 percent. This loan has a high interest rate and a low interest rate, requiring a guarantee from the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said that because Cambodia does not have a policy to guarantee private sector investment, so Cambodia can not guarantee. To address this high interest rate, the Chinese government has provided a grant of US $ 150 million to the Royal Government of Cambodia, and the Royal Government of Cambodia has given all these grants to companies to help lower the interest rate ceiling.
For the senior minister, the above solution is an effort by the Chinese government to help Cambodia build the expressway, which is the main economic artery connecting the Phnom Penh economic pole to Sihanoukville and the deep sea port.
"Due to the good relations between Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen and the Chinese leadership, the Chinese government is helping to encourage companies to invest in Cambodia," he said.
Mr. Sun Chanthol, the Minister, who was very interested in the vibrancy of the national service, said that investment that uses large capital and long-term recapitalization, such as the construction of expressways, is difficult to find investment companies. . If there is no cooperation or good understanding, it is not easy to find a company to invest.
