Russia's oil imports, including supplies through pipelines in the eastern Pacific, Siberia and maritime transport from Russia's European and Far Eastern ports, totaled eight, according to Reuters, citing data from the Chinese Customs Administration. 342 million tons.
Russia's oil exports to China have risen as Chinese independent refiners have expanded their purchases of oil from Russia at a discount, deviating from oil imports from West Africa and Brazil.
China's crude purchases rose to take advantage of a drop in Russian purchases from European countries as Beijing was in dire need of oil as the Ukraine crisis pushed Moscow to seek alternative markets. The West, which stopped buying its oil.
However, crude oil imports from Saudi Arabia recovered last month to 8.475 million tonnes, or 1.99 million barrels a day, up 5 percent from the same period last year. Last year.
Saudi Arabia remained the largest supplier from the beginning of the year to date, importing 58.31 million tonnes from January to August, down 0.3 percent from the same period last year. Earlier, oil imports from Russia were 55.79 million tons, up 7.3 percent. According to Reuters.
Floods inundate four villages in Chheu Tom commune, Krakor district, Pursat province, but not severely
(Pursat): The flood situation in Chheu Tom commune, Krakor district, Pursat province caused flooding and affected the lives of people in 4 villages, but not severe due to heavy rain overnight. One day, the water receded for more than a day after the weather began to ease.
The district governor added that during the rainy day and night, water flowed from the upper part of the Oral mountain range, causing flooding in four villages of Chheu Tom commune, Krakor district, Pursat province, including Kapas village. Pass on Dangkeab Kdam village and Ponnak village from 1:30 pm on September 21, 2022. But by the evening of the same day, the water had receded by more than one, and this was because the weather had begun to ease.
