(Phnom Penh): Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, led a delegation from the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports to attend the Summit on the Development of the Education System at the United Nations Headquarters in New York, USA from 16 to September 20, 2022.
The purpose of this summit is:
* (1): Urges UN member states to set education as the highest priority of their political agenda * (2): Discuss joint actions and strategic solutions based on evidence for systemic reform. Education and rehabilitation of education in the context of Kovid-19 * and (3): Promote the participation and support of all stakeholders, especially youth participation in the reform of the education system.
The summit discussed five priorities, including:
* (1): Improving schools to have an equitable environment, safety and well-being * (2): Improving the quality of teachers, teaching and teaching profession * (3): Improving learning and skills for living with Work and sustainable development * (4): Digital evolution * and (5): Increased funding for education.
