Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Orders to Crack Down on All Kinds of Gambling
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda and Mr. Vong Bun Visoth, Prosecutor of the Provincial Court, on the morning of September 21, 2022, chaired a meeting with the participation of the Deputy Provincial Governor and relevant officials of the Armed Forces. The three types of governors of the 10 districts to put in place a number of measures to crack down on all types of gambling in the territory of Kampong Cham province.
The governor said that so far, all forms of illegal gambling must be cracked down on, including human trafficking, money laundering and drug offenses that must be cracked down on. At the same time, the authorities must identify the places that used to do illegal gambling business, and continue to make the contract for the owners of those places responsible in front of the authorities by ensuring that there is no illegal gambling.
The provincial governor requested all competent officials not to be involved in any kind of gambling offenses. In addition, the commanders of the three types of armed forces must further instruct their officers at the local level not to be involved Behind, do not intervene and do not hide.
The provincial governor also instructed the Municipal Unity Command to continue to cooperate with the Prosecutor's Office of the Provincial Court, to go hand in hand with the legislature, the executive and the court, as well as the media, to continue the cooperation leading to a successful crackdown.
Mr. Vong Bunvisoth also said that regarding the crackdown on gambling of all kinds, the authorities must focus on the evidence and must collect enough equipment as a component of gambling to compile documents to deal with the procedure.
