On that occasion, the team brought 640,000 Riels, 2 fishing rods, 2 cases of drinks, 2 cases of pure water, 1 set of children's equipment as a gift to visit and share as a family burden. Commentary: Peace is the lifeblood of mankind and the lifeblood of the world
BEIJING (Reuters) - Globalization is currently undergoing unprecedented changes in nearly a century of history. The Kovid-19 crisis continues to affect the world, wars have erupted in some countries, and traditional and non-traditional insecurity has been on the rise, so the international community urgently needs mechanisms to help guide the world's ships. He does not get lost in the vast ocean.
We often hear the saying, "Without peace there is no everything." Of course, everyone knows the reason for this, but the ambitions of people who are greedy for power often undermine the foundations of peace. The world has now entered a stage of competition between multilateralism and unilateralism, between polygamy and hegemony, in which the voice of support for multilateralism has been gradually gaining ground.
As we all know, whether bilateral or multilateral relations, communication and exchange must be based on honesty, respect and equality, this is the common idea of the international community, but there are still some countries that think only From personal interests, adhering to the concept of "I am great" in international relations. But it should be noted that from the beginning, hegemony has always pushed the situation into fragility or stagnation.
Whether in the past or in the present, war brings only destruction and tragedy to humanity. Both world wars have left irreparable tragedies, vulnerable groups such as women, children and the elderly have become the food of war, human lives more fragile than ants.
After the end of World War II, humanity was urgently needed for a peaceful world, so the United Nations was established to guide international affairs and play a role in safeguarding world security and peace. The vast majority of humankind do not want war because the desolation and famine caused by the fires of war have brought generations of suffering.
Maintaining order and world order is not in the hands of any country or individual, but requires the participation of all countries and regions. The old saying goes, "A chopstick does not break." If you want to live under the roof of peace, all you have to do is unite, cooperate and manage differences peacefully, but do not use force to oppress others. Do not follow your own ideas.
In this sense, no matter what the circumstances, whether delivering a message to the world or to the Chinese people, the Chinese head of state has always said that China adheres to peaceful development. Indeed, China's chronic war in the past, fueled by foreign famine and civil strife, has hampered and slowed China's development, or in other words, China has to rebuild the nation from the palm of its hand. Empty.
It should also be noted that in 2021 and 2022, Chinese President Xi Jinping outlined two consecutive initiatives, namely the Global Development Initiative and the Global Security Initiative, which contribute to China's wisdom and strength for Promote the development and protection of world security.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, uttered the words "Thank you for peace" to highlight the overwhelming importance of peace for all of us. Cambodia is a country that has suffered from the flames of war, so all people do not want to see the country fall into the abyss of death, because there is peace, we can only talk about development and social security.
