With the launch announcement, the company also unveiled the price list for the first expressway transit in Cambodia. Prices for this expressway trip are divided into the following five categories.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, said that the above price is still lower than some countries in the world.
During the final inspection on the construction of the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway on Wednesday morning, September 21, the Senior Minister emphasized, 8 cents.
Responding to the claim that some neighboring countries' highways are cheaper than Cambodia, the senior minister said that due to changes in the economic situation and economic differences from one stage to another. That is, some roads are built at a time when raw material or labor costs are low, so construction costs are low, but now the cost of construction is different compared to 10 or 20 years ago.
"Some of the roads in our neighboring countries were built 10 to 20 years ago, so the cost is not $ 2 billion, when it can be about 500 million, for example, we get up to $ 2 billion," he said. This road When I studied in 2007, we signed an agreement with a company worth 700 million US dollars, now up to 2 billion US dollars.
Another reason for the difference in prices is that the number of vehicles in Cambodia is small compared to other countries, which requires higher pricing so that companies can recoup their investment within the 50-year investment period set by the Royal Government. . This is the additional confirmation of the Senior Minister.
"Thus, neighboring countries may be a bit cheaper, but many countries have higher prices because they use a base price of 10 cents to 12 cents per kilometer."
Please be informed that the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway project has a length of 187.05 km, which started construction on March 22, 2019. This road connects Village 1, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh to Village 1, Sangkat 3, Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province.
The Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway Project is the first expressway project and the most important strategic corridor project in Cambodia, reducing the travel time from Phnom Penh to Sihanoukville Port from five hours to just two hours. Only and help reduce the cost of logistics.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol emphasized that he had submitted a request to Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen to officially inaugurate the road during November 2022, when Prime Minister Li Keqiang visited Cambodia.
