Phnom Penh Municipal Police Reveals Results of Investigation in Case of Pawning Phone to Get Fines at Kouch Kanong Roundabout
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner on September 21, 2022, presented the results of the investigation into cases where people took people as collateral to get money to pay fines to traffic police officers at the Kouch Kanong roundabout.
Phnom Penh Municipal Police spokesman Colonel San Sok Seiha told Fresh News that the person who took the people to take the phone as a pawn was not a police officer at the target, but a civilian who took the opportunity and the police Searching for arrests.
The statement from the spokesperson of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commission came after a full day of search yesterday, after the incident, when the authorities called both people as tricycle riders and traffic police. All at this destination come for face-to-face interrogation at the Phnom Penh Municipal Police.
Colonel San Sok Seiha described it as follows:
"After careful research related to the case of Keating on September 20, 2022, at about 10:30 am, a tricycle driver was driving from Wat Phnom to the crossing. Chroy Changvar Bridge When you reach the roundabout, Kouch Kanong, suddenly a traffic police officer stopped to fine you for not locking the helmet.
At that time, law enforcement officials confirmed that according to the law, the offender was fined 60,000 riel. He then said that he had no money to pay the fine, and then he called to talk to his boss, then he He also handed over the phone to the officer to talk to his boss in order to ask the traffic police officer not to be fined, but to educate.
Our officer immediately returned the phone to him and let him go without penalty. At that time, an opportunist dressed in civilian clothes took the opportunity to call the man out, telling him that if he had no money, he could take him to a pawn shop to pay the traffic fare without paying attention and in a hurry, he could not believe it and gave him the money. That goes to civilians who pretend to be law enforcement.
The Road Traffic Police Office is searching for the culprit, who is not in charge, in order to clarify whether he is involved with any of the traffic police officers at the above target or not? To find out the truth and punish according to the law.
The Phnom Penh Municipal Police also instructed all officers to use appropriate gestures and words with the people, even if they are busy or tired of performing their duties. On the other hand, it is necessary to carry out ethical work and guide further education on traffic laws, and to respect all laws in order to protect the lives and property of the people.
