Mr. Say Sam Al said that the presence of traps in the forest is due to the need to eat wildlife, which has led to an increase in trapping and hunting. This is a common problem that the Ministry of Environment considers to prevent and prevent wildlife trapping activities in protected areas, which is important to prevent further increase in the number of rare animal losses.
