New corridor line connecting land, sea and sea in western China achieves coverage throughout western region
BEIJING, Sept. 17 (Xinhua) - The Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region Conference on the Joint Construction of a New Corridor to Connect High-Level Railways to the West Sea was held in Nanning, Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region, China on September 17.
During the conference, a groundbreaking ceremony for the Beibu-Gulf Overland-Tibet Railway was held, marking the completion of a new corridor connecting the mainland and sea lanes. Western China has officially achieved full western coverage.
The conference focused on "Building new corridors connecting land and sea, sharing new opportunities for development." The conference focused on the promotion of railways, ferries, cross-border transport, air transport and other products in the corridors and major industrial parks such as "Two Countries and Two Parks", China, Malaysia and the road port. Nanning International Railway and so on.
According to sources, from January to August this year, the new corridor connecting the main corridor connecting the land to the western sea ran a total of 5,816 lines, an increase of 48%, the Bay of Beibu achieved the transport. Shipment of 4.3 million containers increased by 20%, and various indicators of corridor operations continued to improve.
The attractiveness and competitiveness of the new corridor connecting the land to the western seas has been steadily strengthened, and it has become an important corridor for goods in the central and western regions, out to sea and borders, and also a gateway. The fastest and most convenient transport corridor connecting China to ASEAN under the RCEP framework.
