Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner Ordered to Investigate Traffic Police Case at Kouch Kanong Roundabout
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Thet, Deputy Commissioner General and Commissioner of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, has ordered an investigation into the case of a traffic police officer at the Kouch Kanong roundabout who fined residents and he had no money, but turned out to be a police officer at that destination. Take the motorbike owner to take the phone as collateral to get the money to pay the fine.
Colonel San Sok Seiha, Assistant and Spokesman of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, told Fresh News on the afternoon of September 20, 2022, after receiving information related to the traffic police at the Kouch Kanong roundabout to take people to pawn. Call to get money to pay the fine, Phnom Penh police commissioner ordered to investigate this case.
Colonel San Sok Seiha said, "I am doing this work very carefully. Overall, His Excellency the Commissioner has never excused and never allowed officials to do this wrong, as long as we are wrong, we must follow the rules." "Wrong, we must punish, but if the officers do well, we always have the praise, confer the rank and position, etc., but if wrong, we must apply the discipline of the forces."
The spokesman of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police also claimed that around this case, the professional police officers are asking for the cooperation of the people to point out the target where he was fined, especially the police officer who took him to pawn the phone to Take the money to pay the fine.
It should be informed that on the morning of September 20, 2022, a traffic police incident at the roundabout of Chroy Changvar Bridge (Kouch Kanong roundabout, old stadium) fined a man who was driving a tricycle for not wearing the right key. Pay a fine of 50,000 riels.
But the tricycle driver told the traffic police that he had only 4,500 riel in his pocket. He was carrying luggage to deliver to the guest and was afraid of not being able to tell the police that he only had this phone, so he only took it as collateral. This solution was also approved by the traffic police and also transported by motorbike to the tricycle driver to pawn the phone for 60,000 riel and then withdraw 50,000 riel to the police and keep 10,000 in it.
This story has caused a great deal of consternation on Facebook, with each citizen expressing outrage and unpredictability that traffic police officers enforcing traffic rules at the Kouch Kanong roundabout are so strict that they lead you to this level. Who is fined for pawning a phone and taking money to pay a fine for not wearing a helmet key.
