Senior Minister Kun Kim Calls on Authorities to Monitor Flood Situation and Prepare to Assist Flood Victims
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Deputy Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, called on the relevant authorities, especially the Capital-Provincial Disaster Management Secretariat, to pay more attention to the flood situation in their localities and prepare for intervention forces. Save the people.
Senior Minister Kun Kim Hun Sen's personal appeal to Senior Minister Kun Kim on the disaster management work came after the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology announced the impact of the low pressure system (ITCZ) from China, which led to heavy rains. For a week from September 21 to 27, 2022.
In response to this situation, Senior Minister Kun Kim reminded all relevant officials, including the main intervention forces, to be ready to intervene to save the people to safety and in case it is not possible to report to the emergency level. Nation to move out to intervene immediately.
Senior Minister Kun Kim also called on people in vulnerable areas to pay attention to the announcements of professional institutions that regularly inform about climate change and to take good care of their children, property and livestock in case Immediate intervention needs to be reported immediately to the nearest local authority.
However, the National Committee for Disaster Management is ready to help people recover from the floods by providing safe havens in flood-prone areas. This was confirmed by Senior Minister Kun Kim.
The staff, with high responsibility for disaster management, also spoke about the flood situation in Banteay Meanchey and Oddar Meanchey provinces. According to the senior minister, the floods in Oddar Meanchey and Banteay Meanchey provinces are not yet serious. In Banteay Meanchey province, about 35 families were evacuated to safety.
Please be informed that the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology this morning, September 20, 2022, issued a notification on the weather situation in Cambodia from September 21-27, 2022. The Ministry of Water Resources has confirmed that high pressure on China has pushed the low pressure system (ITCZ) downstream for a long time over the Dangrek Mountains and the plateau in northeastern Cambodia. At the same time, the southwest monsoon winds blow from weak to moderate.
