(Phnom Penh): On September 19, 2022, LOLC Microfinance Institution (LOLC) handed over 80,000 leaflets on drug issues and some materials to the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs. Addiction to disseminate the drug problem to the people through the Drug Control Committee of the Capital, Province, Municipality, District, Khan, Commune, Sangkat and the member ministries of the National Authority for Combating Drugs.
The handover ceremony was held at the LOLC headquarters by Mr. Sok Voeun, Chief Executive Officer and Major General Lim Tong Huot, Director of the Department of Legal Education and Rehabilitation of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs.
Mr. Sok Voeun said, "The fight against drugs is a joint work of all of us, not to be considered the exclusive work of any one person or group. The solution is to start with all of us, the elimination of drugs. "It is a major common problem that we must all work together to avoid danger and bring disaster to ourselves, our families and our society."
He urged all stakeholders and all citizens to work together to prevent the spread of the drug problem, which is destroying communities. He added that the LOLC will continue to fully support the National Anti-Drug Authority to join the fight against drugs.
Lt. Gen. Lim Tong Huot stated that LOLC Microfinance Institution is an active partner that has always supported the General Secretariat of the National Anti-Drug Authority on outreach, education, anti-drug and social assistance such as Provide clean water wells, hand washing facilities in schools, fight against the epidemic of Kovid-19 traffic and assist in the rescue of people affected by the floods. Etc.
He added that the implementation of a multi-sectoral strategy to combat drugs is needed from all sectors, especially the private sector, as the LOLC has been doing both now and in the future to ensure security and order. To all people, no drugs, no violence, no crime.
Please note that this is the eighth time that the LOLC has submitted to the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs a leaflet on drug issues, which reflects the LOLC's commitment to continue Participate in the fight against drugs in Cambodia.
