Authorities Continue Operation to Crack Down on Illegal Gambling in Sihanoukville
(Preah Sihanouk): On the morning of September 19, 2022, the joint police force of Sihanoukville Unity Command raided gambling places in the market town, cafes, such as numbers, cards, apong, cockfighting system. Online fishing games and other games in the 4 districts.
The operation was coordinated by Mr. Penh Piseth, Deputy Prosecutor of the Sihanoukville Provincial Court and under the direct supervision of Mr. Sar Kakada, Governor of Sihanoukville, following the orders of the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Mayor Sar Kakada told Fresh News that gambling sites in the town, markets and cafes were confiscated by the police and a contract was terminated from now on.
He added that the owner of the gambling place in the past, after the authorities confiscated the material, also made a contract to stop, if the theft continues, the authorities will follow the legal procedures. Senior Minister Cham Prasidh Meets with Thak Global Institute to Participate in Digital Technology Development in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kittisetha Dr. Cham Prasidh, Senior Minister and Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, allowed the management team of Thak Global Institute to pay a courtesy call to present a strategic plan to participate in the development of digital technology in Cambodia.
On that occasion, the leadership of Thak Global Institute presented to Senior Minister Cham Prasidh and the delegation of the Ministry the background and progress of the institute since its establishment in 2019 and the strategic plan of the institute. The meeting took place at the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation last week.
The meeting was attended by Mr. Sat Samy, Permanent Secretary of State, Mr. Chhem Keat Rithy, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary of State, 20 leaders of Thak Global Institute, led by Mr. Yousinoki Sochi, Honorary President and Founder and Ms. Heang Ohmuy Chairman of the Board and many other relevant officials and officials.
Senior Minister Cham Prasidh said that the Thak Global Institute has been operating rapidly since 2021, including the selection of outstanding students, and he was very pleased that the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation has cooperated with the Institute at the same time as Cambodia needs. More human resources, technology and innovation.
Senior Minister Cham Prasidh added that after seeing the past achievements of the institute, the results showed that the teaching was good and the students were satisfied with the teaching.
At the same time, Senior Minister Cham Prasidh also praised the Institute, which plans to open a short-term bachelor's and master's degrees, which is good and in line with the current situation and the quality of recognition in Southeast Asia.
Since the establishment of the institute, a total of 225 students have received 100% scholarships on tuition fees for vocational training courses.
They have successfully passed three rigorous recruitment exams and are receiving training every weekend for a full year, which includes new business and research courses as well as internships at companies. Well.
Thak Global is a new emerging technology institute in Cambodia, fully sponsored by a group of Japanese men with the vision of becoming the leading institute for human resource development, a skilled workforce in engineering technology in Cambodia and in Asia. Southeast.
Thak Global Institute plans to launch the third generation of vocational training and launch the Innovation and Business Center, as well as establish a bachelor's degree program where students take a short time to complete and become a quality technology resource for the country. Cambodia and the region.
Stove manufacturers in Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province complain that it is difficult to find workers and find clay to make stoves
(Kampong Chhnang): More than 10 families in Kdei Tnaot village, Sre Thmei commune, Rolea Bier district are currently promoting the production of stoves, sales and livelihood, which now can not hire workers in the village to help produce as much as before because the people Most of the forces in their villages have already gone out to work in factories, some in Phnom Penh and some in factories in Kampong Chhnang province.
A woman who sells stoves, who asked not to be named, said that due to the shortage of labor, workers have to produce raw materials, especially clay for production, which is becoming increasingly scarce due to the presence of clay that locals used to take. In the past, they were sold to private companies.
He stated that although the business of making stoves, which is the tradition of the Khmer ancestors, did not earn much money to do, the villagers still struggle to keep the pottery to make all kinds of stoves.
