Many Cambodian women entrepreneurs graduate with new business skills
This project has helped young women entrepreneurs living in Phnom Penh, Siem Reap, Kampong Cham, Kampot and Battambang to be able to develop their small businesses.
"We are proud to support the support of so many young women entrepreneurs through our Women and Active Women project," said Cine Westmin.
"Women entrepreneurs play an important role in strengthening the lives of the people and the politics of a democratic society, not only through the establishment and expansion of their businesses, but also by working together with business associations to create "It also has implications for policy."
About 160 participants, including women entrepreneurs, representatives from partner organizations, representatives of the Ministry of Women's Affairs, Ministry of Economy and Finance, National Bank of Cambodia, participated in the graduation program.
"Strengthening Business Networks and Business Development" for Young Women Entrepreneurs is a three-year project run by the social enterprise C-Investment, funded by USAID through the Pak Cambodia Active Women Project.
C-Investment did not provide 6 basic business training courses, 10 basic financial management courses, and provided assistance under the Small Budget Package to two groups of women entrepreneurs. The offerings also include a video series and a network of women entrepreneurs that increase opportunities, as well as mentoring and training for women entrepreneurs.
She continued, "The training programs, networking programs and tools provided through this project not only strengthen the community of women entrepreneurs who are striving to expand their business, but also to increase their productivity." Positive to society, economy and environment as well. 300 Families in Kampong Tralach District, Kampong Chhnang Province Receive Donations from ASAS Malaysia
