(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Microfinance Association (CMA), the Association of Banks in Cambodia and the Association of the Federation of Finance and Technology of Cambodia on September 19, 2022, signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) to promote effective business initiatives. Social responsibility and capacity building focused on banking and financial business.
"The signing of this MoU will make a significant contribution not only to improving the financial technology system for financial institutions, but also as a new opportunity for Cambodians to learn more about new technologies, especially "An opportunity for new business owners in the financial sector to effectively implement their operations in the future."
Please be informed that the Cambodian Microfinance Association was established in 2004 with the aim of helping all Cambodians to access a wide range of official financial services in a timely and responsible manner through a responsible and sustainable financial system. Ensure the security, prosperity and sustainability of the microfinance sector in Cambodia.
So far, the Cambodian Microfinance Association has 122 members, including: 5 banking institutions, 5 deposit-taking microfinance institutions, 74 microfinance institutions, 12 leasing companies and 26 rural credit institutions.
At the beginning of the 21st century, Beijing was facing major cities such as traffic congestion and air pollution, so in recent years many major projects have put forward development proposals to reduce the volume. For Beijing. While other cities are busy attracting human resources to develop the city, Beijing is constantly reducing its development scale.
After nearly 10 years of efforts, the population and land for Beijing's urban and rural construction have been reduced for four consecutive years, the construction size has been reduced for three consecutive years, and the proportion of the population living in Permanent in central Beijing fell from 59.3 percent in 2015 to 50.2 percent in 2020.
By 2021, Beijing's GDP will reach 4 trillion yuan, which in just three years achieved a "1 trillion yuan" break, breaking the "city record across China." Also new. In the future, facing new situations and challenges, it is necessary to improve the way the city develops and ranks higher.
