Korea interested in investing in Cambodia's mining sector
(Phnom Penh): Korea has expressed interest in investing in the mining sector in Cambodia and requested Cambodia to launch a more detailed study project on mining potential to find funding as well as other working groups to participate in exploration.
This expression of interest was made during a courtesy call between Mr. Ung Dipola, Director General of the General Department of Mineral Resources, represented by Mr. Suy Sem, Minister of Mines and Energy, and Mr. Lee Hyu Ksang, First Secretary of the Embassy of the Republic of Korea in Cambodia.
The courtesy meeting was held at the Ministry of Mines and Energy last week for the purpose of discussing cooperation in the mining industry between Cambodia and Korea.
Mr. Ing Dipola stated, "In this meeting, the Korean side asked the Cambodian side to make a more detailed study project on the mining potential in Cambodia to the Korean side." "The Korean side will be able to raise funds from partners in Korea to cooperate with the Ministry of Mines and Energy."
He said that by studying since the French era, today Cambodia has discovered some mineral potential, then continue to cooperate with Japan, Korea, China, Czech Republic and Russia, but this cooperation can not be studied. Every location and in-depth information on each mineral potential is clear.
Mr. Ing Dipola said that the Korean side has asked Cambodia to submit a project and the Korean side will submit this project to the Royal Government of Korea to find funding as well as other institutions to participate in exploring the potential of minerals in Cambodia. .
