Sala Kamroeuk Commune Chief Calls on People to Maintain Public Property and Environmental Order
(Siem Reap): Mr. Sam Lon, Chief of Sala Kamroeuk Commune, called on people to take care of public property and environmental order in order to contribute to improving the beauty of Siem Reap as a tourist city.
Mr. Sam Lon, Chief of Sala Kamroeuk Commune, said this on September 19, 2022 during the inauguration ceremony of a 754-meter-long and 4-meter-wide concrete road in Wat Svay Village, Sala Kamroeuk Commune, Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province. This road connects from the south of the main road to the concrete road to Phnom Krom (in front of Wat Svay), which is a fund project of Sala Kamroeuk commune.
Mr. Sam Lon, Chief of Sala Kamroeuk Commune, confirmed that this concrete road is another new achievement in Wat Svay village, which was previously a difficult dirt road, and this new concrete road will facilitate the travel of the general public. In daily travel to their respective occupations, it is easy to transport people's agricultural products to sell in the market, which also facilitates quick and easy travel.
The Sangkat Chief continued that these achievements are the correct development plan of Sala Kamroeuk Sangkat Administration in order to serve the common interests of the people and accelerate local development and strengthen democracy in sub-national administration to improve living standards. Of the people to contribute to poverty reduction.
At the same time, Mr. Sam Lon called on the people living along this road to take care of the achievements of the public interest, maintain order, environment and waste management to contribute to the improvement of the beauty of Siem Reap. Also suitable as a tourist city.
