Senior official of the Royal Government: The country is completely at peace under the leadership of Samdech Techo, who has fulfilled the wishes of the people in both the realm and the realm of Buddhism
The Kan Ben festival is celebrated by Cambodian Buddhists in order to prepare monks for the rainy season because it rains this season, making it difficult for monks to perform Ben Bath. On the other hand, also to dedicate merit to the souls of their ancestors to go to death.
It should be noted that Kan Ben Pchum Ben is a major national Buddhist festival in Cambodia. This year, the Kan Ben-Pchum Ben festival is celebrated from the 1st of Roach to the 15th of Roach, the year of Karl Chatva Sak 2566, which is from the 11th to the 25th of September 2022.
It should be noted that Kan Ben Pchum Ben is a major national Buddhist festival in Cambodia. This year, the Kan Ben Pchum Ben festival is celebrated from the 1st of Roach to the 15th of Roach.
