(Phnom Penh): At around 7 pm on September 11, 2022, a violent incident occurred when one party used a sharp knife to stab the other party at the intersection of Group 15 Road, Bak Kheng Village, Prek Leap Sangkat, Khan Chroy Changvar caused the victim, In Sokthy or Sokthy, alias Mab, 29 years old, to be seriously injured and died on the way to the hospital.
Immediately after the incident, Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang, Deputy Commander of the National Gendarmerie and Commander of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie, issued a strict order to the Phnom Penh Gendarmerie to arrive at the scene. Open an investigation to catch the suspect.
According to the confession of the suspect, Nem Sam Ath said that during 2018-2019 he knew a widow named Ny Sokhom and lived together as a couple without a legal marriage.
Upon arrival, due to disagreement, there was a strong verbal conflict with the family of the ex-husband until the fight immediately, In Sok Thy (victim) rushed to find him. He was holding a sharp knife and hitting the victim, causing him to fall, but he did not know where.
After the incident, he got on a motorcycle, escaped and hid for one night, then continued to escape by car to Battambang province, staying there for one night and one day. At about 23:00 on September 14, 2022, the military police arrived near the Cambodian-Thai border to arrest him.
The above suspects were sent to court by the Phnom Penh Anti-Criminal Police Office to be sent to court for legal proceedings on the morning of September 18, 2022. Today is Ben 9! Discover the history of Pchum Ben and Kan Ben, which are the traditions of the Khmer people
