The National Assembly convened a meeting of the Standing Committee to review four agendas.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of September 19, 2022, the Standing Committee of the National Assembly of Cambodia held a meeting chaired by Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly.
The meeting discussed and approved the agenda with the following results:
1. The Meeting approved the submission of the Draft Law on the Approval of the Fourth Protocol on the Amendment of the ASEAN Comprehensive Investment Agreement to the Committee on Investment Planning, Agriculture, Rural Development, Environment and Water Resources of the National Assembly in cooperation with the Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation and Propaganda Committee. And information of the National Assembly, study and report to the Standing Committee of the National Assembly.
2. The meeting approved the budget plan of the National Assembly in 2023 to be submitted to the Ministry of Economy and Finance to be included in the national budget in accordance with the law on the public financial system.
3. The Meeting approved the draft report on the activities of the National Assembly between the 7th and 8th sessions of the 6th legislature, assigning tasks to the General Secretariat of the National Assembly to continue the activities of the National Assembly until the opening day of the 8th National Assembly session. Upcoming 6th legislature.
4: The meeting approved the draft diplomatic plan of the Cambodian Parliament 2023.
Ministry of Health and GX Foundation Sign Memorandum of Understanding on Cataract Eradication Project
(Phnom Penh): Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, signs a Memorandum of Understanding on the Cataract Eradication Project with the GX Foundation, represented by Mr. Loeung Chung Ying, Vice Chairman of the National Committee of the Council. People's Politics of the People's Republic of China and Chairman of the GX Foundation with the participation of Mr. Wang Wintian, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the People's Republic of China to Cambodia.
The signing of the Memorandum of Understanding on the morning of September 19, 2022 at the Rosewood Hotel was in line with the Belt and Road Initiative and the Cambodia-China Comprehensive Strategic Partnership.
The Minister of Health pointed out that the Memorandum of Understanding on the Project for the Elimination of Cataracts in Prey Veng Province was signed in October 2019 but was delayed due to the spread of Kovid-19 disease. All over the world.
The project includes: 1: Providing a mobile clinic for cataract surgery, equipped with 2 eye surgery equipment, 1 35-seat ambulance, 2: Sending ophthalmologists to further training in the country. China and 3: A team of Chinese doctors will cooperate with Cambodian doctors who have been trained to provide free cataract surgery or other eye problems in Prey Veng.
Minister Mam Bunheng also stressed that "This is the second project and the first project was successfully implemented in Kampong Cham in 2019 under the collaboration between the Ministry of Health and the Asia Foundation for the Prevention of Blindness, sponsored by the Cable Center." "The streets and streets of Hong Kong have undergone cataract surgery for more than 6,000 people free of charge, and they can continue to live happily ever after."
The Minister of Health also thanked the Chinese government and people for providing assistance to the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia, including health infrastructure, human resource development, the provision of medical equipment and the Kovid-19 vaccine. Medical team to contribute to improving health services, especially in preventing the spread of Kovid-19 disease.
He also expressed his deep gratitude to Mr. Wang Wintian, Ambassador of the People's Republic of China to Cambodia, for his facilitation in providing assistance to the Royal Government of Cambodia in the field of health, and Mr. Loeung Chunying, Vice Chairman of the National Committee of the Political Council. The Chinese people will be the chairman of the GX Foundation, as well as all its colleagues and the GX Foundation, which has always supported the Ministry of Health.
On that occasion, Mr. Loeung Chun Ying said, "I am very pleased to sign the Memorandum of Understanding on the Project for the Elimination of Cataracts in Prey Veng now after our fund Succeeded in cataract surgery for 6,200 Cambodians living in Kampong Cham province in the past.
He said that for this project in Prey Veng province, a mobile clinic for cataract surgery, equipped with 2 eye surgery equipment, a 35-seat ambulance will arrive in Cambodia in October 2022. This.
He stressed that his team of doctors will stay with the Cambodian people, not just the eye surgeons for more than 20 minutes, but will continue for three years to help treat or operate on cataracts for all people. Throughout Prey Veng, it is as effective and safe as the people in Kampong Cham who have had more than 6,000 successful surgeries.
He also recalled that on September 18, 2022, he also led his delegation to visit Prey Veng province.
