A man was swept away by a whirlwind while crossing a diversion dam to go fishing in Oddar Meanchey province
(Oddar Meanchey): A man was swept away by a whirlwind while crossing a spillway to catch fish, and the water was so strong that he was swept away by the water. This incident happened at 3 pm on September 18, 2022 at the Khtum diversion point in Khtom village, Kon Kreal commune, Samrong city, Oddar Meanchey province.
According to the description of the woman, her husband, who disappeared from the whirlwind, was named Linh Lek, 52 years old.
The wife said that before the incident, at about 1 pm, her husband was lucky enough to go fishing at the dam, and at about 3 pm, someone came to tell him that her husband had been swept away by the flood.
Immediately after receiving this shocking news, the wife and relatives in the village went to the scene to help find.
After a while, the municipal authorities and the Samrong City Police came down to check the condition of the spillway dam and managed to tie the ropes so that people could not walk through the spillway dam where the water was flowing and sent forces to help, but until 8 o'clock. Tonight, the man who was hit by the tornado has not been found yet.
