The joint statement issued after the EDSCG meeting, which brings together senior diplomats and defense officials of the two allies, reaffirmed the United States' strong commitment to defending South Korea and even stated that Any nuclear attack by North Korea will receive a huge response.
In the statement, the United States expressed its commitment to cooperating with South Korea by deploying and conducting various strategic weapons exercises in the region effectively and in a timely manner to prevent and respond to South Korea. Feet and strengthen local security.
The statement cited joint exercises between the two sides' F-35A fighter jets last July and plans to move the Ronald Reagan aircraft carrier to the Korean Peninsula in the near future, for example. The reality of Washington's commitment.
