BEIJING, Sept. 15 (Xinhua) - The summit of the Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO) held in the historic city of Samakhan, Uzbekistan, on September 15 and 16, 2022, attracted a lot of global attention. Since 2019, since the beginning of the 199 Kovid epidemic, this is the first summit attended by all the leaders of the Shanghai Cooperation Organization.
Moreover, in a context where the world is facing serious challenges in terms of security, politics and economy, the world's attention is focused on the agenda of the talks and the outcome of the summit, which will affect The region and the whole world.
Expansion over the past few years has transformed the Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO) into the largest regional organization covering a vast territory in Asia-Europe, extending to the Middle East and South Asia. Southeast Asia and the Caucasus, accounting for about 40% of the world's population, and member countries' gross domestic product accounts for nearly 30 percent of the world's gross domestic product.
This regional organization has made a significant contribution to global governance through its efforts to maintain security, stability and strengthen socio-economic development in its region, and has expanded cooperation with observer countries and dialogue partners. And work closely with the United Nations and other regional and international organizations to address global challenges and strengthen global security, stability and development.
With its expansion to include the world's major oil producers such as Russia, Saudi Arabia and Iran, which represent more than half of the world's annual oil production, the organization is expected to play an increasingly important role in Ensuring global energy stability is a major global challenge today.
In other words, the organization adheres to the principles of openness, environment and transparency, focusing on equal partnership, mutual respect, mutual benefit, rejecting the old stereotype of the relationship. International is a game of winners and losers filled with confrontation as enemies.
In the current context of the world facing serious political and economic security challenges, it is expected that the Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO), with its growing political and economic influence, will act as a strong pillar that sustains the maintenance of stability and development. The world's social economy and the building of a polar and equitable world order.
