Xi Jinping stressed that China has made great efforts to facilitate the fight against and prevent the spread of Kovid 19 with socio-economic development. A strong driving force for global economic recovery and will continue to provide greater market opportunities to all countries.
Xi Jinping added that in another month, we will hold the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China. We will strive to achieve the restoration of a prosperous Chinese nation through Chinese modernization, continue to actively promote the establishment of a common destiny of humanity, so that China's new development brings new opportunities to the world. Contribute to the preservation of peace, global progress, as well as the advancement of human civilization.
Speaking from Uzbekistan at the summit of the China-Russia security-political-economic body, Xi said all SCO members should support each other's efforts. To protect the interests of security and development, respectively.
He added that China will train 2,000 law enforcement officers from SCO member countries for the next five years and set up a training base focusing on combat work. Counter-terrorism.
Xi also invited member states to participate in China's Global Security Initiative, a concept he first proposed in April, including the principle that No country should strengthen its security based on the destruction of other countries' security.
New Delhi and Moscow have had long-standing ties since the Cold War, and Russia continues to be India's largest arms supplier. However, in the first face-to-face meeting since Moscow invaded Ukraine in February this year, Modi told Putin bluntly: "Your Excellency, I know that now is not the time for war." .
The Indian Prime Minister also stressed the importance of using diplomacy and dialogue to resolve issues. However, New Delhi did not openly condemn Moscow for invading Ukraine, despite efforts by the United States to persuade it to do so.
In response, Putin told Modi: "I understand your position as well as your concerns over the conflict in Ukraine. "We will do our best to end the conflict as soon as possible." But Putin added that Ukrainian leaders had rejected the talks and wanted to achieve their goals by military means.
