Under the happy atmosphere of the Cambodian people celebrating the Pchum Ben season, Mr. Hun Many said that when he was a child, he remembered that when it was time to bake Ansam cakes, he always helped to scratch the palm of his grandmother, but today Participated in packing by yourself, just realized that it is not really easy to wrap each cake, starting from the preparation of ingredients in order, when packing, when tying, when cooking and care.
At the same time, he expressed his happiness and appreciation to the organizing team of "Pchum Ben: Let's go and bake Ansam cake together" which organized a program under the atmosphere of Pchum Ben. This atmosphere and the opportunity to meet lovers of Khmer culture like this is really happy and rarely seen.
This program is held to commemorate and create memories, increase friendship, solidarity, inspire, participate in preserving the traditions and customs of the younger generation, as well as create opportunities for the reunion of the Khmer family on the occasion of Kan Ben. At the same time, there is also sharing of Khmer baking methods and traditional Khmer entertainment programs to the participants.
Please be informed that Cambodians usually bake cakes, cakes and pastries during the Pchum Ben festival because it is an opportunity to meet relatives and children, especially in the provinces where Cambodians often visit their hometowns to reunite with their families and grandparents. Bake these cakes to receive offspring. At the base and in each house, the boys always help as a force, while the girls always help the grandmother in packing and cooking these cakes.
