(Battambang): The National Bank of Cambodia continues to promote the campaign of the use of the riel in the provinces to promote the actual use of the riel on September 16, 2022, the National Bank of Cambodia campaign to promote the use of the riel in Battambang province.
Riel Promotion Campaign in Battambang Province, with the participation of Ms. Chea Serey, Deputy Governor and Technical Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia.
Ms. Chea Serey praised and appreciated the participation of all people in Battambang province in promoting the actual use of the riel, the revenue and expenditure in riel of the operation of banking and financial institutions in Battambang province should increase Note:
She said that according to previous studies, 80% of daily expenses in Battambang are made in riel.
Ms. Chea Serey added, "Revenues and expenses of operations of banking and financial institutions in Battambang in riel have increased significantly. In the last two decades, the riel in circulation has increased by 16 percent, deposits in riel by 29 percent and loans in riel by an average of 38 percent per year.
Please be informed that the results of the survey of the National Bank of Cambodia in cooperation with the Japan International Cooperation Agency in 2017 showed that the riel has gained more trust and use, especially for daily expenses, and in rural areas, the riel. Primary and comprehensive role in life.
Mr. Uy Sotheavy, Deputy Governor of Battambang Province, said that the spending of Riel in Battambang Province by the people is very proud, especially the daily expenses such as food, drink, clothes and travel, even though Battambang is a province. Attractive tourism for foreign tourists, which brings a lot of foreign currency revenue.
The Deputy Governor of Battambang Province encouraged people and enterprises to use the riel instead of foreign currency more because the riel is the currency of our nation.
Ministry of Posts inspects telecommunication services in priority tourist areas, protected areas and remote areas in Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): On September 16, 2022, Mr. So Visothy, Secretary of State, led the Inter-Ministerial Working Group and Telecommunication Operators to inspect telecommunication service quality improvement sites in priority tourist areas, protected areas and remote areas in Siem Reap Province. .
This work is done in accordance with the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and in accordance with the mechanism of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, which established a working group to improve the quality of services in five regions in May 2021.
This inspection to study, understand and determine the location for the installation of telephone antennas in 7 locations in Siem Reap, including Angkor, Kampong Phluk resort, Changkarn Roi, Kbal Spean waterfall, Khnar Po, Wat Pheng, which is a priority tourist destination after the inter-ministerial working group organized Meeting with Siem Reap Provincial Administration on September 15 yesterday.
The purpose of the meeting was to discuss the key points to build mobile antenna towers and internet connection to expand the scope of service coverage in priority tourist destinations, protected areas and remote areas in Siem Reap. .
For Siem Reap Province, the fourth area, the inter-ministerial working group and relevant institutions will inspect and study the quality of telecommunication services from 15 to 19 September 2022 according to the location and date set for 7 targets of the temple area. And targeting some other priority eco-tourism communities.
Mr. Pin Prak, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap, expressed his support and close cooperation at all times and hoped that soon the tourist areas in Siem Reap will have access to quality telephone and internet services everywhere.
Mr. Pin Prak noted that so far in many areas in Siem Reap, some of the main targets of the province are difficult or impossible to communicate through the Internet, such as at some points of the provincial administration at the district hall. Banteay Srei, Angkor Thom District Hall, Run Ta Ek Natural Village Area, etc. Poor or no service, difficult to communicate.
Mr. Xanareth, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications and Chairman of Area 4, reminded all service providers to strengthen technical work to avoid indifference and lack of quality of customer service can be subject to transaction penalties.
He claimed that according to the "Prakas on the quality of telecommunications services", telecom operators have 10 (ten) months to improve and enhance the quality of their telecommunications services in case any telecom operators do not comply with the minimum standards set out in this prakas. The telecom operator will be fined, so the relevant telecom operators should cooperate to implement more effectively.
