The case of beating students at Hun Sen Sereypheap School in Takhmao City has been resolved, the school principal and the parents of the students reconciled peacefully
(Phnom Penh): The case of the principal of Hun Sen Sereypheap High School, Takhmao City, Kandal Province, beating a female student and causing a reaction of criticism and support from public opinion, now the school and the guardians have reconciled by both parties Accept mistakes and make suggestions from each other in a peaceful way.
It should be informed that a few days ago, a video was shared on social media about the activities of the principal of Hun Sen Sereypheap High School in Takhmao City beating a female student. This case has caused reactions, criticism and support from the public, leading to research by the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
"On the morning of September 16, 2022, the management of Hun Sen Sereypheap High School in Kandal province met with parents and relevant students to facilitate reconciliation," Ros Sovacha, spokesman for the Ministry of Education, told Fresh News earlier. "Again."
Mr. Ros Sovacha said that the above compromise was very fruitful as follows:
First, parents acknowledge the guilt of their children and stop being angry and have no intention of suing the director. Parents and guardians of students have requested that principals and journalists refrain from releasing information that intentionally alleges that the students were misbehaving, causing the students or their children to be discredited and damaged. .
Second, parents and guardians of students request that there be no intentional or unintentional abuse and burden on students.
Third, the principal accepted the request to improve and ask for forgiveness for his awkward actions on students. General Department of Customs of Cambodia and Hong Kong Customs Administration join hands to strengthen cooperation and mutual assistance
