(Phnom Penh): Four former military officers who shot and killed their fiancé, a medical student and escaped for more than two years, were arrested in Thailand and sent to the National Police on the night of the 15th. September 2022 to interrogate and continue the procedure after receiving from the Thai side.
After questioning at the Internal Security Department, the perpetrator, 28-year-old Yeun Van Det (former military officer), was handed over to the Criminal Police Department for further proceedings and will be sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on 16 September. 2022 tomorrow.
Authorities said the assailant who shot the fiancée was a four-year-old military officer named Yeun Van Det, and that the source of the shooting was initially suspected to be jealous.
One year ago, there were at least two separate shootings by Thai soldiers. And in 2020, a catastrophic incident in which a Thai soldier shot and killed 29 people in a 17-hour attack left many wounded before the suspect was shot dead by special forces.
