Zillanam Co., Ltd., together with its member companies and the Cambodian Association of Appraisers and Realtors, has announced a partnership with government agencies to raise awareness and contribute to the development of the securities and banking sector, a new potential sector. To support economic growth in Cambodia.
Speaking at the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding on September 16, 2022, Mr. Kuy Vat, Chairman of the Board of Directors of Zillanam Ek Co., Ltd., said that the current cooperation is an effort to promote Understand the securities and governance sector to the public, capacity building, sharing knowledge and skills and attracting investment in both sectors.
He added that the real estate sector has a deep relationship with the stock market and the securities and banking sectors, and the growth of the two sectors will complement each other's growth for the real estate sector.
Mr. Sok Dara, Director General of the Governance Regulatory Authority, said that after the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding, the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia and the Regulatory Authority will start working with private companies through training and awareness raising mechanisms.
Chrek Soknim, president of the Cambodian Association of Appraisers and Realtors, said the memorandum of understanding was another new mechanism to pave the way for financial solutions to real estate investment.
Zillan Trust, a company that provides alternative asset management services for joint ventures in Cambodia, was licensed by the Regulatory Authority in 2022 and is part of Zillan Group's 30 ecosystems. .
Cambodian Investment Capital Partner M.C. was licensed by the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia in 2019 as a fund management company.
He added, "This new sector will be a solution, especially for foreigners, individuals or companies who want to buy real estate legally in Cambodia through the government, and today's cooperation will contribute to the development of the sector. Securities and governance, as well as contributing to the diversification of the financial sector in Cambodia.
The Board of Trustees acts as the custodian and administrator of the property without the right to resell it, even if the land or house is the property of the company, and the Board of Trustees is required to register with the Board of Trustees, as these mechanisms are more complex. Provide high confidence to investors, especially foreign investors who come to invest in Cambodia.
The Regulatory Authority is a regulatory authority overseeing and developing the banking sector in Cambodia and was established under the Law on the Organization and Functioning of the Non-Banking Financial Services Authority, which was promulgated in January 2021. To date, 52 public administrators have been registered with the public administration.
(Ratanakkiri): The assailant who raped and killed an 18-year-old Tampoun girl in Samaki commune, O'Chum district, Ratanakkiri province, was arrested by the police on September 16, 2022 after acting on the 14th. September 2022.
Brigadier General Phen Dina, Deputy Commissioner for Criminal Planning, told Fresh News that after receiving the information, the specialized police force, in cooperation with the O'Chum District Inspector Force and the Samaki Commune Administration Police Force, arrived at the scene to examine the body and find it. That the victim was raped and killed.
The victim's family confirmed that on September 13, 2022 (one day before the incident), he saw the victim girl chatting on the phone, but did not know where to chat's. The victim disappeared until nightfall and did not see the girl return home. On the morning of September 14, 2022, he called the victim, but the call did not come in until 20:30, when his daughter's body was found.
Brigadier General Phen Dina further stated that after the specialized force searched until 3:30 pm on September 16, 2022, the suspect named Seng Kosal, 36 years old, a doctor, was born in the village. Svay Ming, Ampil Tapok commune, Ou Raing Ov district, Tbong Khmum province, currently staying at the scene.
During the operation, the specialized police force confiscated a motorcycle (motorcycle for action). The suspect is currently being held at the Ratanakkiri Provincial Police Office of Serious Crimes to complete a referral to the provincial court for further proceedings.
