(Banteay Meanchey): A former boxing coach who was falling ill and living in poverty received a gift from General Ke Kim Yan, Deputy Prime Minister, Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group in Banteay Meanchey Province. Mrs. Mao Malay Ke Kim Yan.
This donation was made by Mr. Sithi Loh, Permanent Member of the Provincial Party Committee and Chairman of the Svay Chek District Assistance Team on September 16, 2022, accompanied by Mr. Sreng Sophal, Governor of Serey Sophorn City and the working group in Dey Lot Village, Teuk Thla Sangkat. Serei Sophorn City.
Former boxing coach Chan Pov, 74, was a boxing coach from 1993 to 2012. Mr. Chan Pov, after a lucrative boxing career, resigned and went to work as a construction worker and fisherman to support his family. He then fell ill with diabetes, high blood pressure and had no money for treatment.
On that occasion, Mr. Sithy Loh instructed Mr. Chan Pov to continue to live hygienically and take good care of his health and go for regular treatment. These gifts can facilitate his daily eating. And a hundred families as well. He said that the leaders of the Cambodian People's Party and the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen did not let a citizen die of starvation.
Mr. Chan Pov and his wife also expressed their excitement and gratitude to the leaders of the Cambodian People's Party, Special Authorities, Mr. Sithi Loh and the team who brought these gifts to his house at the same time. There is a severe shortage of livelihood.
