China's Public Security Bureau Strengthens International Law Enforcement Cooperation to Fight Cyber Fraud
BEIJING (Reuters) - Cybercrime is on the rise, with telecommunications and cybercrime scams becoming a global public scourge. China's public security bureau continues to strengthen cooperation on the implementation of international law and promote the crackdown on cybercrime. Internet telecom fraud is a common transnational crime.
From March to June 2022, the Chinese Public Security Bureau and the police departments of 76 member states of the International Criminal Police Organization (ICPO) participated in anti-fraud operations, destroying 1,770 crime sites in several countries and intercepting them. Seized more than $ 50 million in illegal funds.
Relevant officials of the Chinese Ministry of Public Security said that cooperating in the fight against cross-border Internet telecommunications fraud is the joint responsibility of all national police authorities. China's public security bureau will implement anti-cyber fraud laws, further strengthen cooperation, enforce international law, and crack down on telecommunications and cyber fraud crimes.
