Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Chairs the 7th Meeting of Governors on the Cambodia-Thailand Border to Strengthen Cooperation
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of September 16, 2022, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the Cambodian Delegation, co-chaired the 7th Cambodia-Thailand Border Governors Meeting. Video at the invitation of General Anupong Pao Chenda, Minister of Interior of Thailand.
After the meeting, the two sides issued a joint statement saying that the meeting was conducted in an atmosphere of friendship, solidarity, brotherhood and mutual understanding. Both sides recognize the importance of close relations and cooperation between the provinces bordering Cambodia and Thailand and are willing to maintain peace, friendship, cooperation and sustainable development between the two countries.
The meeting highly valued the strengthening of cooperation between the provinces bordering Cambodia and Thailand on 18 areas of comprehensive cooperation.
* First: Cooperation in the implementation of the border crossing agreement: The two sides agreed to continue educating and disseminating to the people and the competent authorities in the border areas to effectively and fully implement the agreement between the Royal Government. Cambodia and the Royal Government of Thailand on the border crossing between the two countries.
* Second: Cooperation in controlling border crossings during the Kovid-19 epidemic: Both sides encourage the relevant institutions of the two countries to increase coordination on cross-border procedures and measures, including measures. Public health to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 and other infectious diseases aims to facilitate cross-border travel and reopen other border gates that have not yet been opened.
* Third: Cooperation on trade and investment along the border: Both sides stressed the importance of promoting and facilitating cross-border trade and economic activities between Banteay Meanchey-Sa Kaeo and Koh Kong-Trat provinces. In addition, the two sides agreed to cooperate and coordinate trade and commerce activities in the Cambodian-Thai border area to promote the sustainability and prosperity of the people living in the border provinces of the two countries.
* Fourth: Cooperation in the field of transportation: Both sides support the relevant institutions of the two countries to reconsider the negotiation of the bilateral agreement on land transport across the border between Cambodia and Thailand to promote Connect transport between the two countries.
* Fifth: Cooperation on agriculture in the border area: Both sides encourage the border provinces of the two countries to facilitate cross-border trade in agricultural products of people living along the border. The two sides agreed to continue cooperating on sanitation and phytosanitary work, controlling animal and plant disease outbreaks, cooperating on capacity building, information exchange and research and development.
Sixth, industrial cooperation: The two sides agreed to strengthen industrial cooperation to provide support to investors of the two countries to invest, open factories in the border provinces of the two countries and encourage Exchange visits between officials and industry experts to share best practices and knowledge.
Seventh: Cooperation in the field of labor: The two sides agreed to support the relevant ministries, institutions and officials of the two countries to facilitate the workers of the two countries to use the border card for daily and seasonal work in the region. Boundaries.
8th: Cooperation in the management of border gates: Both sides welcomed the official opening of the Phnom Dey International Border Gate (Battambang Province) - Ban Kawdin (Sa Kaeo Province) in 2018 and welcomed the closure. Completed the construction of the Cambodia-Thailand Stung Bot-Ban Nong Ean Friendship Bridge in 2019.
Both sides also encouraged the relevant institutions to cooperate closely to open the Stung Bot International Border Gate (Banteay Meanchey Province) - Ban Nong Ean (Sa Kaeo Province) as soon as possible.
The two sides also agreed to examine the possibility of upgrading the Chakkarka border checkpoint (Battambang province) - Ban Mak Muong (Trat province) to an international border gate. In addition, both sides encouraged the relevant authorities of the two countries to conduct detailed measurements in Prey Chan village, Banteay Meanchey province and Non Mak Muon village, Sa Kaeo province to establish a new border gate.
In addition, both sides agreed not to close the border gate unilaterally. The closure of any border gate should be made with clear reasons and as necessary and with the consent of the relevant authorities of both countries.
Ninth: Cooperation in the field of public health and community development: Both sides agreed to encourage the exchange of study visits or organize seminars or conferences to share knowledge and experience and progress on health services.
Tenth: Disaster Management Cooperation: Both sides agreed to explore the possibility of establishing a Memorandum of Understanding on Emergency Relief and Disaster Response.
Eleventh: Illegal logging cooperation: Both sides praised the provincial authorities and the competent forces in the border provinces of the two countries for educating people not to lose the habit of illegal logging. Laws in the border areas and in the implementation of measures to prevent and crack down on illegal logging in a timely manner.
Twelfth: Cooperation on environmental protection of the border: Both sides agreed to assign the provinces bordering Cambodia and Thailand to strengthen cooperation to take care of the environment, including improving the management of solid and liquid wastes. Along the border.
* 14th: Demining Cooperation: The two sides agreed to continue cooperating to facilitate humanitarian demining operations in areas along the border in order to fulfill their obligations under Article 5 of the Convention on the Prohibition of the Use of Anti-Personnel Mines. .
15th: Tourism Cooperation: Both sides agreed on the development of joint tourism routes under the theme "Two Kingdoms, One Goal" and supported the development of tourism links between the coastal provinces of Cambodia and the eastern provinces. Thailand.
16th: Cooperation of sister provinces / cities: Encourage joint activities to promote better and more sustainable sister city partnerships. As good neighbors, both sides agree to work together, strengthen joint commitment to the protection and preservation of cultural heritage, and work closely to promote public awareness, mutual understanding and respect. The return of each culture and national identity.
* 17th: Provincial and local cooperation mechanisms: Both sides encourage the governors of the border provinces and the leaders of the administrations of the border districts of the two countries to co-organize regular meetings by taking turns to host. According to the agreement between the governors of the border provinces of the two countries.
* 18th: Activities: Both sides expressed their congratulations on the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between the two countries in 2020, which organized many celebrations throughout the year.
