In the press conference of the Spokesperson of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the theme "Achievements in 5 years of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation" this morning, September 16, 2022, Mr. Sin Chanserivutha, Under Secretary of State and Spokesman of the Secretariat of Aviation Civilians claim that so far the Mondulkiri airport development project is still idle.
"As a result of the Kovid 19 crisis, the Chinese company suffered heavy losses and he said he could not afford to continue investing," he said.
According to Mr. Sin Chanserivutha, due to the construction project in connection with the National Economic and Tourism Development Commission, the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation requested three principles to the Ministry of Economy and Finance after the company was unable to get the development. Continuing its work, including:
* First: Examine the feasibility of using the state budget to use on this construction process * Second: Examine the feasibility of using concessional loans from the World Bank or the Asian Development Bank * Third: Find other private partners to study the feasibility of construction .
He added that in response, the Ministry of Economy has suggested exploring the possibility of finding investment partners to build an airport in the northeastern province. So far, three foreign private companies have come to negotiate with the Royal Government of Cambodia, but not yet officially.
Mr. Sin Chanserivutha claims that the development project of Mondulkiri Airport is still on the agenda of the Royal Government of Cambodia, demanding time to find new investors.
Please be informed that the Royal Government has given the right to China Power to build the airport development project in Mondulkiri province. Mondulkiri Airport is planned to be built on an area of 300 hectares, about 20 kilometers from Sen Monorom, with an estimated investment of more than $ 80 million.
