Here is the full text of the Ministry of Health: Europe to increase diesel imports from the Middle East and Asia to replace Russian oil (Video inside) (London): Europe is turning to suppliers outside Russia Increasing demand for its diesel, with imports of this type of fuel, is reaching a three-year high this month. According to Reuters.
The data also showed that diesel imports from Russia accounted for 44% of the total since the beginning of September so far, down from 51% for the whole of August and 60% for the whole month. July.
At the same time, Europe's share of diesel imports from the Middle East rose to 30 percent, up from 23 percent in August.
Diesel imports from the Middle East for the whole of September are expected to increase by about 50 percent from August to 500,000 barrels a day, the highest level since the month, Reuters reported. May 2018.
Imports from Asia are expected to remain stable at about 225,000 barrels a day in September from August, but three times higher than in July and close to the highest level ever seen, the data showed. In November last year.
The European Union (EU) will stop buying all Russian crude oil by sea from early December this year and will ban all Russian refined products within two months in protest of the city's aggression. Moscow on Ukraine. According to Reuters.
