Kampong Thom Fisheries Administration District Leads Operation to Prevent and Suppress Tonle Sap Lake Fishing Crimes
(Kampong Thom): Kampong Thom Fisheries Administration District led the prevention and suppression of illegal fishing in Tonle Sap Lake, Kampong Thom Province, which overfished and used large-scale fishing gear.
This operation took place on September 15, 2022, led by Mr. Chin Sitha, Director of Kampong Thom Fisheries Administration, in cooperation with the Provincial and District Unity Command.
Mr. Hourn Phal, Chief of Peam Bang Fisheries Administration Sangkat, led the working group to implement the order to prevent and crack down on illegal fishing in Tonle Sap Lake in Peam Bang commune, Stong district. In Peam Bang commune, Stong district, Kampong Thom province.
In order to prevent and suppress the crime of fishing in Tonle Sap Lake in Peam Bang commune, the result was that 1 case was implemented and the evidence of fishing offenses was destroyed on the spot, including 3 nets, 600 m long nets, 8 nets. Meatballs, 5 nets, 450 wooden poles, fish no longer enter the natural lake, weighing 10 kg.
It should be noted that the working group for the implementation of regulations to prevent and crack down on fishing offenses in the Tonle Sap Lake stands at Phat Sanday commune, Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province, and is stationed today due to bad weather. Inspected "Bing Chheng International Entertainment Co., Ltd." related to illegal business case and some other crimes.
