(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian-Cambodian Bar Association, the Cambodian Ambassador to Malaysia, and the Norodom Bopha Devi Dance School recently met to discuss cooperation in bringing artists to Malaysia for the traditional drama. Jayavarman VII and Indra Devi "to perform in Malaysia during the Cambodian Independence Day, which takes place on November 7, 2022.
Wednesday's discussion focused on supporting artists' travel, accommodation, transportation, materials and stage fit. As a result, all parties have a clear understanding of each other and have expressed a willingness to participate in promoting national culture to the world.
Preparations to lead a large group of 74 artists to perform the traditional drama "Jayavarman VII" in Malaysia after the event was a great success.
"On that occasion, we will also promote the good policy of the Royal Government to attract foreign investment to Cambodia, because the performance of the traditional drama" King Jayavarman VII and "Indra Devi" was also attended by various embassy officials as well as major investors in Malaysia.
"This program will be supported by relevant institutions, including the Asia-Cambodia Bar Association and other partners," she added.
Mr. Choy Vichet, Cambodian Ambassador to Malaysia, said that the Cambodian Embassy in Malaysia will organize a celebration of the independence of the Kingdom of Cambodia in Malaysia on November 7, 2022.
He expressed his pleasure to meet with the Cambodian Asian Lawyers Association to bring a group of Cambodian artists to perform in Malaysia on this occasion in order to promote and promote national culture to the world and help promote the attraction. Tourists to visit Cambodia more and more.
The Embassy plans to invite a total of 400-500 senior diplomats, senior officials from the Ministry of State of Malaysia and the Malaysian and Cambodian business communities to attend the Cambodian Independence Day celebrations in November.
