Mr. Hor Sarun made this statement at the opening ceremony of the workshop on "Reducing the Poverty of People with Disabilities by Promoting Employment Growth in Tourism", co-organized by the Ministry of Persons with Disabilities Action Team. Tourism and General Secretariat of the Council for the Disabled, Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation in Stung Treng Province on September 16, 2022.
"As a signatory to the Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities and the Rights of Persons with Disabilities, Cambodia regularly pays attention to the promotion of the disability sector in response to progress in all areas," the senior official said. Under the shadow of peace and wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The disability sector has become a priority for the Royal Government of Cambodia, with great emphasis on all sectors, including education, health, tourism, employment and vocational access to social protection, life, culture, entertainment, sports and more. "Gender in the sense of ensuring that people with disabilities have access to opportunities and incentives to receive development values and full recognition in society."
He said that what is remarkable is the arrangement of infrastructure to help people with disabilities in public places, buildings, public and private institutions, from parking lots to walkways, ramps into buildings, bathrooms and so on. In addition, there is a limit on the recruitment of people with disabilities to work at the rate of 1% of the total number of workers in the private sector and 2% in government ministries and institutions.
Mr. Hor Sarun added that in the context of the global epidemic of Kovid 19, the fight against Kovid 19 in Cambodia was directed and launched by the Samdech directly. The Prime Minister, who has made Cambodia one of the leading countries in the world, has managed to control the spread of Kovid-19 and strengthened community immunity through the "Blossom" vaccination strategy.
