Minister Vong Soth: UNICEF Commits to Support and Strengthen Cooperation with the Royal Government of Cambodia to Prevent All Forms of Violence Against Children
(Phnom Penh): Minister Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, commended and commended the Steering Committee for the Implementation of the Action Plan for the Prevention and Response to Violence against Children and the Technical Working Group for leading and reviewing the report. Evaluate a responsible action plan based on criteria and a clear basis.
He said the action plan evaluation report will be an important reference in the development of relevant plans and the introduction of specific strategies to prevent and respond to violence against children more effectively to achieve the Sustainable Development Goals. 2030 to end violence against children.
Mr. Vong Soth made the remarks while presiding over the launch of the 2017-2021 Action Plan for the Prevention and Response to Violence Against Children, attended by the leadership of the Ambassador of Japan and UNICEF President. Partner organizations, relevant institutions and more than 200 civil servants on September 16, 2022.
Ms. Furofu Yozat, UNICEF Country Director for Cambodia, congratulated the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation for drafting this important child protection law and providing a solid foundation for strengthening the child protection system. In the future, in accordance with the principles of the United Nations Convention on the Rights of the Child.
She also pledged to support and strengthen cooperation with the Royal Government of Cambodia, development partners, civil society organizations and communities in the implementation of the VAC Action Plan to continue and develop a new action plan 2024-2028 to ensure the protection of all children from all forms of abuse. Violence.
In addition, Minister Vong Soth emphasized that the Royal Government of Cambodia has ratified the International Convention on the Rights of the Child and additional protocols, as well as international agreements to protect the best interests of children.
At the same time, the "Cambodia Protest" strategy, co-initiated by UNICEF, is a communication strategy to raise awareness by ensuring that families are a safe and optimal environment for the growth and development of children. One of the activities of the "Strong Family" campaign to end violence against children and the unnecessary separation of children from their families.
Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, made good recommendations as a priority to strengthen the effective implementation of relevant action plans and requested UNICEF Cambodia and other development partners to further strengthen cooperation with relevant ministries and institutions. On the preparation of action plans to prevent and respond to violence against children in 2024-2028 in the future.
