Turkish ambassador vows to boost direct flights to Cambodia
The pledge was made during a courtesy call by Ms. Ul Kuko Jae Fei with Minister of Tourism Thong Khon on the afternoon of September 15, 2022 at the Ministry of Tourism after she received her new mission as Ambassador of the Republic of Turkey to Cambodia. .
Minister Thong Khon briefed the Ambassador on the gradual recovery of Cambodia's tourism situation through efforts by the Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to restore and promote tourism during the Kovid 19 crisis. Sen Prime Minister. This has prompted Cambodia to receive nearly 1 million international visitors (an increase of 720%) by the first eight months of 2022.
According to Minister Thong Khon, the Cambodian-Turkish side agreed to promote the implementation of the tourism agreement, which was signed in Turkey in 2018 and has already set up a working group to implement it. Effective, fruitful and mutually beneficial.
At this point, Minister Thong Khon added that the agreement on tourism is focused on promoting mutual tourism movement, especially the connection of direct flights between Cambodia and Turkey.
"During her tenure in Cambodia, the Turkish ambassador has promised to achieve a direct Cambodia-Turkey direct flight connection, because in order to boost tourism, transportation is needed," he said.
The minister claimed that Phnom Penh, Siem Reap and Sihanoukville international airports are now able to land large aircraft, so landing from Turkey is not a problem.
In addition, the agreement also focuses on encouraging investors in the tourism sector, while Turkey is a large investor, and Cambodia-Turkey must continue to train human resources in tourism, exchange visits between officials of the two countries.
