Samdech Techo Hun Sen urges ASEAN-China to reduce trade barriers to expand the scope of economic cooperation (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and ASEAN Chair, urged ASEAN and China to expand Broader and deeper economic cooperation. In particular, focus on reducing barriers to trade in goods, services and investment.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's request was made during the opening remarks at the 19th China-ASEAN Expo via video. The China-ASEAN Expo 2022 is held under the theme "Sharing New Opportunities Gained from the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (APEC) to Build a New China-ASEAN Free Trade Area 3.0."
In his opening remarks, Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted that ASEAN-China economic cooperation has achieved many fruitful achievements since the signing of the Framework Agreement on Comprehensive Economic Cooperation between ASEAN and China. China in 2002 and the signing of trade and investment agreements.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that ASEAN and China need to pay more attention to expanding the scope of economic cooperation between ASEAN and China to expand and deepen, focusing on reducing trade barriers. Services and investments. In addition, promote the development of the digital economy, green growth and capacity building of small and medium enterprises (SMEs).
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also expressed confidence that the implementation of the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (AEC) in 2022 will bring many trade and investment opportunities for countries in the region and contribute significantly to the promotion. To economic growth. In particular, it will be the "core framework" for the upcoming ASEAN-China Free Trade Area Form 3.0.
As the chair of ASEAN for 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced that Cambodia will continue to work to strengthen ASEAN cooperation with China to ensure the sustainability, environment and resilience of socio-economic development in both regions.
In his opening remarks, the Prime Minister of Cambodia also highlighted the social and economic developments in the aftermath of the Kovid 19 crisis.
ASEAN-China is a major trading partner in the region. In 2021, the trade volume between ASEAN and China will reach nearly 9 billion US dollars. Of that, China exported nearly 5 billion US dollars to ASEAN and imported nearly 4 billion US dollars from ASEAN.
Chinese investment in ASEAN is over 14 billion US dollars and ASEAN investment in China is over 10 billion US dollars.
