Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration clarifies the case of a Vietnamese woman who posted a video that she was detained for work
(Preah Sihanouk): Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration on September 15, 2022 said that recently, some social media and media have shared a video clip of a Vietnamese woman (speaking Khmer). Posted that he was detained to work for a company in Sihanoukville.
According to the source of the report on the results of the police investigation, on August 29, 2022 at 13:00, the specialized force of Sihanoukville Provincial Police visited the location where the woman posted the video clip. He was detained to work for the company in Village 4, Sangkat 4, Sihanoukville.
With the cooperation of the owner, the police found the Vietnamese woman and brought her and a male Chinese manager to the Sihanoukville Provincial Police for questioning.
After the interrogation, he worked for three companies in Sihanoukville, the other two companies did not have any problems with him, but in the third company, the company has strict working conditions, requiring him to work. Many hours from 14 to 15 hours a day.
By the third company above, when he first started working, the company told him that he had to work for 6 months before he could apply for termination. When he worked for almost 3 months, the company asked him to sign a new contract in writing with the company for another 6 months, which made him dissatisfied.
Later, the Vietnamese woman received the news that her mother was ill. She asked the company to stop working, but the company refused, so she complained to the authorities to help her get out of the company.
And the video clip in which he said he saw a Chinese man in a company with a handgun was not true, and he had never seen a Chinese man with a firearm, he just overheard the source. Clear.
When he made the video clip, he was scared and worried, so he cried because the company did not restrain and beat him. And the reason he did this was because he wanted the authorities to get him out of the company as soon as possible because he wanted to return to his home country to see his sick mother.
At the same time, the provincial administration calls on the media and social media users to stop disseminating and sharing misinformation that is different from what actually happened, which confuses the public.
