(Kampong Speu): Police Chief of Treng Trayeung Police Station, Phnom Sruoch District, Kampong Speu Province, Mr. Sem Vudy, was accused of beating and torturing a deaf suspect after handcuffing him and taking him to the Treng Troyeung Administrative Police Station in the middle of the night. Deaf people throw stones at the roof of an online cockfighting game.
She said the throw was because the cockfighting venue was buzzing, disturbing her family's sleep every night. After his son threw stones, at 10:30 pm, four policemen in a red Highlander arrived home and handcuffed his son, who pushed him into a car and took him to the police station. Treng is gone.
When he was taken to the police station, the police chief and his children punched his son in the face with many hands, handcuffed him, causing him to fall to the ground and lift him up, forcing him to give a thumbs up to end the story. Released home at 12:30 pm the same day.
The deaf mother also confirmed that when she arrived home, she saw her son's face swollen, bruised and cracked. At that time, his son told the story of the police chief and his accomplices who beat and tortured him while he was handcuffed.
He said that his son only threw stones at the roof of the house, not to the point of handcuffing and not to torture, and that his son was also disabled. He asked for justice for his disabled son by making the post chief of Treng Trayeung commune responsible for this, and also asked the authorities to crack down on all kinds of gambling that is playing a dirty game, shouting and disturbing. Citizens sleep at night as well.
In relation to this indictment, Mr. Sem Woody said by telephone on September 15, 2022 that he had not beaten or tortured because he also knew that the man who was detained was not physically fit. (C) But what he took was to make a contract to stop doing so, as such activities have happened many times.
