(Pursat): 79 vulnerable fishing families on September 15, 2022 received humanitarian donations from Pursat Provincial Red Cross Branch through Mr. Chiao Tay, Governor of Pursat Provincial Board of Governors and Chairman of Branch Committee to facilitate To the hardships of daily life.
The humanitarian assistance ceremony was held at Suy Sem Kanhchor Primary School, located in Kanhchor Commune, Kandieng District, Pursat Province, with the participation of Mr. and Mrs. Government Officials, Provincial Red Cross Branch Committee, Commune / District and Provincial Authorities.
Mr. Chiao Tai said that seeing the hardships of the people, the CRC Sub-Branch of Kandieng District went directly to the base and reported to the Provincial Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross only today on behalf of the Branch Honorary Committee and Branch Committee. In collaboration with the sub-branch, we have organized to provide humanitarian donations to 79 families now.
He said that all these activities are highly recommended by Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who always thinks of the suffering of the people at all times without leaving anyone to suffer. Because we did not think that.
At the same time, he brought a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who always thinks about the suffering of the people at all times, without letting anyone suffer because we did not think about it. No.
Taking that opportunity, the provincial governor advised the people to be self-conscious in making a living, because these gifts are a one-time solution, not a daily or monthly regime. We need to share this humanitarian gift across the province because of the high vulnerability.
In addition, he called on all people to take care of their health to live well, there will be enough time to make a living, so to maintain good hygiene, clean living, clean homes, eat clean. Drink clean regularly and prevent various diseases such as Kovid, because this disease has not gone away yet, please be very careful, do not neglect it.
It should be noted that the humanitarian donation of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Pursat Province provides to the 79 families who are fishermen from 4 villages: Prek Trabek Village, Luong Road, Po Andet Village and Kanhchor Village in Kanhchor Commune, Kandieng District, with each family Received: Angkor 25 kg, 1 long fish, 1 fish sauce, 1 box of noodles and 50,000 Riels.
