Ministry of Labor and relevant partners consult on reducing the effects and risks of asbestos
(Phnom Penh): The National Asbestos Information Working Group, in collaboration with the International Labor Organization and Afida, organized a workshop on drafting a roadmap on reducing the impact and risk of asbestos disease in Cambodia and Sharing the results of the latest research on asbestos-related diseases in the world.
According to Hui Hansong, the biggest dangers of asbestos can be incurable diseases, most of which are lung cancer, throat cancer, stomach cancer and colon cancer. Many countries have now stopped using asbestos. For these reasons, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and relevant ministries, including workers and employers, want to avoid the risks posed by asbestos.
