Ms. Youk Sambath: Construction of the first 19 Kovid vaccine plant in Cambodia is slowly beginning as the official groundbreaking ceremony is scheduled for November (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Ms. Youk Sambath, Secretary of State for the Ministry of Health, said: The first 19 Kovid vaccine plants in Cambodia are scheduled to open in November 2022, and construction is now underway.
Ms. Youk Sambath made this statement at a press conference on "Achievements of the past five years of the Ministry of Health" organized by the spokesperson of the Royal Government on the morning of September 15, 2022.
Ms. Youk Sambath said, "Regarding the construction of the Kovid 19 vaccine factory, the Ministry of Health has done a lot of work with Sinovak after Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, decided in the past that the construction is underway. Led by Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health.
She added that the Ministry of Health is currently working with Sinovak with the support of private partners who are willing to invest in the construction of the plant.
She stated that until now, the private company has filled almost 100 percent of the land in Tuol Ampil village, Ponhea Leu commune, Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province, with an area of about 5 hectares. After the land is filled, the company will start construction.
She stated that the vaccine factory has international standards and focuses on packaging and supply.
Ms. Youk Sambath stated, "For the official opening of the government, the company will ask the Royal Government to come to the official inauguration in November 2022. Currently, the construction process has been starting slowly. Pour soil to build roads and so on.
She said that according to the project on the 5 hectares of land, the factory will build many large buildings in each section, such as the production chain and other parts, including buildings for workers and professionals.
