(Phnom Penh): The Accounting and Auditing Regulator (NRC) of the Non-Banking Financial Services Authority in collaboration with the Cambodian Shoe Association organized a dissemination workshop on "Accounting and Auditing Obligations and Related Provisions" for Shoe Association Members Cambodia Online (ZOOM) for the purpose of disseminating laws and regulations for enterprises that are members of the Shoe Association in Cambodia.
The workshop will be held on the afternoon of September 14, 2022 under the chairmanship of Mr. Bou Tharin, Director General of Accounting and Auditing, with the participation of Mr. Lim Tong, President of the Travel and Leather Products Association of Cambodia. Leaders and officers of accounting and auditing, as well as the presence of a total of 99 members of the Cambodian Shoe Association.
He added that currently some laws and regulations have been implemented, including:
1: Law on Accounting and Auditing 20162: Sub-Decree on Transitional Penalties for Violations of the Law on Accounting and Auditing 3: Prakas on the obligation to submit an independent audit report 4: Proclamation of some circulars.
The Director General emphasized that in accordance with the Law on Accounting and Auditing, three basic obligations have been established for enterprises, namely the obligation to keep the accounting records, the obligation to prepare financial statements in accordance with the applicable standards and the obligation to submit financial statements. Independent audit in accordance with the terms and conditions.
