China, ASEAN to build closer China-ASEAN common destiny
1. Help each other in the fight against Kovid 19
Following the outbreak of Kovid 19, China and ASEAN share experiences of Kovid 19, promote the supply of materials for Kovid 19, cooperate in research and vaccine production, and reach consensus Many in common support the stability of the industrial chain and the supply chain.
2. Frequent cultural changes to humanity
China and ASEAN have close cultural ties, and human cultural exchanges are frequent. The format of communication between the people of the two sides will exceed 50 million by 2018.
3. Infrastructure connectivity continues to grow
The two sides have enhanced connectivity and cooperation in infrastructure such as railways, roads, ports and airports. As of the end of July 2022, the construction sites contracted by Chinese enterprises in ASEAN countries have been stable, with a business volume of more than 3.8 billion US dollars.
4. Bilateral trade continues to grow rapidly
From January to July this year, China-ASEAN trade volume reached 54.49 billion US dollars, up 13.1 percent year on year. Of China's total export-import volume.
5. Outstanding effect of investment cooperation
As of the end of July this year, the volume of mutual investment between China and ASEAN exceeded 3.4 billion US dollars, making it the most active cooperation partner in mutual investment.
Article by Cambodia-China Friendship Radio Mr. Ly Chantola became the only candidate for President of the 14th Mandate Bar Association because there were no candidates
