Media Cooperation Forum on "ASEAN Partners" 2022 opens in Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region, China
BEIJING, Sept. 15 (Xinhua) - A media cooperation forum on "ASEAN Partners" 2022, co-organized by the Central Radio and Television of China and the Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region, was held in Nanning on September 15.
More than 180 Chinese and international guests from 70 media outlets in 17 countries participated online and on-site to discuss the topic of "Intelligent Integration of Forces" in order to promote the Chinese media and countries. ASEAN calls for greater and deeper cooperation and exchanges in the field to contribute to the establishment of a more cohesive China-ASEAN common destiny.
China Central Radio and Television is willing to continue to cooperate, build, share and win-win to promote exchange and mutual learning of human civilization. China Central Radio and Television will use the innovative superiority of "5G + 4K / 8K + AI" technology to add new impetus to the innovative development of the world's media culture industry.
Deng Xijun said the development of a comprehensive strategic partnership between China and ASEAN could not have been possible without the active participation of the media. We need to continue to expand the potential of media cooperation to contribute to mutual understanding.
Mr. Kao Kim Hourn expressed the hope that ASEAN and China will continue to make efforts to establish constructive and positive relations. Increase mutual trust. We work hand in hand to address future challenges and challenges to contribute to ensuring prosperity, security, peace and stability in the region as well as globally.
