Sor Saroeun, a former Royal Ballet dancer, has died at the age of 88.
Dr. Hee Virak said that Sor Saroeun passed away on Tuesday, September 13, 2022 and considered this a loss of valuable resources of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Dr. Hee Virak expressed his condolences on the death of the elderly grandmother and offered his condolences to the family of the deceased.
"Even though Sor Saroeun has passed away, she has left a lot of scars on her face, which is a valuable work for Cambodian children who love culture," he said. May the soul of the old woman, Sar Saroeun, be born in death with the power of goodness and meritorious deeds that her children have dedicated to her, and may not be wasted. "
Dr. Hee Virak presented the following profile of Sor Saroeun:
After the Pol Pot regime, Ms. Sor Saroeun stayed and worked for the state in Kampong Thom province as a traditional dancer in her character until 1995, when she retired in that province.
* Later, after Mr. Seng Sam An's son-in-law transferred his job from the province to Phnom Penh, he followed and stayed with his son-in-law and his children forever until the day he passed away.
* By 2022, Sor Saroeun, a former Apsara Royal Ballet dancer with Princess Ream Norodom Bopha Devi, who has performed abroad, such as the French Republic, the People's Republic of China, the Russian Federation, Malaysia, Thailand, Singapore and Many other countries.
NEC Holds Meeting to Review and Decide on Draft Calendar and Master Plan for the 7th National Assembly Election
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Thursday, September 15, 2022, at the meeting hall of the National Election Committee (NEC), a meeting was held under the chairmanship of Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the NEC to review and decide on Handbook for Voter Registration on 2022 Voter List and Voter Registration and Decision Review on Draft Calendar and Master Plan for the 7th National Assembly Election 2023.
After careful review and discussion, the NEC has decided to revise some of the contents of the 2022 Voter Registration Book and some of the contents of the Master Plan for the 7th National Assembly Election 2023. Agree in principle on the calendar of the 7th National Assembly Election 2023.
According to the calendar of the 7th National Assembly Election 2023, the registration of political parties and the list of candidates will run for 15 days, from April 24 to May 8, 2023.
Political parties wishing to participate in the election must apply for registration of political parties and lists of candidates in the form prescribed by the NEC.
