Nearly 1,000 families in Veal village have been drawn to win plots of land in the natural village of Run Ta Ek, Banteay Srei district, in order for the authorities to make the Angkor resort area more attractive. During the ceremony, the people were very happy that the Royal Government arranged to give them land ownership, as well as thanked Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara for this successful mission.
