Ministry of Public Works in Cooperation with Kandal Provincial Authority to Enforce the Law on Transportation Exceeding the Limit
(Kandal): The Steering Committee for Inspection of Overweight Vehicles of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport for two days, on September 13 and 14, 2022, in cooperation with the Kandal Provincial Authority to tighten the law. Enforce the overweight rule by inspecting hundreds of vehicles, but none of them are overweight.
The operation was led by Mr. Kim Sann, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Public Works and Transport, in collaboration with Mr. Hak Sok Makara, Deputy Governor of Kandal Province, and also attended by Mr. Moeung Youleng, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kandal Province, with the scales at the base. Prek Samrong Bridge from afternoon to midnight in Takhmao, Kandal province.
Mr. Kimsan explained to the car owners to understand the rules of overweight (road rules) and request not to overweight because overweight has caused damage to national roads and accidents. Serious traffic. He recalled the instructions of Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, "Please all transport drivers, do not be afraid of law enforcement officials, but be afraid of the law."
According to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, the team will proceed with the procedure without understanding anyone if it is found that the trucks dare to overweight. The operation will continue throughout the country to restrict transportation in accordance with the law to prevent criminals from arbitrarily destroying roads.
