Cambodian Health Minister on the Success of Kovid 19 Control at ASEAN-China Forum and Confirmed Readiness to Build Regional Health Safety
(Phnom Penh): Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health of Cambodia, on September 15, 2022, attended the 4th ASEAN-China Forum on Health Cooperation through Video Conference.
At the ASEAN-China Health Forum, Minister Mam Bunheng highlighted Cambodia's success in managing Kovid-19 under the strong, wise and prudent leadership of Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen. At the same time, Cambodia reaffirmed its full commitment and readiness with all ASEAN members and China to build better health and safety for the region.
The People's Republic of China holds a bi-annual forum in Nanning, Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region. The 10 ASEAN members and ministers of the Health Committee of the People's Republic of China and the accompanying delegation.
The ASEAN-China Forum is organized to share experiences, knowledge and priorities of ASEAN-China cooperation, especially the 2022 theme, focusing on "Improving regional health and safety and strengthening cooperation." "On the resilience of the health system after the Kovid-19 crisis."
The Minister of Health stated that at the official opening ceremony of the 4th ASEAN-China Forum on Cooperation in the Health Sector, the key experiences were shared as follows:
First, the world has agreed on the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), resolving to "never leave anyone without access to health care." The Royal Government of Cambodia has partnered with all development partners to implement the Health Equity Fund, providing the most disadvantaged 3 million people with access to quality and free health care.
Second, after the global epidemic of Kovid-19, like many countries around the world, Cambodia needs to address the Kovid-19 crisis and strengthen the country's economy to recover and ensure future resilience. Good until now. Cambodia has fully reopened the country in all areas from November 1, 2021, based on four factors:
1: Complete basic vaccination for 95% of the population of 16 million people
2: Access to effective treatment and cure for Kovid-19
3: Increased experience in Kovid-19 response response
The Minister added that this success can be achieved under the strong, wise and skillful leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, led by the National Committee for Disease Control 19 to promote participation. Of the Royal Government, the whole society and international cooperation.
Third, Cambodia as a member of ASEAN and cooperation in the Cambodia-China Comprehensive Strategic Partnership, the Ministry of Health has supported the following commitments:
* Complete the ASEAN-China Memorandum of Understanding on Health Cooperation as soon as possible.
* Strengthen cooperation to prevent, manage and enhance preparedness and response to Kovid-19 and new and recurrent infectious diseases, as well as any possible public health emergencies in the future.
Expand maternal and child health cooperation, especially policy and coordination through the exchange of knowledge and experience to improve maternal and child health in the region.
* Promote cooperation in human resource development, including healthcare professionals, health administration managers, public health professionals and researchers.
* Working together to transform digital health technology to improve people's health through cooperation and multilateral partnerships to invest in and transform digital health into support for post-Kovid-19 recovery.
The Minister of Health also stressed at the forum that the Ministry of Health is fully committed and ready with all ASEAN member countries and the Chinese Health Committee to build better health safety for the region and strengthen cooperation. Aims to increase the resilience of the health system after the Kovid-19 crisis.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin pays a courtesy call on the Prime Minister of Laos
(Laos): During his official and friendly visit to the Lao People's Democratic Republic, Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia, led a delegation to pay a courtesy call on Dr. Phorn Kham Viphavan, Prime Minister of Laos in the afternoon. September 14, 2022 in the capital Vientiane.
Dr. Phorn Kham Viphavan expressed his pleasure that the President of the National Assembly led a high-level delegation of the National Assembly of Cambodia to pay an official visit to the Lao People's Democratic Republic this time, which reflected the close ties and cooperation between the two countries. Both of which have been around for a long time.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin informed the Prime Minister that the purpose of the current visit of the delegation of the National Assembly of Cambodia is to continue to strengthen and expand the relationship of traditional solidarity and cooperation in all fields between our two countries. - Laos, which has been around for a long time, to become even stronger.
At the same time, Samdech congratulated and highly appreciated the great achievements that the Party, State, Government and people of Laos have achieved in building and developing a society that has grown steadily and has improved the lives of the people of Laos. The prestige and role of Lao friends are increasingly being promoted on the international stage.
