Investment Council Minister: ASEAN must unite more than ever to solve challenges and attract investment, investment flow in 2021 to increase to 174 billion US dollars
He stressed that in this context, ASEAN must be more united than ever and must continue to work together to address all challenges and continue to promote and attract sustainable and environmentally friendly investment in the ASEAN region.
The 25th ASEAN Investment Area Council Meeting will be held on 14 September 2022, in conjunction with the 54th ASEAN Economic Ministers' Meeting, which is being held from 14 to 18 September 2022. Siem Reap Province.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, extended a warm welcome to the Ministers of the ASEAN Member States and all the delegates present at the meeting and encouraged the delegation to take the opportunity to visit. Unique and rich temples in the territory of Siem Reap.
The ASEAN Investment Council Ministerial Meeting also noted the progress of discussions on improving the investment climate in the ASEAN region to make the region an investment destination and a regional production base.
The meeting also reviewed the ASEAN Investment Survey 2022, compiled by the United Nations Conference on Trade and Development (UNCTAD).
This report shows a significant increase in investment inflows into ASEAN in 2021 to about 174 billion US dollars, equivalent to the inflow of investment in 2019 before the region as a whole. Effects of Kovid-19 disease. Of these, investment in manufacturing, the catalyst for the recovery of the ASEAN economy in the aftermath of the Kovid-19 crisis, is the most prominent.
With record growth in investment flows, the report shows a sharp increase in new investment. Along with the positive findings, the report also highlighted that investment facilitation is a priority agenda for countries around the world to attract more investment and to revive the national economy in the aftermath of the Kovid-19 crisis.
Overall, ASEAN investment ministers hailed the report, while some investment ministers stressed that regional connectivity, especially along the borders of neighboring countries, would be beneficial to trade facilitation. And investment.
On the other hand, simplification of investment-related procedures and the promotion of digitalization will accelerate the achievement of a joint venture framework called a single digital framework.
The above is in response to the latest developments in the investment climate in the ASEAN region, with ASEAN initiating and striving to enhance investment facilitation through efforts to implement the ASEAN Investment Facilitation Framework adopted in 2021.
Duke Kith Meng Chairs the 20th Joint Business Council Meeting of ASEAN Members with US, China, Europe, Japan, UK and Stakeholders
(Siem Reap): Neak Oknha Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Chairman of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council, this morning, September 15, 2022, chaired a meeting of the Joint Business Council in Siem Reap, Kingdom of Cambodia. Cambodia, with the participation of members of the 10 ASEAN Business Advisory Council and members of the Joint Business Council from the United States, China, Europe, Japan, the United Kingdom, as well as other stakeholder associations.
Neak Oknha Kith Meng, Chairman of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council, thanked the members of the 10-member Business Advisory Council and members of the Joint Business Council from all countries for attending the 20th meeting in person at Siem Reap Province of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The President Duke chaired the meeting to discuss each of the above agendas and there was a lively discussion from the members of the meeting. The 20th meeting of the Joint Business Council was held successfully and fruitfully in a friendly and fraternal atmosphere.
Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh: Despite the spread of Kovid 19, the Cambodian-Lao troops continue to work closely together in good neighborliness
(Laos): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense of Cambodia, confirmed that despite the outbreak of Kovid 19, the armies of the two countries, Cambodia and Laos, continue to work closely together as neighbors. Good traditional friendship aims to enhance relations to the level of comprehensive and long-term strategic partnership, to strengthen and expand friendship, solidarity and cooperation in the field of defense.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh said this on September 14, 2022 during a bilateral meeting with General Chan Samorn Channhalath, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense of Laos, held at the Lao Ministry of National Defense in Vientiane. On the occasion of his official and friendly visit to the Lao People's Democratic Republic and his participation in the meeting of the three Defense Ministers of Cambodia, Vietnam and Laos in Laos.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh expressed his deep gratitude to the Government, Army and people of Laos, especially the Minister of National Defense of Laos, who has always supported and cooperated well with the Royal Government, the Army and the people of Cambodia to promote brotherhood and solidarity. Cambodia-Laos Armed Forces Cooperation Partners.
During the meeting, General Chan Samorn Channhalath also thanked Samdech Picheay Sena for leading a delegation of the Ministry of National Defense to visit Laos to strengthen the precious traditional ties between the two governments and the two armies. Cambodia, Laos are brothers.
The General also considered this visit as an important symbol in making a great contribution to deepening the friendship and cooperation between the two parties, the two armies and the people of the two countries, especially in the field. National defense, security work of both armies.
General Chan Samorn Channhalath also expressed his support for Cambodia, which has hosted the ASEAN Summit and has worked to address many issues that have arisen in ASEAN in the past. On behalf of the Government and the Lao People's Army, he also thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces for their support to Laos in the past, especially in helping to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 in Laos.
It should be noted that on that occasion, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh and General Chan Samorn Channhalath also presided over the signing ceremony of the Protocol on Cooperation between the Ministries of Defense of Cambodia and Laos.
