Tycoon Try Pheap's company, which has a lot of business in hand with a well-known university in Thailand, has been working together to improve human resource training for 5 years with good results. Better. In particular, contributed a lot of knowledge to students on both the Cambodian and Thai sides.
After seeing the good results of this cooperation, the company and the university also agreed to renew the MoU on this human resource training for another 5 years. The re-signing of the Memorandum of Understanding on this cooperation took place on Wednesday, September 14, 2022.
The MoU was signed at the Try Pheap Group headquarters in Phnom Penh, chaired directly by Duke Try Pheap, and the Thai University side was chaired by Associate Rector Dr. Narong Polwong.
At the memorandum of understanding, Dr. Narong Polwong presented the reasons why the university joined hands with Duke Try Pheap's company to improve education. The reason for the cooperation is because the company of Duke Try Pheap is a company that develops clean and green business, contributes to reducing poverty, promoting peace and democracy in Cambodia.
In addition to Tycoon Try Pheap's company, a private company with many businesses in hand, such as agro-industrial special economic zones (rubber plantations), civil engineering and oil banks, logistics and drying centers, recreation and tourism and real estate. Original.
Duke Try Pheap expressed his pleasure at the cooperation with a well-known Thai university for contributing to the training of human resources in Cambodia to have a clear knowledge to meet the needs of the company.
Duke Try Pheap claimed that through this cooperation, Cambodian students and students from Duke's company will have the opportunity to study at RMUTI University.
He added that in order to support the development plan under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the company will provide funding for the study of Cambodian students at RMUTI University.
