On Monday, Chinese Premier Li Keqiang said that China will take measures to stabilize job growth and consumer prices, Reuters reported, citing state media.
"China will accelerate the recovery of consumption to become a major driving force and make greater efforts to promote effective investment," Li was quoted as saying on state radio.
The world's second-largest economy shrank in the second quarter of this year amid an outbreak of Kovid-19 and a slump in the real estate market that reduced consumption and factory activity. Production.
Li also said China will accelerate the construction of major projects and increase policy banking financing based on the needs of the domestic economy.
Recent data showed that China's economy lost further momentum in August, with factory activity continuing to slow and export growth slowing as demand slowed amid tight restrictions. Prevent Kovid-19 disease.
China's cabinet last week announced further steps to boost investment by expanding measures to boost the economy, which has been devastated by Kovid-19. According to Reuters.
