Ministries and relevant organizations discuss the mining sector in Cambodia to promote transparent management and development of mineral resources
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Mines and Energy and relevant organizations on September 14, 2022 met to discuss the governance of the extractive industry in Cambodia, a sector that uses machinery and technical equipment to extract gas and oil. Etc. to promote transparent management and development of mineral resources.
Speaking at the 9th Extractive Industry Governance Forum on September 14, 2022, Mr. Meng Saktheara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Mines and Energy, said that this forum is a mechanism for discussing the work between the three main stakeholders: (1): Government, (2): Companies, (3): Local community organizations.
Mr. Meng Saktheara added that the three main stakeholders are discussing the governance of the extractive industry in three joint goals: (first), mineral resources for all, (second), promoting Provide transparent management and development of mineral resources and (3) be responsible for the environment, society and culture.
At the same time, Mr. Meng Saktheara emphasized that the 9th Forum on Extractive Industry Governance was held for the purpose of discussing the work and sharing to the organizations, associations and local authorities to know about the following work:
1: Progress in the management and development of the mining sector 2: Development of local communities using mining funds 3: Contribution to the development of local communities and good governance in the mining sector of mining companies 4: Progress of gold mining operations and operations in Okvau province Mondulkiri.
At the 9th Extractive Industries Governance Forum, Mr. Ing Depola, Director General of the General Department of Mineral Resources of the Ministry of Mines and Energy, also presented the latest updates on the management of the mining sector and the establishment of a mining fund to the participants in this forum. .
According to OXFAM representatives, the forum sets a good example of multilateral dialogue with stakeholders and the company's best practices to promote community engagement and partnerships. Promote the governance of the extractive industry in Cambodia.
The Extractive Industries Governance Forum is an important forum for information sharing, knowledge and solution-oriented discussions among stakeholders, especially to increase mutual understanding and trust between mining companies and affected communities. Touch.
The forum will provide stakeholders with an opportunity to hear updates on extractive industry policies, mining companies, mining funds for community development, information and community concerns regarding social, cultural and environmental impacts, particularly Indigenous peoples.
