Mr. Vongsy Visoth: ASEAN trade with countries around the world about 3.3 trillion dollars, trade between ASEAN members will be 712 billion dollars in 2021
(Siem Reap): Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Minister of the AFTA Council of Cambodia, on the morning of September 14, 2022, chaired a meeting of the ASEAN Free Trade Area Council. The 36th AFTA Council Meeting at the Sokha Hotel, Siem Reap, with the participation of the Minister of the AFTA Council of ASEAN Member States and the Secretary-General of ASEAN.
The meeting reviewed and exchanged views on the progress of the implementation of the ASEAN Trade Agreement, trade facilitation and customs integration within the ASEAN framework.
ASEAN trade with the rest of the world is estimated at $ 3.3 trillion, of which trade between ASEAN members will reach $ 712 billion in 2021, contributing to ASEAN economic growth of about 3% in 2021.
In addition, the meeting commended the progress of the preparations for the negotiations to upgrade the ASEAN Commodity Trade Agreement to ensure that the agreement will be modern and forward-looking, as well as better respond to needs and requirements. Regional and global development. The first meeting of the Trade Negotiation Committee of the ASEAN Commodity Trade Agreement is scheduled for the end of September 2022.
