As for the construction of the concrete road, it has reached 50 percent, with the construction scheduled to be completed before Pchum Ben this year. Cambodia urges tourism businesses to use solar as much as possible
(Phnom Penh): During the recovery phase of tourism during the Kovid 19 crisis, the Royal Government of Cambodia and partner organizations have pushed for the most efficient use of energy that reduces environmental impacts, such as solar energy. .
The Ministry of Tourism, WWF, Tourism Federation of Cambodia and partner organizations have all mentioned the environmental impact of using fossil fuels and supported the use of solar energy, which reduces the impact on the environment, reduces costs in line with Current visitor trend choices.
Surveys show that most young tourists support reducing the impact on the environment, so they always choose a place that is connected to nature or stay somewhere environmentally friendly. For international tourists, they want to contribute to protecting the environment and improving the lives of people living in the area through accommodation and tourism services.
For this reason, the Royal Government of Cambodia, WWF Cambodia and its partner organizations have launched the project "Restoration and Promotion of Cambodian Tourism with Brotherhood, Environment and Environment", which officially opened on September 14. 2022 at Topas Restaurant, Phnom Penh.
WWF Cambodia Director Seng Teak said that WWF Cambodia has partnered with the Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation (SDC) to officially launch the project "Restoring and Promoting Cambodian Tourism with Brotherhood and Environment". Atmosphere.
He said the project would help the tourism business move forward by adhering to a more responsible and sustainable standard and supporting environmental protection through the use of renewable energy and energy-efficient refrigeration systems. Save on accommodation, eco-tourism, hotels, community sites, eco-tourism and restaurants. This project is a standard that will bring about positive changes for tourism in Cambodia.
President of the Federation of Tourism of Cambodia, Mr. Din Somethearith, said that the solar power system for use in hotels, natural resorts and community eco-tourism sites.
Mr. Somethearith promised to use the voice of the Cambodian Tourism Union to promote the use of solar panels in the tourism industry, as the use of solar energy systems is not yet widespread across the country.
Mr. Kuch Panhasa, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, called on tourism operators and tourism communities, as well as all relevant institutions, to support the project "Rehabilitation and Promotion of Cambodian Tourism with Harmonization, Climate and Environment" to join. The Royal Government in promoting the recovery of Cambodia's tourism sector in and after the Kovid-19 crisis, as well as the development of sustainable and green tourism.
