Bangkok warns of heavy rains that will cause floods across 12 districts
BANGKOK, Sept. 13 (Xinhua) - The Bangkok Metropolitan Administration on Tuesday issued a warning of moderate to heavy rain and flooding from 4pm to 11pm local time. 12. This is according to a release by the Xinhua news agency.
The announcement comes after parts of the city were flooded after heavy rains in recent days.
According to the Department of Irrigation, the average daily rainfall in Bangkok during the first 10 days of September was 96.5 mm, compared to an average of 52.2 mm in the same period last year. Last year. On September 10, 24-hour rainfall reached 112.7 mm, the highest in six years.
