He allowed an open discussion between the private sector and the Royal Government on the challenges, concerns and suggestions of the private sector to find appropriate and fair solutions, as well as to promote a more equitable investment and business environment. Be transparent and maintain the implementation of applicable laws and regulations.
The meeting discussed 5 agendas, including: 1. Tax on trademarks and taxes on billboards, 2. Illegal trade (referring to illegal and counterfeit cigarettes), 3. Taxes on stock transfers, 4. Monopoly and import of the latest model vehicles, while others hold monopoly and 5. Value-added tax on e-commerce transactions and basic financial services in the financial sector.
As a result, the meeting resolved the issues and clarified the issues raised by the private sector, setting out the next mechanism, mechanism and work for the respective ministries and institutions to continue to fulfill their duties and achieve in response to the request of Private sector, especially for the next meeting. Based on this, the private sector also agreed and continued to cooperate and participate.
General Khieu Sopheak: Video of foreigners shooting and stabbing several knives distributed through chat does not happen in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): After researching a video in which foreigners had a dispute with each other until the explosion of weapons and stabbing several knives, the authorities confirmed that the case in this video did not occur in Sihanoukville or in Cambodia No. This is according to General Khieu Sopheak, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, confirmed to Fresh News.
According to Fresh News, General Khieu Sopheak confirmed that after receiving the video, which has no clear source, the Sihanoukville Provincial Police has launched a careful investigation and concluded that the shooting did not take place. In Cambodia, this video is made abroad.
At the same time, General Khieu Sopheak also called on the people not to be confused and not to conclude what they have received without a clear basis or source.
In addition, those who know Chinese also claim that the voice correspondence in the shooting is not Chinese.
