159 Cambodian national team players ready to leave for training in China for 6 months
(Phnom Penh): A team of 159 Cambodian national team players is ready to go to train in the People's Republic of China for 6 months from September 15, 2022 to March 2023 to gain experience and good techniques To win medals in the 32nd Southeast Asian Games 2023, which Cambodia hosts.
Speaking at the meeting and farewell to the Cambodian national team athletes to train in China under the Sports Technical Assistance Program, a grant from the Chinese government on the morning of September 13, 2022 at the National Sports Training Center. Wu Guoquan, Economic and Trade Adviser of the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia, congratulates all Cambodian athletes and coaches who will be training in China in the near future.
He said that the project to send Cambodian athletes to study in China came from the efforts of the leadership of the National Olympic Committee of Cambodia and the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia. He stressed that China and Cambodia are steel friends and a common destiny, and bilateral relations have long maintained high levels of development.
He said that in order to assist Cambodia in hosting the 32nd Southeast Asian Games 2023, the Chinese government has not only implemented the stadium construction project, which Cambodia has set up a sports venue, but also has implemented technical sports projects for Cambodia. Well.
On that occasion, HE Vath Chamroeun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism and Secretary General of the National Organizing Committee of the 32nd Southeast Asian Games 2023, thanked the Chinese friends for their support of sports in Cambodia in the past through the construction of stadiums. National Heritage of Techo and helping Cambodian athletes to train effectively.
HE emphasized that the training of Cambodian athletes at this time is very important for Cambodia, especially for the 64-year historical event that Cambodia is waiting to host the 32nd Southeast Asian Games 2023. This face.
Ms. Sokvalak, a swimmer who is preparing to train in China, expressed her pride in attending this swimming training in China because China has good teachers, high experience and sufficient equipment.
"I am happy to be training in China to gain experience to improve my ability to prepare for the 2023 SEA Games, which Cambodia is hosting," she said.
At the same time, Ms. Bo In-soo is a table tennis player, thanks to the Chinese government, and she will be committed to training successfully in China and using that knowledge to build a reputation for Cambodia.
"Hopefully the Chinese teachers will train us well in new techniques," she said. "And I am highly committed to preparing to bring knowledge from China to participate in the 2023 SEA Games to get good results for the nation."
