(Phnom Penh): The new “Techo” Business Training Center and the Active Women Entrepreneurs Project of PAC Cambodia, with the support of the United States Agency for International Development, signed a Memorandum of Understanding on the morning of September 13, 2022. List of businesses in the information technology nursery, with the participation of relevant representatives of the two institutions in the business development building.
The joint purpose of the MoU is to establish a framework for cooperation and joint activities between the two institutions to expand the dissemination of business registration systems in information technology nurseries to a wide range and to those most in need.
In the past, the two institutions have cooperated many times and have disseminated the business registration system in the information technology nursery by sending speakers from the new business training center "Techo" to the programs of the partner institutions. Pak Cambodia.
The signing of the MoU will open a new page of strengthening cooperation between the new Business Center "Techo" and PAC Cambodia in order to promote and support entrepreneurs in gaining knowledge related to business registration.
Through the signing of this Memorandum of Understanding, the new Business Training Center "Techo" and PAC Cambodia have also shown a strong will to work together with a pro-active spirit and high responsibility for the common good of society. And the Cambodian economy. The signing of the MoU was completed smoothly and in a joyful atmosphere.
It should be noted that the registration of businesses in the information technology nursery is carried out under the coordination of the Economic and Financial Policy Committee, with the new business training center "Techo" as the staff of the Ministry of Economy and Finance in charge of support and technical support.
The system was officially launched on June 15, 2020 and is being expanded to the second and third phases.
Information technology nursery business registration system is one of the sharp reforms of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which is based on the principle of reducing inspection time, reducing costs and reducing complicated procedures.
PAC Cambodia is a non-profit foreign non-governmental organization that supports the development of human resources based on information and data obtained from communities to build resilience, increase accountability, strengthen knowledge and skills to participate in sustainable social development. .
