(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia will increase research, repression and law enforcement in a fair and strict manner, without exception, on locations and individuals involved in all forms of human trafficking and smuggling in Cambodia.
The Royal Government's decision was made through the remarks of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the report of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, on the situation and operations against human trafficking and human trafficking.
1. Increase cooperation in the fight against human trafficking in order to rescue victims, search for perpetrators and punish them according to the law, and crack down on related illegal gambling.
2. In cases where it is found to be related to real human trafficking or labor trafficking or online fraud, the research should be expanded to include money laundering offenses.
3. Apply fairly in accordance with the law in force and with high responsibility in all locations suspected of being involved in human trafficking and all forms of human trafficking by applying strict legal measures on locations and individuals who are found to be Involved in this offense and shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of the law without exception.
4: Relevant authorities shall respond and respond in a timely manner to all dissemination of provocative information and request to correct the contrary to the truth in order to neutralize the negative attacks from various circles both inside and outside the country and to avoid any repercussions. On the political environment and social security.
5: Increase cooperation between relevant institutions to monitor and organize order in places where there is concentration, accommodation, business and the use of foreign labor to thoroughly control foreigners and prevent the intrusion by Illegal along the border.
Court postpones verdict in Sam Rainsy case in case of "attempt to cede a foreign state"
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Municipal Court on September 13, 2022, decided to postpone the verdict in the case of Sam Rainsy convicted in connection with the case of "attempting to hand over part of the national territory to a foreign state."
The charges relate to the case of Sam Rainsy signing an agreement with Vietnamese ethnic leader Kok Sar in order to hand over four Khmer provinces to the Montagnards if he is elected.
At the date of the court, the case is scheduled to be announced on September 13, 2022, but now the court has decided to postpone it indefinitely.
The spokesman added that the court would announce the verdict later.
During the trial, Sin Sovannaroth, president of the Trial Chamber, stated that in this criminal case, Sam Rainsy, a 72-year-old man, was charged by prosecutors with "attempting to hand over territory to a foreign state." Part of the Nation ”in accordance with the provisions of Article 27 and Article 440 of the Penal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia, committed in Phnom Penh and other places on April 14, 2013.
According to the charges and the provisions of the above article, the accused and the existing convict, Sam Rainsy, could face life imprisonment if the court finds him guilty of the above charges.
