(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, praised and highly appreciated the good cooperation in providing services in the field of child welfare and people with disabilities, with many fruitful results. He added that the situation of children in Cambodia has given priority to the implementation of the policy on alternative care for children by promoting family and community care.
Mr. Vong Soth made the remarks as he met with World Vision Country Executive Director Jan Emanuel Genting on the morning of September 13, 2022 at the Ministry of Social Affairs.
Jan Immanuel Ginting congratulated Cambodia on joining the Partnership to End Violence Against Children, as well as implementing various UN plans and recommendations.
He said that this organization mostly works at the sub-national level and works with the Committee on Women and Children at the commune / sangkat level on various training activities and also works with parents and guardians of children at the sub-national level to participate in preventing violence against children.
