Commentary: The United States incited "Color Revolution" to destroy world peace and stability
It should be noted that while swallowing more foreign territory, the United States has often begun to interfere in the internal affairs of other countries. Incomplete statistics show that since the turn of the 20th century, the United States has planned dozens of successful or unsuccessful coups in Latin America.
The American National Democratic Foundation, dubbed the "Second US Intelligence Agency", is closely linked to events such as the "Rose Revolution" in Georgia, the "Orange Revolution" in Ukraine and the "Spring Revolution". The United States is a "prisoner" who often causes unrest in other countries.
Too much injustice will actually bring self-harm. Coalition wars helped the United States defeat their rivals, but at the same time gradually undermined the foundations of American hegemony. The more short-term benefits it can bring, the more serious the consequences for the United States in the long run.
