In relation to the local education sector, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also recommended the construction of schools with primary, secondary and high schools, which must be built step by step while the construction of primary schools has already been completed. For this school, Samdech also provided a house for a teacher with 2 floors and 20 rooms for 20 teachers.
Regarding the health sector, Samdech Techo Hun Sen recommended the construction of a hospital, which will have three health centers, one for general examination and treatment, one for maternity ward and one for 20-room accommodation. For doctors in this area.
In this ceremony, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also presented the project to build 8 markets in the Run Ta Ek area, including good food and coffee to push this area into a civilized area.
With this infrastructure, the Ministry of Environment is also preparing to plant fruit trees for the people on each plot of land. Samdech Techo also called on microfinance institutions to provide loans to people who go to live in the Run Ta Ek area with low interest rates and favorable because those who go to live there will need capital to create a business.
Residents in Taksin Tbong and Trapeang Ses villages, who meet all the conditions and voluntarily demolished illegal constructions, went to draw lots to select 1,117 plots of land in Run Ta Ek Natural Village, with each family receiving one plot of land measuring 20 meters by 30 meters.
