(Phnom Penh): According to the circular of the Ministry of Tourism on September 13, 2022, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, introduced five points to manage the flow of tourists and improve the quality of tourism products and continue to participate in preventing the spread of Kovid-19 disease on the occasion of Pchum Ben from September 24-26.
* First, to continue to promote the strict implementation of measures taken by the Royal Government to prevent the spread of Kovid-19, especially the measures "3 prevent 3" to be consistent with the strengthening. Implement tourism safety rules and minimum operating standards (SOP) procedures along the new normal path to maintain business stability and ensure the safety of national and international tourists.
* Second, continue to encourage business owners and tourist destinations to organize incentives for vaccinated tourists, while all staff must be vaccinated as required by the Ministry of Health.
* Third: To cooperate with traders and tour operators to improve the quality of tourism products, maintain a clean environment and maintain appropriate prices for products and services. All accommodation, food and other services must be clearly written in the table to inform guests in advance to avoid excessive fees. In case of non-compliance with the posted schedule, the business owner shall be liable before the law in force.
* Fourth: To instruct the owners of boats, ferries and water transport means that transport tourists across the sea, rivers, streams and lakes not to overload and must be equipped with the necessary rescue equipment.
* Fifth: To set up a working group to disseminate and promote the implementation of the contents of this circular in a comprehensive and comprehensive manner to tour operators and to make a summary report of tourist statistics at resorts and tourist destinations and send Ministry of Tourism on time on a daily basis.
