(Siem Reap): On the morning of September 13, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, met with people who volunteered to relocate their houses and other structures from Angkor and other areas under Management of APSARA Authority.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen spoke for more than 2 hours, as follows:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the people for agreeing to remove the building from the Angkor resort area and thanked Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara for leading the demolition work.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the work of organizing order in Angkor can no longer sit in the wind, which can lead to the loss of great benefits for the nation and the people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that what does Samdech have a headache doing in order to maintain order in the resort area if it is not necessary?
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk took great care of the Angkor resort area.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen recalled that His Majesty the King had directly initiated the proposal to include the Angkor site in the World Heritage List, and expressed his full support.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Angkor site, when inscribed on the World Heritage List in 1992, must comply with the regulations set by UNESCO.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that many World Heritage Sites, including in Germany, have been removed from the UNESCO World Heritage List due to disqualification by UNESCO.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated with confidence that even without Samdech, there is no political party leading the country other than the Cambodian People's Party.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that if Hun Manet was not Samdech's son, he would still support the candidacy of the Prime Minister because he was qualified.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen advised to prepare land as a policy to distribute to the children of the people to move out of the Angkor resort area when the family is separated.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the current campaign has allowed the Angkor resort area to remain on the World Heritage List, which is in the national interest.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that people have changed from having illegal housing to having legal housing.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Siem Reap province ended the fighting in 1993.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the preparation of the Angkor resort area is a necessary task for the preservation of the cultural heritage of the ancestors.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructs the army to help transport people's belongings from the Angkor resort area to Run Ta Ek Natural Village.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen supported the people who agreed to dismantle 1,117 buildings, including 50 kg of rice, 6 boxes of noodles, 1 small box of fish, 200,000 Riels and 1 million Riels for house demolition. Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces the donation of 30 sheets of zinc to a family.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces to provide poor cards and pregnant women to all citizens who agree to move from the Angkor resort area to Run Ta Ek Natural Village. Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructs the Minister of Social Affairs to arrange for poor cards and pregnant women cards for all citizens who agree to move from the Angkor resort area to Run Ta Ek Natural Village.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces 10-year validity for poor cards and pregnant women cards for citizens agreeing to move from the Angkor resort area to Run Ta Ek Natural Village.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen advised to pave the road to Run Ta Ek Natural Village. Samdech Techo Hun Sen recommends the construction of road infrastructure in Run Ta Ek Natural Village with a total length of 140 km. Currently, 18 kilometers have been built.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructed Senior Minister Cham Prasidh to provide clean water system to the people of Run Ta Ek Natural Village at a cost of about 3 million US dollars. Samdech Techo Hun Sen Instructs Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) to Prepare the Electricity Network for Run Ta Ek Natural Village
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructs Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) to prepare the electricity network for Run Ta Ek Natural Village.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen requests microfinance institutions to provide loans with low interest rates to people living in Run Ta Ek Natural Village.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asks political parties not to use the issue of solving problems in the Angkor resort area for political gain because it is a national need. Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that his current arrangement is to solve the nation's problems, not for politics.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen forbids political parties from using the settlement of housing in the Angkor resort area as a weapon to attack the Cambodian People's Party.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to provide 200,000 Riels per family for the construction of toilets in people's homes.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that even though Samdech resigned from the Prime Minister, Samdech was still the party president and could check the work activities of the Prime Minister.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that one of his strengths is the inaccurate assessment of his leadership and working methods.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the people clearly understood that the story of Samdech Harm celebrating the New Year and Pchum Ben when Kovid 19 spread was to protect lives. There is no greater right than the right to life.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the success of the vaccination policy helped Cambodia to overcome Kovid 19.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech did not disappoint the people who voted for Samdech and the Cambodian People's Party.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech did not disappoint the King in appointing Samdech as Prime Minister. Samdech will try to maintain peace.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that yesterday, 16 cases of 19 cases of Kovid were found.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asks Mr. Khem Veasna to respond to the accusation that Samdech is behind the event to organize an event at Phnom Kulen.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that those who opposed the Prime Minister's bodyguards were attempting a coup d'etat.
