Exporters of trout to China, officials say exporters are carefully processing, but the export time is not clear
(Phnom Penh): A senior official of the Fisheries Administration confirmed that Hun Ty, a trout processing company, has been granted permission to export to China and has been carefully ordering processed trout for export in the future.
Mr. Hav Piseth stated that "Currently, the fish processing company has been ordering 6 tons of trout in Prek Pnov district, ordering 1 ton per day, so when the order and processing the full amount will work. "Exports to China soon in the amount of about 40 tons."
The official claimed that the plan to export trout to China is still ongoing, but may be delayed due to the meticulous processing of the first export to ensure better quality.
He said that now the processing company has enough equipment to process and store trout, combined with specialized processing experts to make the trout export quickly, good quality according to Chinese standards.
He said that the process of buying fish, processing of trout is still normal, but the exact export date can not be determined, but will be exported when processed 40 tons soon.
Mr. Sok Raden, Chairman of the Board of the Cambodian Aquaculture Association, confirmed that the fish processing company Hun Ti actually ordered the fish from the fish farm, which is a member of the association, 6 tons, after buying 2 tons. And suspended for a while due to processing technical issues.
He was informed by his members that after the next purchase of 6 tons, the company began to suspend orders again, most likely due to technical problems again.
However, in order for the production and export of fish in the international market as well as China to be smooth, Mr. Sok Raden proposed to invest in local fish feed factories to reduce costs and call for investment. On as many processing plants as possible.
"Currently, we see that the problem for local fish farmers is the high cost of production because fish feed has to be imported, so if we can produce locally, we can reduce the cost a lot," he said. On the other hand, we now have only one processing plant, so exporting is difficult. Please call on the government, investors, both inside and outside, to invest more in our fish processing infrastructure.
