Understand the business: Financial experts advise financial planning for those who want to buy real estate for profit
(Phnom Penh): Financial experts advise people who can afford to buy houses and land to know how to prepare a clear financial plan to cope with a crisis to avoid selling houses immediately in the event of a global crisis. Especially those who can afford to buy a house and land for sale at a profit later.
According to the financial expert, the number of people selling houses has increased significantly after the global crisis for more than two years, which makes people Many Cambodians are affected and lose income and are forced to sell their real estate, such as houses or land, both houses bought separately and houses that are being paid in installments with the Borey or the bank, to solve their livelihood problems and bank debt.
Although some people put the property at a loss or below market value, there are not many buyers, which is a lesson for those who want to invest in buying a house and for land for sale. .
Nget Chou, an expert on financial and investment management, told Fresh News that the resale was due to the fact that most buyers did not seem to have a clear financial plan to deal with the crisis. Growth. And in the past, those who bought houses and land were able to buy one after another without studying and without preparing a financial plan to cope with the crisis.
He observed that most of the land and house payments of Cambodians are not to meet the needs or necessities of living and doing business, most of them are for profit. When problems or economic crises occur while they do not have a clear financial plan, they lack the ability to pay in installments, so they are forced to resell and sell below market value.
He explained that in order not to face this problem, people should prepare a clear financial plan, especially to cope with any crisis. Buying a home in installments requires the buyer to be clear about his monthly income, which can ensure that it does not affect the cost of living and does not affect the cost of the monthly installment. Well.
He explained, "The lesson for the people is that they have to have clear rules and financial plans and have a way to deal with problems when there is a dead end, when there is a crisis, how to avoid it. Selling at a huge discount, selling below cost, leading to losses. "So what is stuck in the market, there are not many buyers and there are many sellers in the future, it may be absorbed."
Third. The value of the home you buy should not exceed three times the total annual income of your household. For example, your family earns $ 1,500 a month, your family earns $ 18,000 a year. Therefore, the house you buy for living should not cost more than $ 54,000.
