(Ratanakkiri): Vulture experts from the Life and Nature Organization of Cambodia, which works on the conservation of vultures, highlight the changing situation, characteristics and activities of vultures as Cambodia is a country that has started to conserve endangered species. This breed has been around since 2004.
According to the vulture expert, vultures breed only once a year, and a female vulture can only produce one vulture, so if there is any disturbance, it will not be able to breed. Vultures for one year.
Ms. Nikey said that Cambodia has made great efforts to conserve this species of vulture, while the three species of vultures present in Cambodia are among the 14 species of vultures that are endangered. Extinct.
Cambodia is the last hope for these vulture species in the region, but that number has halved over the past 10 years. Not many vultures are still present along the Mekong River in the Siem Pang Wildlife Sanctuary in Stung Treng Province and the Chep Wildlife Sanctuary in Preah Vihear Province.
