Senior official of the Ministry of Public Works confirms the implementation of the law to stop 5 overweight trucks
(Phnom Penh): A senior official of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport confirmed the law enforcement of the Ministry's mobile team, which recently stopped five overweight trucks, in accordance with the law.
This confirmation was made after the Chief of Spean Thmor Commune, Dangkor District and some land truck owners asked Samdech Techo Metta to intervene with the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to release five land trucks that were detained by the Ministry's mobile team. Recently, to help repair the road in the local and resume business.
Mr. Kimsan said that the five land trucks seized by the Ministry's mobile team on September 6 were carrying up to 20 percent, so it is a legal measure to be fined and detained for a period of time. 1 more year.
He said that what the Ministry's mobile working group is doing is in accordance with the Law on Roads under Articles 60, 26 and 25, which relate to overweight. There is also a law on road traffic related to some crimes where drivers drive stubbornly and do not listen to the call of the authorities.
The official also said that the Ministry's working group has some understanding and related to the overweight, according to the development of the country, because according to the law can lead to arrest, revocation of driving licenses or stop driving. But today, just stop the car and pay the fine.
Mr. Kimsan added that in the past, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol had said that it is very difficult for us to find funds to build roads because it takes a lot of money, some kilometers cost more than 1 million dollars. Therefore, he called on people to respect the law and take care of our roads together so that we can use them for a long time.
For this detailed explanation, the wisdom of the Dangkor district authority, especially Mr. Hang Chum, the chief of Spean Thmor commune, understood this detailed explanation and agreed to participate in the implementation of the law to restrict overweight traffic on the road. To avoid overloading, destroy national roads.
