(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Municipal Police on September 10, 2022 came out to clarify and completely reject the baseless allegations in the sense of defaming law enforcement officers over the death of a suspect in connection with the theft. .
According to Fresh News, Colonel San Sok Seiha, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, confirmed that the suspect's death was caused by chronic kidney failure and that the authorities had sufficient forensic evidence confirmed by a specialist doctor and Some security camera evidence as well.
Colonel San Sok Seiha described that on August 22, 2022 at 2:16 AM, the victim named Sok Vannak came to report and file a complaint at the Kork Roka Administrative Police Station of the Prek Pnov District Police Inspectorate for missing car parts. Under the porch of house No. 200, Street D in Borey Pi Phop Thmey Chhouk Va 1, Phlou Paem village, Sangkat Kork Roka, Khan Prek Pnov.
After receiving a complaint from the victim, the police intervened at the scene and searched for the suspect by opening the security camera near the scene and found 3 suspects: First: Hai Bunna, second: Kim Chhon and third: Kim Sour, stole the victim's car parts on August 21, 2022 at 02:16 and escaped.
Until August 25, 2022, at 06:30 pm, the police conducted a search and arrested the three suspects at the point on the concrete road, Andong 3 village, Sangkat Kork Roka, Khan Prek Pnov, for interrogation at the Kork Roka Administrative Police Station. The three suspects confessed that they had stolen the victim's car parts at the scene on August 21, 2022, and sold them for 100,000 Riels. Come and share and spend.
It was not until September 1, 2022, at 4:30 pm, that the police sent the suspect, Hai Bunna, to the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital for treatment by the General Department of Prisons, Ministry of Interior, 1st Correctional Center. Management continued until the 3rd of the same month at 4:30 pm, suddenly the suspect named Hay Bunna died at the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital.
After that, the scene analysis office of the Police Technical and Scientific Department of the Ministry of Interior and Mr. Oknha Dr. Nong Sovannaroth, Phnom Penh Medical Examiner, as well as officials representing the General Department of Prisons, the 1st Correctional Center (M1) of the Ministry of Interior visited. An autopsy revealed that the suspect, Hay Bunna, had died of late-stage kidney failure.
