Ministry of Justice Establishes Working Group on Combating All Forms of Human Trafficking, Labor Trafficking, Labor Exploitation and Sexual Exploitation (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Minister of Justice Keut Rith All forms of human trafficking, labor trafficking, labor exploitation and the sex trade.
The Task Force of the Ministry of Justice is responsible for the fight against all forms of human trafficking, labor trafficking, and sex trafficking, with the following roles and responsibilities:
Coordinate procedures to investigate, search and control foreigners on suspicious targets in order to arrest the perpetrators and rescue the victims in a timely manner.
Promote and strengthen the investigation, prosecution, investigation and prosecution of human trafficking, labor trafficking and sexual exploitation in strict accordance with applicable laws and procedures.
Collect, compile and compile statistical data on investigations, charges, investigations and convictions for human trafficking, labor trafficking and sex trafficking.
* Promote the investigation, prosecution, investigation and prosecution of money laundering offenses in accordance with the law and the Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) in force, in collaboration with the Ministry of Justice's anti-money laundering and terrorist financing and financing agencies. Disseminate weapons of mass destruction in case the team finds clues to money laundering crimes resulting from human trafficking, labor trafficking and sex trafficking
* Regularly report on the results of work to the Minister of Justice
Perform other duties as determined by the Minister of Justice.
The following is Mr. Keut Rith's decision:
