The assailant who stabbed the victim in the left wrist in Sihanoukville was arrested by the police in Phnom Penh
(Preah Sihanouk): The perpetrator involved in the case of cutting the victim's left wrist in Sangkat 1, Sihanoukville last weekend, was searched by police and arrested on September 9 2022 Yesterday, behind Wat Trom Chreung, Kngok village, Sangkat Boeung Thom, Khan Kampoul, Phnom Penh.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Chuon Narin told Fresh News this morning, September 10, 2022 that the operation was carried out by the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police in cooperation with the Criminal Police Department of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police and Kandal Provincial Police.
According to the General Commissioner in front of the police, the suspect confessed that on September 4, 2022, he actually used a machete to cut the victim, causing his left wrist to break. He escaped and hid in Phnom Penh.
After arresting the suspect, the competent authorities of the Sihanoukville Police Inspectorate took the suspect to point out where he threw the knife behind the construction site next to the volleyball table near Wat Leu.
It should be informed that on September 4, 2022, there was a case of aggravated violence (using a machete to cut the victim, causing the left wrist to be amputated), seriously injured at the factory near Wat Leu, Group 15, Village 3 Sangkat 1, Sihanoukville, caused by the suspect named Vong Veasna, alias Cho, 32 years old, temporarily staying at a construction site near Wat Leu, Group 15, Village 3, Sangkat 1, Sihanoukville.
The victim in this incident is Choeun Cheat, 34 years old, a construction worker who lives at the scene. The victim is currently receiving emergency treatment at a Chinese hospital at the corner of a traffic light.
