Royal Government Encourages Recruitment of Local Officials for Sub-National Administration (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia encourages recruitment of local officials for various positions in Sub-National Administration to Ensure work efficiency and comply with the principles of decentralization and deconcentration policies.
This encouragement was made during a cabinet meeting chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Friday morning, September 9, 2022.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has also raised this issue. This is because Samdech has seen that the appointment of officials for positions in sub-national administrations is often selected from various ministries and institutions at the national level.
To decide Techo Hun Sen, the appointment of officials from the national level to positions at the sub-national level makes local officials dissatisfied and the service of the people is not in accordance with the wishes of the people.
Board of Engineers of Cambodia launches laboratory for forensic engineering
(Phnom Penh): The Board of Engineers of Cambodia has inaugurated its laboratory to assist in the management, inspection, analysis, monitoring and forensic examination of the engineering profession of professional engineers at the Board of Engineers of Cambodia to develop the national engineering intellectual resources that are needed. Necessary to build the country.
The inauguration ceremony of this laboratory was held at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh on the afternoon of September 9, 2022, presided over by Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training and Chairman of the Board of Engineers of Cambodia.
He said that the development of engineering resources is one of the strongest and indispensable driving force for the development of a prosperous society. Therefore, it is necessary to increase the leadership mechanism to make this engineering institution a strong center that can contribute to the Royal Government in developing a sustainable social development plan.
He said that these achievements are achieved due to the introduction of policies, strategies and development plans that are clear, combined with the mechanisms of each institution that has effective management in all areas, including the significant progress. Notice on the infrastructure sector, where high-rise buildings are booming, the construction of intersecting roads, subways, airways, highways, and so on.
Royal Government advises to pay attention to flood response
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has instructed the National Committee for Disaster Management and all relevant authorities to increase their attention to responding to floods caused by floods, floods and the Mekong River.
This instruction was made in the meeting of the Council of Ministers this morning, September 9, 2022, chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
According to the results of the meeting of the Council of Ministers, during the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructed all relevant authorities to be prepared and take the necessary measures to save the lives of the people in the responsible areas. Timely and minimize the hardships and impact on the property and lives of the people.
According to the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, Cambodia will be affected by low pressure from neighboring countries, which will cause heavy rains throughout the country. This could lead to flooding in some areas of Cambodia.
In recent days, some areas in the northwestern province bordering Thailand have suffered some flooding due to rain and runoff from Thailand.
However, the relevant authorities, especially Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice-Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, who is the staff of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, have been monitoring and preparing for the rescue of the people. So far, however, the floods in the Thai border provinces have not yet reached serious levels.
