(Phnom Penh): For September 08, 2022, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking (NCDD), received 17 more complaints. Involves requesting intervention in cases of detention and trafficking. This is according to General Khieu Sopheak, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, confirmed to Fresh News.
The general stated that in the complaint, 15 Chinese, 4 Malaysians, 4 Vietnamese, 1 Taiwanese and 1 Cambodian were requested to intervene.
According to a spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, from August 18, 2022 to September 08, 2022, Samdech Krala Hom received a total of 154 complaints related to the request for intervention to rescue foreigners who were claimed to be in detention. And labor trafficking.
It should be noted that Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng recently issued a letter calling on the national and international public, the Foreign Representation in Cambodia and the competent authorities of the countries concerned to continue to provide information related to human trafficking and other transnational crimes to prevent And crack down in a timely and effective manner.
In the meeting of the Council of Ministers on the morning of September 9, the Royal Government of Cambodia also issued strict orders to all capital, provincial and local administrations, as well as relevant authorities to launch a campaign to fight and suppress drug crimes. Trafficking and smuggling of human beings, forced labor and sex work effectively.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen praises Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara for his efforts to address illegal construction in the Angkor area
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, praised Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, for his leadership and cooperation with relevant ministries and authorities in resolving the problem of illegal construction in the Angkor area and the region. Other.
