(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to suspend the celebration of the Royal Water Festival, floating lanterns and worshiping the moon Ok Ambok 2022 for the national level. This decision was made in a meeting of the Council of Ministers chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia this morning, September 9, 2022.
Although the Royal Water Festival, the floating of lanterns and the worship of the moon Ok Ambok for the national level has been postponed, the organization of the Water Festival in various capitals and provinces throughout the country is possible as far as possible. To make people happy, increase the tourism environment, as well as provide opportunities for people to earn money.
