(Phnom Penh): To implement the Law on Construction and related legal documents in order to promote the beauty of the environment and the rights of people with disabilities for sustainable living and environment, the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction has recently issued 5 points of advice for land development project owners, construction project owners and construction owners in Cambodia.
According to this instruction, land development project owners, construction project owners and construction owners must implement the following:
First, to prepare a waterproof garden and plant luxury trees such as Thnong Neang Nuon Kranhong and prepare a green garden with fragrant grass and flowers in the land development project, construction project or construction as defined in Sub-Decree No. 42 Dated April 3, 2015 on the urbanization of capitals, cities and towns.
Third, to have a common bin for storing solid waste bags packed in bags in its location or management area and solid waste bins in each private area and garbage disposal port, as well as Sanitation management in accordance with technical standards in all land development projects, construction projects or constructions as defined in Sub-Decree No. 113, dated August 27, 2015 on Urban Solid Waste Management.
Fifth, to set up mailboxes for multi-functional building projects, mixed-use buildings, commercial buildings, co-ownership buildings and to set up mailboxes for private residences according to the technical standards set by the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications.
