Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration Informs Owners of Locations Where Foreigners Reside and Work to Report to Local Authorities Regularly
(Preah Sihanouk): The Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration has issued a notice to the site owners, who are the managers of buildings where foreigners live and work, to participate in strengthening security, public order, security and safety for foreigners.
At the same time, the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration has requested the landlord or manager of the place where foreigners live and work to report on the presence of foreigners under their control to the local authority on a regular basis.
This report must be sent to the Commune / Sangkat Administrative Police Station where the building is located before September 24, 2022. The provincial administration urges all building owners to act responsibly from the time of this announcement.
Two students were killed and two others were seriously injured when a motorcyclist turned left on a bicycle.
(Svay Rieng): A horrific traffic accident caused by a schoolboy riding a bicycle turning left carelessly hit by a motorcycle driving in the opposite direction, causing the immediate loss of life and two other male and female motorcyclists Serious injuries.
The incident happened at 11:20 a.m. on September 9, 2022 on a paved road in Chambok Kong village, Kampong Chak commune, Romduol district, Svay Rieng province.
According to Romduol district police, the dead student was 9-year-old Long Bunheng, a resident of Chambok Kong village, Kampong Chak commune, Romduol district, Svay Rieng province.
According to witnesses at the scene, prior to the incident, a schoolboy was riding a bicycle on a paved road from west to east and turned left carelessly when a motorbike appeared. Two people riding in opposite directions, the brakes are not fully hit, causing a surprise.
At present, the dead boy has been recorded and handed over to his family for a traditional ceremony, while the two seriously injured have been taken to Samaki Rumduol Referral Hospital. As for the evidence of the two vehicles, the authorities measured and dragged them to be stored at the Romduol District Police Inspectorate for later handling according to the law.
