(Phnom Penh): On September 7, 2022, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking (NCDD), received 12 related complaints. And requesting intervention in cases of labor detention and trafficking. This is according to General Khieu Sopheak, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, confirmed to Fresh News.
The general stated that out of the 12 complaints, 16 foreigners were requested to be intervened, including 10 Chinese, 4 Vietnamese and 2 Taiwanese, and 4 of them were received from General Commission of National Police. Among the lawsuits are in Oddar Meanchey, Preah Sihanouk, Koh Kong, Kandal and Phnom Penh.
From August 18, 2022 to September 7, 2022, Samdech Krala Hom received a total of 137 complaints related to the request for intervention to rescue foreigners who were allegedly detained and trafficked in Cambodia. Of these, 274 foreigners were asked to search for 10 nationalities.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking, Samdech Krala Hom expressed his regret and condemnation of these inhumane acts. Samdech also thanked and welcomed the information provided by individuals and foreign representatives in Cambodia in the past related to the above case.
The Royal Government of Cambodia also remains committed to complying with applicable laws to combat fraud and technology extortion, drug offenses, money laundering and illegal online gambling, and to continue to provide protection. And save both Cambodians who are victims of trafficking abroad and rescue foreigners who are victims of trafficking in Cambodia.
