The postal sector is considered to have the potential to contribute to sustaining economic growth and improving the quality of life of the people of Cambodia by connecting it with daily life in urban and rural areas.
Developing a development policy for the postal sector is crucial as a beacon to guide the development of priority action plans to respond to the evolving needs of both social and economic needs in line with the international postal development framework to expand the scope of services. Post quality, efficiency and sustainability to the people.
This policy aims to develop the postal sector and the postal service market to serve businesses, enterprises and people effectively, sustainably and innovatively to contribute to national socio-economic development.
The policy sets four goals, including: 1. Improving the management of the postal sector to ensure the improvement of service quality and protect the interests of consumers.
2: Modernize postal services, develop infrastructure, expand postal network to reach a wider population and use digital technology.
3. Facilitate the private sector to do business in the postal sector, transport and postal distribution by promoting fair competition.
4: Promote the role of Cambodia Post in providing postal services.
To achieve the goals and objectives of the postal sector development, eight key strategies have been identified. Those strategies include:
1: Strengthen the legal framework related to the management and development of the postal sector
2: Establish a mechanism to improve the quality of postal services and protect the interests of consumers
3: Promoting occupational safety and environmental sustainability in postal business operations
4: Develop physical infrastructure, postal logistics network and promote digital transformation of postal ecosystems, services and postal network.
5: Better management of the private sector postal service business
6: Promote the increase of the capacity of Cambodia Post to conduct business operations
7: Establish a global postal service obligation program and support the provision of public services by the Royal Government
8. Promote capacity building, research and innovation in the postal sector. Each strategy has priority activities, which are projects to be implemented from 2022 to 2030.
The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications will play a collaborative role and coordinate with ministries, institutions, private sector development partners, national and international organizations to implement priority activities to achieve the above strategy under the monitoring and evaluation system, with measurable target indicators. .
With the implementation of this policy, all stakeholders are required to have high political will and commitment to benefit the people and make the postal sector achieve its full potential as a sector contributing to economic diversification. Cambodia.
