An audio message of the order sent to the commanders of the units under the Army was leaked on social media on Thursday night, September 08, 2022.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet emphasized in an audio message that combating and preventing the use of drugs in military units is a task that he attaches the utmost attention to and does not allow.
The Army Commander, who graduated from the U.S. Military Academy, recommended the implementation of measures against the military using two conditions. In that, the military uses drugs in various units, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet gives the right to the unit commander to check whether to educate or dismiss from the unit.
However, Dr. Hun Manet does not want to see too lax or understanding measures that lead other armies not to be afraid of the army's actions.
Separately, for military trainees or staff working in the military academy under the Army, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet issued a strict order not to favor or educate, namely military trainees and staff who train or serve in the military academy. Those who use drugs must be expelled from the army.
Dr. Hun Manet emphasized that "the school must be implemented strictly. In this school case, those who use drugs do not have access to education, they are excluded from the army. For this school, not only the soldiers, military officers or staff of the school, trainees sent from any unit to see the use of drugs during the study, we have to cut out.
A senior official of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF), who has undergone many reforms in the army, instructed the commanders of the various units of the army to be very strict in enforcing this order to prevent drug use in the unit. Troops.
