Siem Reap Provincial Administration Rejects Khem Veasna's Allegations of Taking Transportation Home and Calls Allegations of Diverting Attention to Its Deception
(Siem Reap): The Siem Reap provincial administration has reacted strongly to Khem Veasna, president of the Coalition for Democracy Party, alleging that authorities took money to transport people from the plantation back home. The Siem Reap provincial administration has denied the allegations and called the allegations by Khem Veasna diverting public attention to its deception.
The reaction of the Siem Reap provincial administration came after Mr. Khem Veasna posted on his Facebook page at around 12 noon on September 7, 2022, accusing the Siem Reap provincial authorities of taking 10 dollars. 100,000 to 200,000 Riels for transporting people who volunteered to leave the gathering place to their homes and did not provide food or water.
The provincial administration claims that under the care of the Royal Government, headed by Samdech Techo Prime Minister, the Provincial Administrative Unity Command has organized a team of doctors, ambulances, vehicles to transport people back to their homes and distribute food free of charge. 19 people and 3 cars. Most of the people and activists of the Coalition for Democracy decided to return to their homes by personal means or relatives or rent transportation.
With this reaction, the Siem Reap Provincial Administration welcomes and requests Mr. Khem Veasna and the people affected by the above allegations to present the evidence to the Siem Reap Provincial Administrative Team, which has a temporary headquarters in front of the pepper plantation in Thmor Choul Village, Khum Commune. Tbeng, Banteay Srey district or Siem Reap provincial hall, or contact 078 800 988.
In a press release reacting to Mr. Khem Veasna on September 08, 2022, the Siem Reap Provincial Administration stressed that the individual Khem Veasna continues to have bad intentions, continue to lie, deceive, accuse and blame the Ministry of Interior delegation. And the Provincial Administrative Unity Command in the sense of diverting the attention of its supporters or losing its past deceptive tactics.
In this press release, the Siem Reap Provincial Administration also considered Mr. Khem Veasna's announcement regarding the end of the world news due to the flood as a propaganda of unscientific information, propaganda of superstition, fantasy, and misrepresentation.
The provincial administration added that the gathering organized by Mr. Khem Veasna caused many consequences, including: family relationships, livelihood problems, job loss, loss of property, loss of time, school dropouts, health problems, risks. With Kovid-19 and other diseases.
