Minister Thong Khon Shares Cambodia's Experience in Rehabilitating Tourism at Vietnam International Tourism Fair
(VOVworld) - Cambodian Minister of Tourism Thong Khon has shared the experience of the Royal Government of Cambodia during the Kovid Crisis in Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam on September 8, 2022. 19 High-Level Forum on Solutions on International Tourism Rehabilitation and Sustainable Development, attended by approximately 350 participants.
The main points of sharing this experience are focused on preventing the spread of Kovid 19 and Kovid 19 vaccination strategies for the people of Cambodia, the restoration of tourism during and after the Kovid 19 crisis, the future vision of the sector Tourism, in particular, strengthening connections to revitalize tourism.
The high-level forum in Ho Chi Minh City was chaired by Vu Duc Dam, a member of the Party Central Committee and Deputy Prime Minister of Vietnam. Tourism Authority, Consulate General of ASEAN Member States, International Private Sector, a total of 350 people.
On that occasion, Mr. Thong Khon shared his Cambodian experience to the forum on vaccination of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to ensure immunity in the community leading to the opening. Socio-economic recovery, especially the reopening of the country to receive full international tourism.
The Minister also highlighted the effectiveness of the implementation of rescue measures and interventions put in place by the Royal Government to rescue businesses and tourism workers, among other socio-economic sectors.
In his participation, the Minister shared four key recommendations to strengthen connectivity to restore regional and international tourism in a sustainable manner as follows:
1. In the future, vaccines remain the key to building tourism confidence in travel: In the face of the world embracing a new normal path of living, that is, living with Kovid-19, the vaccine is the only tool to contribute to life insurance. Tourists as well as restore the confidence and trust of tourists. Therefore, tourist destinations should continue and increase vaccination.
4. ASEAN Tourism Ministers, ASEAN Partners and World Tourism Leaders should continue to strengthen human resource development, promote digital connectivity, promote innovation and innovation in the context of the 4.0 generation industry and the future trends of tourism.
5. Minister Thong Khon went on to highlight the efforts to promote online training (e-learning) and digital literacy that the Royal Government of Cambodia, as well as the Ministry of Tourism, has implemented during the Kovid 19 crisis and in the recovery and promotion of tourism. Repeat this.
6. In addition, the Royal Government has cooperated with banks and microfinance institutions to provide a total of $ 150 million for co-financing for business owners in the tourism sector to apply for loans to renovate their business locations. Those businesses must be registered with the Ministry of Tourism and recognized by the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
