Skeleton found in Sangkat Kakap II, Khan Por Sen Chey
At more than 5 pm on September 7, 2022, the owner of a plot of land cleared the forest and found the dead body of a man with only a skeleton in his forest plot in Prey Sala village, Sangkat Kakap II, Khan Por Sen Chey. Also reported to the police, causing a surprise.
Immediately after receiving the news, on the morning of September 8, his wife and daughter and siblings went to see the clothes and knew that they were her husband and father, who had been missing for more than a year. Afterwards, the skeletons were taken to be cremated at Wat Tang Sang South.
The deceased was identified as Tep Pheap, 37, a scavenger, his wife Sek Sitha, 38, a son and a daughter in the family. In the same village. According to the forensic results of the Phnom Penh Technical Council, the man died of cholera.
The wife said that in the past, her husband was a waiter in Ly Kea shop in Pochentong, but later due to the outbreak, the shop was closed and her husband was unemployed. Then, not knowing what to do, her husband went to pick up scrap metal for sale, then went out to pick it up in the morning and returned home in the evening every day.
The woman said that on July 14, 2021, she disappeared forever, while she searched everywhere but could not find him. For more than a year now, she has no hope of being able to Not found.
