He pointed out that out of the 164 complaints, 74 were sent to other institutions to resolve, 7 were unresolved, 5 were withdrawn, 103 were investigated and resolved by a delegation. Closing 23 cases, referring to other institutions to resolve 9 complaints, writing letters to promote 21 complaints, complainants request to resolve 17 complaints.
Commentary: Relations between Cambodia and China have reached a new historical level.
(Phnom Penh): A senior official of the Royal Government of Cambodia said that the relationship between Cambodia and China has reached a new historical level. He also praised the Belt and Road (BRI) initiative, which is rapidly closing the development gap in the world, as the initiative will run for 10 years by 2023.
In a recent interview with Cambodia-China Friendship Radio, HE Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Deputy Prime Minister, said that relations between Cambodia and China have reached a new historical level.
He stressed that the bilateral relations between the two countries have been strengthened in all areas as a deepening strategic partnership in all fields. At the same time, Cambodia has received a lot of support from China, such as investment and trade, and the two sides have signed a bilateral free trade agreement, which brings great benefits to the Cambodian people.
In addition, Cambodia has also benefited from Chinese investment in infrastructure development, such as roads, ports, etc., which HE believes that this is a continuation of the long-standing relationship under the leadership of Samdech Hun Sen, the Prime Minister. And is building further to strengthen this bilateral relationship.
He emphasized that the strengthening of bilateral relations was an important task for the diplomatic, political, economic, commercial and cultural sectors, between parliament and parliament, government and civil society, and the private sector between the two countries. Overall, HE Dr. assessed that Cambodia and China have so far strengthened bilateral relations at all levels and in all fields, which has greatly expanded.
In 2023, the 10th anniversary of the Belt and Road Initiative, he asserted that the initiative, which is not just an idea but a practical one, has benefited countries around the world. Significantly, there has been considerable development, which demonstrates China's increasingly important role in the world through the Belt and Road Initiative.
According to HE Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, for Cambodia, there are many benefits from BRI, such as: the construction of thousands of kilometers of roads, bridges, ports, airports, special economic zones and hospitals are all that Cambodia needs most and benefits. These are really given to the people of Cambodia, not just the Royal Government.
"So the project that we got through BRI to help the Cambodian people is the ultimate goal, so we have to thank China for helping Cambodia through this BRI to accelerate Cambodia's development in 10 years." "Last year."
"Not only that, the Chinese people have sacrificed a lot to help countries all over the world, not only Cambodia has really contributed a lot, and the Chinese people today have made a lot of progress under Leading the policy of the Chinese government. "
