Cambodia-China Friendship Radio announces the new position of Director of Battambang Provincial Department of Social Affairs, Minister Vong Soth advised to work hard to fulfill the duties of the people in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government
(Battambang): Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, on the morning of September 08, 2022, presided over the inauguration ceremony of the new Director of the Battambang Provincial Department of Social Affairs with the participation of Mr. Sok Loo, Governor of Battambang Province. , Mr. Uy Ry, Chairman of the Provincial Council, many other relevant officials, including commune chiefs throughout Battambang province, a total of 103 communes.
Mr. Phuong Sithy has been appointed as the new Director of the Battambang Provincial Department of Social Affairs, replacing Mr. Kim Teng, the former Director of the Battambang Provincial Department of Social Affairs.
Speaking on that occasion, Mr. Vong Soth commended the leadership of civil servants in the Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation of Battambang Province for their hard work in achieving better results by cooperating with relevant departments, units and development partners. Local authorities, national and international civil society organizations to assist the victims and the vulnerable.
At the same time, Mr. Vong Soth instructed the newly appointed Director of the Provincial Department to make more efforts to fulfill his duties to serve the interests of the people and the motherland in accordance with the policies of the Royal Government and the upper level. Strengthening social welfare services for the poor and vulnerable and strengthening institutional capacity, partnerships, mobilizing resources to increase the efficiency of social services.
The Minister also requested the relevant departments, provincial administrations, authorities at all levels, especially local officials to cooperate in implementing this work to be transparent and highly effective.
He said that the new director of the department must continue to maintain the tradition of internal unity and close cooperation between civil servants in the unit, as well as institutions, departments, civil society units in the implementation of its core work and follow the guidelines of the Ministry responsibly.
On the occasion of receiving this new position, Mr. Phuong Sithy also committed to strictly respect and implement the programs and policies of the Royal Government and the recommendations of Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Battambang.
