General Chhum Socheat Leads a Delegation of the Ministry of National Defense to Participate in the Defense Dialogue in Seoul 2022
While leading a delegation of the Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia to attend three meetings in the Republic of Korea, on September 7, 2022, General Chhum Socheat, Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense, attended the Seoul 2022 Defense Dialogue held in Seoul. Seoul.
The dialogue was organized by the Ministry of Defense of the Republic of Korea under the theme "How to Resolve Complex Security Challenges: Strengthening International Solidarity" with 54 participating countries, including representatives of the Ministry of Defense, national security experts, and the United Nations. The European Union and the North Atlantic Treaty Organization (NATO) to discuss finding common ways to respond to regional and international security threats.
The Seoul Defense Dialogue 2022 will be held with a number of plenary discussions focusing on key topics such as the first round of talks on cooperation and international measures for the complete denuclearization of North Korea, and the second round of talks on exploration. Confidence-building cooperation in the Indo-Pacific and the third round of talks on the role of the military in Hybrid Warfare.
At the opening ceremony, Lee Jung-soo, Minister of Defense of the Republic of Korea, stated that the main purpose of the Ministry of Defense of the Republic of Korea in organizing the dialogue is to strengthen and enhance the multilateral forum that serves as a forum for cooperation. Regional and international defense operations.
The ROK Defense Minister also stressed that the choice of topics for this year's Seoul Defense Dialogue really reflects the realities of the current regional and global strategic security environment, which requires a strategic dialogue to Address issues that are a common concern.
This is the 11th time that the Ministry of Defense of the Republic of Korea has held the Seoul Defense Dialogue since 2012, which is a high-level multilateral dialogue aimed at contributing to peace talks on the Korean Peninsula and promoting cooperation. Security operations in the Asia-Pacific region.
