Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Inaugurates Two Buildings Worth More Than $ 14 Million at Phnom Penh Police
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, presided over the inauguration ceremony of the 10-storey administrative building and 3-storey meeting hall of the Police Commission this morning. Phnom Penh.
The ceremony was also attended by senators, members of the National Assembly, leaders of the Royal Government, leaders of the Ministry of Interior, General Commissioner of the National Police, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the National Gendarmerie, Deputy Commissioner General of Civil Service and the three Armed Forces. Too many, too.
According to the report of General Sar Thet, Deputy Commissioner General and Commissioner of Police of Phnom Penh, said that seeing the condition of the existing administrative building is old and can not guarantee the performance of duties, I respectfully report to Prince Kralahom Sar Kheng to be aware of these situations and difficulties and respect the principles to build new buildings instead.
After receiving the principle of approval and support from Samdech Krala Hom, he tried to raise funds from various philanthropists to support the construction, and on May 9, 2019, the construction of two buildings was started by giving the right to ENG CONSTRUCTOR. The construction contract was signed for two years, but due to the status of Kovid 19, it took more than 3 years to complete the construction on May 6, 2022.
Taking this opportunity, General Sar Thet would like to further clarify the functions of the two buildings as follows:
* Building 1: The administration building is organized as a working place for the 13 special plans, which is 40 meters wide, 50 meters long, with a total area of 20,000 square meters and a height of 10 floors, each floor has an area of 2,000 square meters.
* Building 2: A three-story meeting hall with a width of 30 meters, a length of 40 meters, with a total area of 3,600 square meters, with each floor area of 1,200 square meters. The first floor is a space for organizing various events. The second floor is the residence of the commanding officer, and the third floor is the auditorium, which can accommodate between 500 and 600 people.
Separately, at the beginning of 2022, the Phnom Penh Municipal Police has started to build a new building with a width of 25 meters, a length of 75 meters, a height of 2 floors, with a total area of 3,750 square meters, each floor has 1 area. 875 square meters to be used as a permanent room, living room and canteen for the fire brigade.
