Xi Jinping and Putin to meet in Uzbekistan next week
MOSCOW, Sept. 7 (Xinhua) - Russian President Vladimir Putin and Chinese President Xi Jinping will meet next week at a summit in Uzbekistan, a Russian official said on Wednesday.
Putin and Xi last met in Beijing in February, weeks before the Kremlin sent troops into Ukraine. The two presidents attended the signing ceremony of an agreement, promising that relations between the two sides will be unlimited. It remains unclear whether Xi was aware of Russia's plans to launch what Moscow calls "special military operations" in Ukraine.
