Diplomat: Cambodia suffers the most from cultural trade in ASEAN due to civil war and instability (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, says Cambodia is the hardest hit. They trade in cultural assets compared to other ASEAN countries and suffer from civil war and instability.
The head of the Cambodian diplomatic corps said this via video at the International Conference on the Prevention and Control of Illegal Trafficking in Cultural Property: ASEAN Perspectives, held in Siem Reap from 5 to 8 September 2022.
In a video shared by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs on September 7, 2022, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon stated, "Compared to other ASEAN countries, I believe that Cambodia has suffered the most in "Trafficking, vandalism, theft and illegal mining during decades of civil war and instability."
He said that due to the growing demand of the black market in the trade of cultural property, there has been a scattering of many temples, heritage sites and ancient sites.
Preventing the illegal trade in cultural property, Mr. Prak Sokhon claimed that this is a sensitive issue that Cambodia has been facing and trying to solve for many years.
He added that it was no coincidence that the Minister of Culture and Fine Arts, Ms. Phoeung Sakona, had invited a national and international delegation to attend the International Conference on the Protection of Cultural Property in Siem Reap, a region rich in cultural heritage, a region of refuge. Angkor Heritage will be accompanied by thousands of ancient temples and is a UNESCO World Heritage Site.
"I believe that in Cambodia, Siem Reap is the best province and also the ASEAN cultural city for the Minister of Culture and the Arts to meet to discuss the sensitive issues of illegal trade in our cultural assets." This is according to Mr. Prak Sokhon.
The Cambodian head of diplomacy also expressed his pleasure at the fact that the delegation was personally present here to see the richness of Cambodian culture, the beauty of the artifacts and to get preliminary information about the challenges we are facing. Experiencing the protection of cultural property to combat theft, piracy and illegal trade in the international art market.
