(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, on the morning of September 7, 2022, led the officials of departments around the province to celebrate the release of 100,000 fish and plant seedlings in Thmor Da village, Boeung Nay commune, Prey Chhor district.
The provincial governor reminded that every year from the beginning of June until the end of September is the closed fishing season to allow the mother fish to spawn for the next year. That is why we have chosen this day and place to hold a fish release ceremony and a tree planting ceremony, and also to declare the end of the fishing season in the province as well as throughout the country.
The governor said that as you know, our country is rich in freshwater fish because of the Tonle Sap Lake, river system, rivers, lakes, which can provide a large amount of fish to serve as food for our people. In fact, our country has a good quality rice area in line with the needs of the people and the growing world market.
In particular, the fisheries sector in Cambodia is also part of the national income of many people involved in the fisheries sector, such as full-time fishermen, part-time fishermen, occasional fishermen, fishery processors or fishermen. And so on. That is why Cambodia can be considered a fish-eating society, with an average of 52.40 kg of fish per person per year.
The provincial governor confirmed that our country is rich in freshwater fish, supplying enough food for our people. But lately, Cambodia's fisheries sector has been affected by global climate change, illegal fishing, and so on.
