Comment: ASEAN countries expect peace in Taiwan Strait
Internationally, most countries have a clear understanding of the causes of the tense situation in the Taiwan Strait, especially in Southeast Asia, which is still pushing the Taiwan Strait. As long as the Taiwan Strait is affected, Southeast Asian countries will definitely be affected, so these countries are very interested in the situation in the Taiwan Strait.
Currently, the biggest consensus of ASEAN countries is not to expect China and the United States to clash. Singapore Foreign Minister Vivian Balakrishnan notes that if Sino-US relations break down, it will mean that commodity prices will rise sharply, and the effects of the global supply chain will fall further, becoming more chaotic and increasingly fragmented. Danger.
If you look at the United States, it can be seen that the United States has always provoked the issue of Taiwan, which is contrary to the purpose and efforts of ASEAN to maintain peace and stability in the region, the United States has not only destroyed the interests of ASEAN. Both have seriously undermined regional security and stability, so ASEAN countries have a clear understanding of their strategic goals.
