The introduction of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng was made this morning, September 7, 2022, on the occasion of presiding over the handover ceremony and appointing Lt. Gen. Em Vichet as the Inspector General of the Inspectorate of the Ministry of Interior to replace Mr. Iv. Leang, who was appointed Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Interior.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng emphasized that all complaints, requests of the people or the public opinion is a bright mirror for officials to see the problem to improve, and therefore Samdech advised to collect all those issues to see if it is true or not. True and there are remedial measures.
Samdech continued to emphasize the efforts to collect and accept the requests, suggestions and concerns of the people related to the authority of the Ministry of Interior, whether from the people directly or from the media and through any channel. Samdech advised the new Secretary General and Secretary of State in charge to pay more attention to resolving this issue quickly and effectively, as many other complaints and requests have not yet been resolved.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also spoke about the anti-trafficking operation, which recently received 117 complaints from the Ministry of Interior. He stressed that all operations must adhere to three main principles: rescue the victims, crack down on illegal locations and punish the perpetrators, because human trafficking is an issue that international attention and Cambodia must pay attention to. Strong too.
(Phnom Penh): Next week, Cambodia will host the 54th ASEAN Economic Ministers' Meeting and related meetings held in Siem Reap. The official opening ceremony of this important meeting will be presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chair of ASEAN.
To ensure the success of this meeting as planned, Cambodia, as the chair of ASEAN and the chair of the meeting, has been preparing for several months. The Royal Government of Cambodia has established an Inter-Ministerial Committee chaired by Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and Chairman of the ASEAN Economic Ministers' Meeting, to organize and organize this important meeting.
Mr. Pan Sosak has chaired the meeting to review and update this work many times. On the morning of September 6, 2022, Mr. Pan Sosak chaired a meeting to review the preparations for this meeting for the last time.
The meeting was attended by the Permanent Secretary of State, the Chairman, the Vice-Chairman and the members of the Sub-Committee and the Secretariat Working Group, relevant officials, as well as Excellencies, Lok Chumteavs and experts from relevant ministries and institutions.
According to the sub-committees, the preparations for the 54th ASEAN Economic Ministers' Meeting and related meetings have been completed as planned.
However, Minister Pan Sosak made some recommendations to each subcommittee and the Secretariat to ensure that the meeting was a success.
Minister Pan Sosak said that the preparation process has progressed well and went smoothly despite some obstacles. Problems and especially good solidarity with each other.
The Minister thanked and commended all the chairpersons and vice chairmen of the sub-committees for their dedication to fulfilling their duties and responsibilities in a proactive and responsible manner in organizing meetings under the community pillars. The economy to run smoothly and get good results for the nation.
(Phnom Penh): The first Phnom Penh Forum on the Role of Brain Bank, NGOs and the Media has been compared by national and international scholars and experts to "three angles" contributing to social power, ensuring stability, progress and Social prosperity. In particular, it has contributed to the formulation of policies with quality, accountability, transparency and environment.
The Phnom Penh Forum was held on September 7, 2022, an initiative of the Institute of International Relations of Cambodia of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, with a total of 22 keynote speakers from Cambodia, Indonesia, Malaysia, Laos, Thailand, Vietnam and the United States. Australia, Germany, Italy, etc., all of whom specialize in policy work and are veteran journalists with a doctoral degree.
Dr. Yong Pov, Secretary General of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, believes that "Brain Bank, NGOs and the media like outside the government are like , contributing to social power, ensuring stability, progress and social prosperity. In addition, it also contributes to the formulation of policies with quality, accountability, transparency and environment. This is the view of a group of doctors and national-international experts.
"The quality of national, regional, international and global policies is inseparable from the contribution of ," he said. "We see that the main emerging issues and challenges that nations have been able to address have always involved actors, banks, brains, NGOs and the media."
According to Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Institute of International Relations of Cambodia of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, "The Bank for Ideas and Media will look beyond the important issues, especially global issues, and we see that "All this has to do with the environment, security, trade, human rights and so on."
"What we see as a challenge in terms of public policy thinking, we see the brain banks, the government, civil society and the media working separately, does not seem to have a platform for working together," said Dr. Kin Phea. At the same time, these characters are important players in society.
"The first Phnom Penh Forum is a new era of concept banking," said Dr. Tan Srida Tuk Ong Tikat, President of the Center for New Asia in Environment and former Minister of Federal Communications and former Vice President of the Malaysian Parliament. "And the media in our ASEAN region is something I have looked at over the last two years."
"Now we need to work together to address the challenges for the first Phnom Penh Forum, a time to bring some key points together to find a common solution," he said.
600 Families in Russey Keo Receive Donations from Islamic Development Bank
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of September 7, 2022, Dr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in charge of Special Mission and President of the Cambodian Muslim Development Foundation, presided over a reception and distribution of gifts to vulnerable people. In Russey Keo district, 600 families received the donation from the Islamic Development Bank (IsDB) in collaboration with the Muslim Development Foundation of Cambodia (CMDF).
The ceremony was held at Vihear Thom, Kilometer 9, Sangkat Chrang Chamres 1, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh, and was attended by Mr. Ek Khun Doeun, Governor of Russey Keo District, Mr. Onur Sezer, Representative of the Turkish Embassy in Cambodia, Member of the National Assembly, Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State Local and youth associations of the Cambodian Muslim Youth League as well.
On this occasion, Dr. thanked the Islamic Development Bank (IsDB) for always paying attention to the development of human resources in Cambodia, as well as providing various assistance and joint activities for the Islamic community in Cambodia in the past. In particular, I would like to express my deep gratitude to the Cambodian Prime Minister for his peace and generosity in accepting donations from other countries to contribute to the development of the country.
Senior Minister Osman Hassan said that today's donation is to join the Royal Government in helping to alleviate the lives of the people, and today's gift is also given to the people regardless of race or religion.
Please be informed that the gift distributed to 600 families, each family received 20 kg of rice, 2 liters of cooking oil, 2 kg of sugar, 10 packets of bear noodles, 4 cans of fish, 1 kg of salt, soap. 4 pieces of body and 1 bottle of dish soap.
The meeting was attended by the Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, Director General of Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport and the Deputy Director General of the Department as well as the Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of the relevant capital / province.
At the same time, the Senior Minister confirmed that for the construction of some important telephone tower towers along the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport has agreed with CRBC to provide the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications with legal installation. Its way with stakeholders.
In addition, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol expressed his appreciation and gratitude to the China Road and Bridge Corporation (CRBC) for carrying out the construction work faster than planned in the contract.
Please be informed that the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway with a total length of 187.05 km was opened for construction on March 22, 2019. This road has achieved 96.60% as of August 26, 2022. This road connects Village 1, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh to Village 1, Sangkat 3, Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province.
