(Canberra): Russia's war in Ukraine and the use of nuclear weapons to threaten the West by President Vladimir Putin has sparked a heated debate over "nuclear weapons". In 2021, when a UN Convention on the Prohibition of Nuclear Weapons entered into force, none of the nine nuclear powers were among the 86 signatories to the treaty.
The world has already avoided a nuclear war in the 1963 Cuban Missile Crisis. But the current war in Ukraine has been worrying more than ever, with most experts believing that Putin could use nuclear weapons in Ukraine if Russia faces defeat, as the West, led by the United States, has shown. Determined to help Ukraine win the war today.
No one can know for sure when a nuclear war will break out. But what is best known now is that the world is on the brink of nuclear war.
